(function(){if(!window.__hermes_register_book)return;window.__hermes_register_book("samaveda",[{"sp": "HDR", "t": "CHAPTER I"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "1.1", "t": "Come, Agni, praised with song, to feast and sacrificial offering: sit<br>As Hotar on the holy grass!"}, {"st": "1.2", "t": "O Agni, thou hast been ordained Hotar of every sacrifice,<br>By Gods, among the race of men."}, {"st": "1.3", "t": "Agni we choose as envoy, skilled performer of this holy rite,<br>Hotar, possessor of all wealth."}, {"st": "1.4", "t": "Served with oblation, kindled, bright, through love of song may Agni, bent<br>On riches, smite the Vritras dead!"}, {"st": "1.5", "t": "I laud your most beloved guest like a dear friend, O Agni, him<br>Who, like a chariot, wins us wealth."}, {"st": "1.6", "t": "Do thou, O Agni, with great might guard us from all malignity,<br>Yea, from the hate of mortal man!"}, {"st": "1.7", "t": "O Agni, come; far other songs of praise will I sing forth to thee.<br>Wax mighty with these Soma-drops!"}, {"st": "1.8", "t": "May Vatsa draw thy mind away even from thy loftiest dwelling place!<br>Agni, I yearn for thee with song."}, {"st": "1.9", "t": "Agni, Atharvan brought thee forth by rubbing from the sky, the head<br>Of all who offer sacrifice."}, {"st": "1.10", "t": "O Agni, bring us radiant light to be our mighty succour, for<br>Thou art our visible deity!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Agni"}, {"st": "2.1", "t": "O Agni, God, the people sing reverent praise to thee for strength:<br>With terrors trouble thou the foe"}, {"st": "2.2", "t": "I seek with song your messenger, oblation-bearer, lord of wealth,<br>Immortal, best at sacrifice."}, {"st": "2.3", "t": "Still turning to their aim in thee the sacrificer’s sister hymns<br>Have come to thee before the wind."}, {"st": "2.4", "t": "To thee, illuminer of night, O Agni, day by day with prayer,<br>Bringing thee reverence, we come."}, {"st": "2.5", "t": "Help, thou who knowest lauds, this work, a lovely hymn in Rudra’s praise,<br>Adorable in every house!"}, {"st": "2.6", "t": "To this fair sacrifice to drink the milky draught art thou called forth:<br>O Agni, with the Maruts come!"}, {"st": "2.7", "t": "With homage will I reverence thee, Agni, like a long-tailed steed,<br>Imperial lord of holy rites."}, {"st": "2.8", "t": "As Aurva and as Bhrigu called, as Apnavana called, I call<br>The radiant Agni robed with sea."}, {"st": "2.9", "t": "When he enkindles Agni, man should with his heart attend the song:<br>I kindle Agni till he glows."}, {"st": "2.10", "t": "Then, verily, they see the light refulgent of primeval seed,<br>Kindled on yonder side of heaven."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Agni"}, {"st": "3.1", "t": "Hither, for powerful kinship, I call Agni, him who prospers you,<br>Most frequent at our solemn rites."}, {"st": "3.2", "t": "May Agni with his pointed blaze cast down each fierce devouring fiend:<br>May Agni win us wealth by war!"}, {"st": "3.3", "t": "Agni, be gracious; thou art great: thou hast approached the pious man,<br>Hast come to sit on sacred grass."}, {"st": "3.4", "t": "Agni, preserve us, from distress consume our enemies, O God,<br>Eternal, with thy hottest flames"}, {"st": "3.5", "t": "Harness, O Agni, O thou God, thy steeds which are most excellent!<br>The fleet ones bring thee rapidly."}, {"st": "3.6", "t": "Lord of the tribes, whom all must seek, we worshipped Agni set thee down,<br>Refulgent, rich in valiant men."}, {"st": "3.7", "t": "Agni is head and height of heaven, the master of the earth is he<br>He quickeneth the waters’ seed."}, {"st": "3.8", "t": "O Agni, graciously announce this our good fortune of the Gods,<br>And this our newest hymn of praise!<br>9, By song, O Agni, Angiras! Gopavana hath brought thee forth<br>Hear thou my call, refulgent one!"}, {"st": "3.10", "t": "Agni, the Sage, the Lord of Strength, hath moved around the sacred gifts,<br>Giving the offerer precious things."}, {"st": "3.11", "t": "His heralds bear him up aloft, the God who knoweth all that lives,<br>The Sun, that all may look on him.<br>12, Praise Agni in the sacrifice, the Sage whose holy laws are true<br>The God who driveth grief away."}, {"st": "3.13", "t": "Kind be the Goddesses to lend us help, and kind that we may drink:<br>May their streams bring us health and wealth"}, {"st": "3.14", "t": "Lord of the brave, whose songs dost thou in thine abundance now inspire,<br>Thou whose hymns help to win the kine?"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Agni"}, {"st": "4.1", "t": "Sing to your Agni with each song, at every sacrifice for strength.<br>Come, let us praise the wise and, everlasting God even as a well-beloved friend,"}, {"st": "4.2", "t": "Agni, protect thou us by one, protect us by the second song,<br>Protect us by three hymns, O Lord of power and might, bright God, by four hymns guard us well!"}, {"st": "4.3", "t": "O Agni, with thy lofty beams, with thy pure brilliancy, O God,<br>Kindled, most youthful one! by Bharadvaja’s hand, shine on us richly, holy Lord!"}, {"st": "4.4", "t": "O Agni who art worshipped well, dear let our princes be to thee,<br>Our wealthy patrons who are governors of men, who part, as gifts, the stall of kine!"}, {"st": "4.5", "t": "Agni, praise-singer! Lord of men, God! burning up the Rakshasas,<br>Mighty art thou, the ever-present, household-lord! home-friend and guardian from the sky."}, {"st": "4.6", "t": "Immortal Jatavedas, thou bright-hued refulgent gift of Dawn,<br>Agni, this day to him who pays oblations bring the Gods who waken with the morn!"}, {"st": "4.7", "t": "Wonderful, with thy favouring help, send us thy bounties, gracious Lord.<br>Thou art the charioteer, Agni, of earthly wealth: find rest and safety for our seed!"}, {"st": "4.8", "t": "Famed art thou, Agni, far and wide, preserver, righteous, and a Sage.<br>The holy singers, O enkindled radiant one, ordainers, call on thee to come."}, {"st": "4.9", "t": "O holy Agni, give us wealth famed among men and strengthening life!<br>Bestow on us, O helper, that which many crave, more glorious still through righteousness!"}, {"st": "4.10", "t": "To him, who dealeth out all wealth, the sweet-toned Hotar-priest of men,<br>To him like the first vessels filled with savoury juice, to Agni let the lauds go forth."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Agni"}, {"st": "5.1", "t": "With this mine homage I invoke Agni for you, the Son of Strength,<br>Dear, wisest envoy, skilled in noble sacrifice, immortal messenger of all."}, {"st": "5.2", "t": "Thou liest in the logs that are thy mothers: mortals kindle thee.<br>Alert thou bearest off the sacrificeer’s gift, and then thou shinest to the Gods."}, {"st": "5.3", "t": "He hath appeared, best prosperer, in whom men lay their holy acts:<br>So may our songs of praise come nigh to Agni who was born to give the Arya strength!"}, {"st": "5.4", "t": "Chief Priest is Agni at the laud, as stones and grass at sacrifice.<br>Gods! Maruts! Brahmanaspati! I crave with song the help that is most excellent."}, {"st": "5.5", "t": "Pray Agni of the piercing flame, with sacred songs, to be our help;<br>For wealth, famed Agni, Purumilha and ye men! He is Suditi’s sure defence."}, {"st": "5.6", "t": "Hear, Agni who hast ears to hear, with all thy train of escort Gods!<br>With those who come at dawn let Mitra, Aryaman sit on the grass at sacrifice."}, {"st": "5.7", "t": "Agni of Divodasa, God, comes forth like Indra in his might.<br>Rapidly hath he moved along his mother earth: he stands in high heaven’s dwelling-place."}, {"st": "5.8", "t": "Whether thou come from earth or from the lofty lucid realm of heaven,<br>Wax stronger in thy body through my song of praise: fill full all creatures, O most wise!"}, {"st": "5.9", "t": "If, loving well the forests, thou wentest to thy maternal floods,<br>Not to be scorned, Agni, is that return of thine when, from afar, thou now art here."}, {"st": "5.10", "t": "O Agni, Manu stablished thee a light for all the race of men:<br>With Kanva hast thou blazed, Law-born and waxen strong, thou whom the people reverence."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "6.1", "t": "The God who giveth wealth accept your full libation poured to, him!<br>Pour ye it out, then fill the vessel full again, for so the God regardeth you."}, {"st": "6.2", "t": "Let Brahmanaspati come forth, let Sunrita the Goddess come,<br>And Gods bring to our rite which yields a fivefold gift the hero, lover of mankind!"}, {"st": "6.3", "t": "Stand up erect to lend us aid, stand up like Savitar the God,<br>Erect as strength-bestower when we call on thee with priests who balm our offerings!"}, {"st": "6.4", "t": "The man who bringeth gifts to thee, bright God who fain wouldst lead to wealth,<br>Winneth himself a brave son, Agni! skilled in lauds, one prospering in a thousand ways."}, {"st": "6.5", "t": "With hymns and holy eulogies we supplicate your Agni, Lord<br>Of many families who duly serve the Gods, yea, him whom others too inflame."}, {"st": "6.6", "t": "This Agni is the Lord of great prosperity and hero, strength,<br>Of wealth with noble offspring and with store of kine, the Lord of battles with the foe."}, {"st": "6.7", "t": "Thou, Agni, art the homestead’s Lord, our Hotar-priest at sacrifice.<br>Lord of all boons, thou art the Potar, passing wise. Pay worship, and enjoy the good!"}, {"st": "6.8", "t": "We as thy friends have chosen thee, mortals a God, to be our help.<br>The Waters’ Child, the blessed, the most mighty one, swift conqueror, and without a peer."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Agni"}, {"st": "7.1", "t": "Present oblations, make him splendid: set ye as Hotar in his place the Home’s Lord, worshipped<br>With gifts and homage where they pour libations! Honour him meet for reverence in our houses."}, {"st": "7.2", "t": "Verily wondrous is the tender youngling’s growth who never draweth nigh to drink his mother’s milk.<br>As soon as she who hath no udder bore him, he, faring on his. great errand, suddenly grew strong."}, {"st": "7.3", "t": "Here is one light for thee, another yonder: enter the third and, be therewith united.<br>Beautiful be thy union with the body, beloved in the Gods’ sublimest birthplace!"}, {"st": "7.4", "t": "For Jatavedas, worthy of our praise, will we frame with our mind this eulogy as ‘twere a car;<br>For good, in his assembly, is this care of ours. Let us not, in thy friendship, Agni, suffer harm!"}, {"st": "7.5", "t": "Agni Vaisvanara, born in course of Order, the messenger of earth, the head of heaven,<br>The Sage, the sovran, guest of men, our vessel fit for their mouth, the Gods have generated."}, {"st": "7.6", "t": "Even as the waters from the mountain ridges, so sprang the; Gods, through lauds, from thee, O Agni.<br>To thee speed hymns and eulogies, as horses haste, bearing him who loves the song, to battle."}, {"st": "7.7", "t": "Win to protect you, Rudra, lord of worship, priest of both worlds, effectual sacrificer,<br>Agni, invested with his golden colours, before the thunder strike and lay you senseless!"}, {"st": "7.8", "t": "The King whose face is decked with oil is kindled with homage offered by his faithful servant.<br>The men, the priests adore him with oblations. Agni hath shone forth at the flush of morning."}, {"st": "7.9", "t": "Agni advanceth with his lofty banner: through earth and heaven the Bull hath loudly bellowed<br>He hath come nigh from the sky’s farthest limit: the Steer hath waxen in the waters’ bosom."}, {"st": "7.10", "t": "From the two fire-sticks have the men engendered with thoughts, urged by the hand, the glorious Agni,<br>Far-seen, with pointed flame, Lord of the Homestead."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Agni"}, {"st": "8.1", "t": "Agni is wakened by the people’s fuel to meet the Dawn who cometh like a milch-cow.<br>Like young trees shooting up on high their branches, his flames. are mounting to the vault of heaven."}, {"st": "8.2", "t": "Set forth the gleaming one, the song-inspirer, not foolish with. the foolish, fort-destroyer,<br>Who leadeth with his hymns to thought of conquest, gold-bearded, richly splendid with his armour"}, {"st": "8.3", "t": "Thou art like heaven: one form is bright, one holy, like Day and Night dissimilar in colour.<br>All magic powers thou aidest, self-dependent! Auspicious bethy bounty here, O Pushan!"}, {"st": "8.4", "t": "As holy food, Agni, to thine invoker give wealth in cattle, lasting, rich in marvels!<br>To us be born a son and spreading offspring. Agni, be this thy gracious will to us-ward!"}, {"st": "8.5", "t": "Stablished to fill the juice with vital vigour, giver of wealth, guard of his servant’s body,<br>The great Priest, born, who knows the clouds, abider with men, is seated in the waters’ eddy."}, {"st": "8.6", "t": "Let the song, honouring the best, with longing honour the Asura’s most famous sovran,<br>The deeds of him the mighty, deeds like Indra’s, the manly one in whom the folk must triumph!"}, {"st": "8.7", "t": "In the two kindling-blocks lies Jatavedas like the well-cherished germ in pregnant women, — <br>Agni who day by day must be entreated by men who watch provided with oblations."}, {"st": "8.8", "t": "Agni, from days of old thou slayest demons: never shall Rakshasas in fight o’ercome thee.<br>Burn up the foolish ones, raw flesh devourers: let none of them escape thine heavenly arrow!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Agni"}, {"st": "9.1", "t": "Bring us most mighty splendour thou, Agni, resistless on thy way:<br>Prepare for us the path that leads to glorious opulence and strength!"}, {"st": "9.2", "t": "May the brave man, if full of zeal he serve and kindle Agni’s flame,<br>Duly presenting sacred gifts, enjoy the Gods’ protecting help."}, {"st": "9.3", "t": "Thy bright smoke lifts itself aloft, and far-extended shines in heaven,<br>For, Purifier! like the Sun thou beamest with thy radiant glow."}, {"st": "9.4", "t": "Thou, Agni, even as Mitra, hast a princely glory of thine own.<br>Bright, active God, thou makest fame increase like means of nourishment."}, {"st": "9.5", "t": "At dawn let Agni, much-beloved, guest of the house, be glorified,<br>In whom, the everlasting one, all mortals make their offerings blaze."}, {"st": "9.6", "t": "Most moving song be Agni’s: shine on high, O rich in radiant light!<br>Like the chief consort of a King riches and strength proceed from thee."}, {"st": "9.7", "t": "Exerting all our strength with thoughts of power we glorify in speech<br>Agni your dear familiar friend, the darling guest in every house."}, {"st": "9.8", "t": "His beam hath lofty power of life: sing praise to Agni, to the God<br>Whom men have set in foremost place, like Mitra for their eulogy!"}, {"st": "9.9", "t": "To noblest Agni, friend of man, chief Vritra-slayer, have we come-<br>Who with Srutarvan, Riksha’s son, in lofty presence is inflamed."}, {"st": "9.10", "t": "Born as the loftiest Law commands, comrade of those who grew with him.<br>Agni, the sire of Kasyapa by faith, the mother, Manu, Sage."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Agni"}, {"st": "10.1", "t": "We in King Soma place our trust, in Agni, and in Varuna,<br>The Aditya, Vishnu, Surya, and the Brahman-priest Brihaspati."}, {"st": "10.2", "t": "Hence have these men gone up on high and mounted to the heights of heaven:<br>On! conquer on the path by which Angirasas travelled to the skies!"}, {"st": "10.3", "t": "That thou mayst send us ample wealth, O Agni, we will kindler thee:<br>So, for the great oblation, Steer, pray Heaven and Earth to come to us!"}, {"st": "10.4", "t": "He runs when one calls after him, This is the prayer of him who prays.<br>He holds all knowledge in his grasp even as the felly rounds the wheel."}, {"st": "10.5", "t": "Shoot forth, O Agni, with thy flame: demolish them on every side!<br>Break down the Yatudhana’s strength, the vigour of the Rakshasa!"}, {"st": "10.6", "t": "Worship the Vasus, Agni! here, the Rudras and Adityas, all<br>Who know fair sacrifices, sprung from Mann, scattering blessings down!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "11.1", "t": "Agni, thy faithful servant I call upon thee with many a gift,<br>As in the keeping of the great inciting God."}, {"st": "11.2", "t": "To Agni, to the Hotar-priest offer your best, your lofty speech,<br>To him ordainer-like who bears the light of songs."}, {"st": "11.3", "t": "O Agni, thou who art the lord of wealth in kine, thou Son of Strength,<br>Bestow on us, O Jatavedas, high renown"}, {"st": "11.4", "t": "Most skilled in sacrifice, bring the Gods, O Agni, to the pious, man:<br>A joyful Priest, thy splendour drives our foes afar"}, {"st": "11.5", "t": "Taught by seven mothers at his birth was he, for glory of the wise.<br>He, firm and sure, hath set his mind on glorious wealth"}, {"st": "11.6", "t": "And in the day our prayer is this: May Aditi come nigh to help,<br>With loving-kindness bring us weal and chase our foes"}, {"st": "11.7", "t": "Worship thou Jatavedas, pray to him who willingly accepts,<br>Whose smoke wanders at will, and none may grasp his flame"}, {"st": "11.8", "t": "No mortal man can e’er prevail by arts of magic over him<br>Who hath served Agni well, the oblation-giving God."}, {"st": "11.9", "t": "Agni, drive thou the wicked foe, the evil-hearted thief away,<br>Far, far, Lord of the brave! and give us easy paths!"}, {"st": "11.10", "t": "O hero Agni, Lord of men, on hearing this new laud of mine<br>Burn down the Rakshasas, enchanters, with thy flame!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Agni"}, {"st": "12.1", "t": "Sing forth to him the holy, most munificent, sublime with his refulgent glow,<br>To Agni, ye Upastutas"}, {"st": "12.2", "t": "Agni, he conquers by thine aid that brings him store of valiant sons and does great deeds,<br>Whose bond of friendship is thy choice"}, {"st": "12.3", "t": "Sing praise to him the Lord of light! The Gods have made the God to be their messenger,<br>To bear oblation to the Gods."}, {"st": "12.4", "t": "Anger not him who is our guest! He is the bright God Agni, praised by many a man,<br>God Hotar, skilled in sacrifice."}, {"st": "12.5", "t": "May Agni, worshipped, bring us bliss: may the gift, blessed one! and sacrifice bring bliss.<br>Yea, may our eulogies bring bliss."}, {"st": "12.6", "t": "Thee have we chosen skilfullest in sacrifice, immortal Priest among the Gods,<br>Wise finisher of this holy rite."}, {"st": "12.7", "t": "Bring us that splendour, Agni, which may overcome each greedy fiend in our abode,<br>And the malicious wrath of men!"}, {"st": "12.8", "t": "Soon as the eager Lord of men is friendly unto Manu’s race<br>Agni averteth from us all the Rakshasas!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "13.1", "t": "Sing this, beside the flowing juice, to him your hero, much-invoked,<br>To please him as a mighty Bull"}, {"st": "13.2", "t": "O Satakratu Indra, now rejoice with that carouse of thine<br>Which is most glorious of all!"}, {"st": "13.3", "t": "Ye cows, protect the fount: the two mighty ones bless the sacrifice.<br>The handles twain are wrought of gold."}, {"st": "13.4", "t": "Sing praises that the horse may come; sing, Srutakaksha, that the cow<br>May come, that Indra’s might may come"}, {"st": "13.5", "t": "We make this Indra very strong to strike, the mighty Vritra dead:<br>A vigorous hero shall he be."}, {"st": "13.6", "t": "Based upon strength and victory and power, O Indra, is thy birth:<br>Thou, mighty one! art strong indeed,"}, {"st": "13.7", "t": "The sacrifice made Indra great when he unrolled the earth, and made<br>Himself a diadem in heaven."}, {"st": "13.8", "t": "If I, O Indra, were, like thee, the single ruler over wealth<br>My worshipper should be rich in kine."}, {"st": "13.9", "t": "Pressers, blend Soma juice for him, each draught most excellent, for him<br>The brave, the hero, for his joy."}, {"st": "13.10", "t": "Here is the Soma juice expressed. O Vasu, drink till thou art full:<br>Undaunted God, we give it thee"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "14.1", "t": "Surya, thou mountest up to meet the hero famous for his wealth,<br>Who hurls the bolt and works for man."}, {"st": "14.2", "t": "Whatever, Vritra-slayer! thou, Surya hast risen upon to-day,<br>That, Indra, all is in thy power."}, {"st": "14.3", "t": "That Indra is our youthful friend, who with his trusty guidance led<br>Turvasa, Yadu from afar."}, {"st": "14.4", "t": "O Indra, let not ill designs surround us in the sunbeams’ light<br>This may we gain with thee for friend!"}, {"st": "14.5", "t": "Indra, bring wealth that gives delight, the victor’s ever-conquering wealth,<br>Most excellent, to be our aid"}, {"st": "14.6", "t": "In mighty battle we invoke Indra, Indra is lesser fight,<br>The friend who bends his bolt at fiends."}, {"st": "14.7", "t": "In battle of a thousand arms Indra drank Kadru’s Soma juice<br>There he displayed his manly might."}, {"st": "14.8", "t": "Faithful to thee, we sing aloud, heroic Indra, songs to thee<br>Mark, O good Lord, this act of ours!"}, {"st": "14.9", "t": "Hitherward! they who light the flame and straightway trim the sacred grass,<br>Whose friend is Indra ever young."}, {"st": "14.10", "t": "Drive all our enemies away, smite down the foes who press around,<br>And bring the wealth for which we long!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "15.1", "t": "I Hear, as though ‘twere close at hand, the cracking of the whips they hold:<br>They gather splendour on their way."}, {"st": "15.2", "t": "Indra, these friends of ours, supplied with Soma, wait and look to thee<br>As men with fodder to the herd."}, {"st": "15.3", "t": "Before his hot displeasure all the peoples, all the men bow down,<br>As rivers bow them to the sea."}, {"st": "15.4", "t": "We choose unto ourselves that high protection of the mighty Gods,<br>That it may help and succour us."}, {"st": "15.5", "t": "O Brahmanaspati, make thou Kakshivan Ausija a loud<br>Chanter of flowing Soma juice!"}, {"st": "15.6", "t": "Much honoured with libations may the Vritra-slayer watch for us:<br>May Sakra listen to our prayer"}, {"st": "15.7", "t": "Send us this day, God Savitar, prosperity with progeny<br>Drive thou the evil dream away!"}, {"st": "15.8", "t": "Where is that ever-youthful Steer, strong-necked and never yet bent down?<br>What Brahman ministers to him?"}, {"st": "15.9", "t": "There where the mountains downward slope, there at the meeting of the streams<br>The Sage was manifest by song."}, {"st": "15.10", "t": "Praise Indra whom our songs must laud, sole sovran of mankind, the chief<br>Most liberal who controlleth men"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "16.1", "t": "Indra whose jaws are strong hath drunk of worshipping Sudaksha’s draught,<br>The Soma juice with barley brew."}, {"st": "16.2", "t": "O Lord of ample wealth, these songs of praise have called aloud to thee,<br>Like milch-kine lowing to their calves!"}, {"st": "16.3", "t": "Then straight they recognized the mystic name of the creative Steer,<br>There in the mansion of the Moon."}, {"st": "16.4", "t": "When Indra, strongest hero, brought the streams, the mighty waters down,<br>Pushan was standing by his side."}, {"st": "16.5", "t": "The Cow, the streaming mother of the liberal Maruts, pours her milk,<br>Harnessed to draw their chariots on."}, {"st": "16.6", "t": "Come, Lord of rapturous joys, to our libation with thy bay steeds, come<br>With bay steeds to the flowing juice"}, {"st": "16.7", "t": "Presented strengthening gifts have sent Indra away at sacrifice,<br>With night, unto the cleansing bath."}, {"st": "16.8", "t": "I from my Father have received deep knowledge of eternal Law:<br>I was born like unto the Sun."}, {"st": "16.9", "t": "With Indra splendid feasts be ours, rich in all strengthening things, wherewith,<br>Wealthy in food, we may rejoice"}, {"st": "16.10", "t": "Soma and Pushan, kind to him who travels to the Gods, provide<br>Dwellings all happy and secure."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "17.1", "t": "Invite ye Indra with a song to drink your draught of Soma steeds, juice,<br>All-conquering Satakratu, most munificent of all who live"}, {"st": "17.2", "t": "Sing ye a song, to make him glad, to Indra, Lord of tawny<br>The Soma-drinker, O my friends!"}, {"st": "17.3", "t": "This, even this, O Indra, we implore: as thy devoted friends<br>The Kanvas praise thee with their hymns!"}, {"st": "17.4", "t": "For Indra, lover of carouse, loud be our songs about the juice<br>Let poets sing the song of praise."}, {"st": "17.5", "t": "Here, Indra, is thy Soma draught, made pure upon the sacred grass:<br>Run hither, come and drink thereof"}, {"st": "17.6", "t": "As a good cow to him who milks, we call the doer of good deeds<br>To our assistance day by day."}, {"st": "17.7", "t": "Hero, the Soma being shed, I pour the juice for thee to drink<br>Sate thee and finish thy carouse!"}, {"st": "17.8", "t": "The Soma, Indra, which is shed in saucers and in cups for thee,<br>Drink thou, for thou art lord thereof!"}, {"st": "17.9", "t": "In every need, in every fray we call, as friends, to succour us,<br>Indra, the mightiest of all."}, {"st": "17.10", "t": "O come ye hither, sit ye down: to Indra sing ye forth your song,<br>Companions, bringing hymns of praise"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "18.1", "t": "So, Lord of affluent gifts, this juice hath been expressed for thee with strength:<br>Drink of it, thou who lovest song!"}, {"st": "18.2", "t": "Great is our Indra from of old; greatness be his, the Thunderer<br>Wide as the heaven extends his might."}, {"st": "18.3", "t": "Indra, as one with mighty arm, gather for us with thy right hand<br>Manifold and nutritious spoil!"}, {"st": "18.4", "t": "Praise, even as he is known, with song Indra the guardian of the kine,<br>The Son of Truth, Lord of the brave."}, {"st": "18.5", "t": "With what help will he come to us, wonderful, ever-waxing friend?<br>With what most mighty company?"}, {"st": "18.6", "t": "Thou speedest down to succour us this ever-conquering God of yours<br>Him who is drawn to all our songs."}, {"st": "18.7", "t": "To the assembly’s wondrous Lord, the lovely friend of Indra, I<br>Had prayed for wisdom and success.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [96, 95]]}, {"st": "18.8", "t": "May all thy paths beneath the sky whereby thou speddest Vyasva on,<br>Yea, let all spaces hear our voice"}, {"st": "18.9", "t": "Bring to us all things excellent, O Satakratu, food and strength,<br>For, Indra, thou art kind to us!"}, {"st": "18.10", "t": "Here is the Soma ready pressed: of this the Maruts, yea, of this,<br>Self-luminous the Asvins drink."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "19.1", "t": "Tossing about, the active ones came nigh to Indra at his birth,<br>Winning themselves heroic might."}, {"st": "19.2", "t": "Never, O Gods, do we offend, nor are we ever obstinate<br>We walk as holy texts command."}, {"st": "19.3", "t": "Evening is come: sing loudly thou Atharvan’s nobly singing son:<br>Give praise to Savitar the God!"}, {"st": "19.4", "t": "Now Morning with her earliest light shines forth, dear daughter of the Sky:<br>High, Asvins, I extol your praise."}, {"st": "19.5", "t": "Armed with the bones of dead Dadhyach, Indra, with unresisted might<br>The nine-and-ninety Vritras slew."}, {"st": "19.6", "t": "Come, Indra, and delight thee with the juice at all our Soma feasts,<br>Protector, mighty in thy strength"}, {"st": "19.7", "t": "O thou who slayest Vritras, come, O Indra, hither to our side,<br>Mighty one, with thy mighty aids!"}, {"st": "19.8", "t": "That might of his shone brightly forth when Indra brought together, like<br>A skin, the worlds of heaven and earth,"}, {"st": "19.9", "t": "This is thine own Thou drawest near, as turns a pigeon to his mate:<br>Thou carest, too, for this our prayer."}, {"st": "19.10", "t": "May Vata breathe his balm on us, healthful, delightful to our heart:<br>May he prolong our days of life"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "20.1", "t": "Ne’er is he injured whom the Gods Varuna, Mitra, Aryam.<br>The excellently wise, protect."}, {"st": "20.2", "t": "According to our wish for kine, for steeds and chariots, as of old,<br>Be gracious to our wealthy chiefs"}, {"st": "20.3", "t": "Indra, these spotted cows yield thee their butter and the milky draught,<br>Aiders, thereby, of sacrifice."}, {"st": "20.4", "t": "That thou much-lauded! many-named! mayst, with this thought, that longs for milk,<br>Come to each Soma sacrifice."}, {"st": "20.5", "t": "May bright Sarasvati, endowed with plenteous wealth and spoil, enriched<br>With prayer, desire the sacrifice."}, {"st": "20.6", "t": "Why ‘mid the Nahusha tribes shall sate this Indra with his Soma juice?<br>He shall bring precious things to us."}, {"st": "20.7", "t": "Come, we have pressed the juice for thee; O Indra, drink this Soma here:<br>Sit thou on this my sacred grass"}, {"st": "20.8", "t": "Great, unassailable must be the heavenly favour of the Three,<br>Varuna, Mitra, Aryaman."}, {"st": "20.9", "t": "We, Indra, Lord of ample wealth, our guide, depend on one like thee,<br>Thou driver of the tawny steeds!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Indra"}, {"st": "21.1", "t": "Let Soma juices make thee glad! Display thy bounty, Thunderer:<br>Drive off the enemies of prayer!"}, {"st": "21.2", "t": "Drink our libation, Lord of hymns! with streams of meath thou art bedewed:<br>Yea, Indra, glory is thy gift."}, {"st": "21.3", "t": "Indra hath ever thought of you and tended you with care. The God,<br>Heroic Indra, is not checked."}, {"st": "21.4", "t": "Let the drops pass within thee as the rivers flow into the sea<br>O Indra, naught excelleth thee!"}, {"st": "21.5", "t": "Indra, the singers with high praise, Indra reciters with their lauds,<br>Indra the choirs have glorified."}, {"st": "21.6", "t": "May Indra give, to aid us wealth handy that rules the skilful ones!<br>Yea, may the Strong give potent wealth"}, {"st": "21.7", "t": "Verily Indra, conquering all, drives even mighty fear away,<br>For firm is he and swift to act."}, {"st": "21.8", "t": "These songs with every draught we pour come, lover of the song, to thee<br>As milch-kine hasten to their calves."}, {"st": "21.9", "t": "Indra and Wishan will we call for friendship and prosperity,<br>And for the winning of the spoil."}, {"st": "21.10", "t": "O Indra, Vritra-slayer, naught is better, mightier than thou<br>Verily there is none like thee!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "22.1", "t": "Him have I magnified, our Lord in common, guardian of your folk,<br>Discloser of great wealth in kine."}, {"st": "22.2", "t": "Songs have outpoured themselves to thee, Indra, the strong, the guardian Lord,<br>And with one will have risen to thee!"}, {"st": "22.3", "t": "Good guidance hath the mortal man whom Arya-man, the Marut host,<br>And Mitras, void of guile, protect."}, {"st": "22.4", "t": "Bring us the wealth for which we long, O Indra, that which is concealed<br>In strong firm place precipitous."}, {"st": "22.5", "t": "Him your best Vritra-slayer, him the famous champion of mankind<br>I urge to great munificence."}, {"st": "22.6", "t": "Indra, may we adorn thy fame, fame of one like thee, hero! deck,<br>Sakra! thy fame at highest feast!"}, {"st": "22.7", "t": "Indra, accept at break of day our Soma mixt with roasted corn,<br>With groats, with cake, with eulogies!"}, {"st": "22.8", "t": "With waters’ foam thou torest off, Indra, the head of Namuchi,<br>When thou o’ercamest all the foes."}, {"st": "22.9", "t": "Thine are these Soma juices, thine, Indra, those still to be expressed:<br>Enjoy them, Lord of princely wealth!"}, {"st": "22.10", "t": "For thee, O Indra, Lord of light, Somas are pressed and grass is strewn:<br>Be gracious to thy worshippers!"}, {"st": "22.1", "t": "We seeking strength, with Soma drops fill full your Indra like a well,<br>Most liberal, Lord of boundless might."}, {"st": "22.2", "t": "O Indra, even from that place come unto us with food that gives<br>A hundred, yea, a thousand powers!"}, {"st": "22.3", "t": "The new-born Vritra-slayer asked his mother, as he seized his shaft,<br>Who are the, fierce and famous ones?"}, {"st": "22.4", "t": "Let us call him to aid whose hands stretch far, the highly-lauded, who<br>Fulfils the work to favour us"}, {"st": "22.5", "t": "Mitra who knoweth leadeth us, and Varuna who guideth straight,<br>And Aryaman in accord with Gods."}, {"st": "22.6", "t": "When, even as she were present here, red Dawn hath shone from far away,<br>She spreadeth light on every side."}, {"st": "22.7", "t": "Varuna, Mitra, sapient pair, pour fatness on our pastures, pour<br>Meath on the regions of the air!"}, {"st": "22.8", "t": "And, at our sacrifices, these, sons, singers, have enlarged their bounds,<br>So that the cows must walk knee-deep."}, {"st": "22.9", "t": "Through all this world strode Vishnu: thrice his foot he planted, and the whole<br>Was gathered in his footstep’s dust."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "23.1", "t": "Pass by the wrathful offerer; speed the man who pours libation, drink<br>The juice which he presents to thee!"}, {"st": "23.2", "t": "What is the word addressed to him, God great and excellently wise?<br>For this is what exalteth him.<br>3, His wealth who hath no store of kine hath ne’er found out recited laud,<br>Nor song of praises that is sung."}, {"st": "23.4", "t": "Lord of each thing that giveth strength, Indra delighteth most in lauds,<br>Borne by bay steeds, libations’ friend."}, {"st": "23.5", "t": "With wealth to our libation come, be not thou angry with us, like<br>A great man with a youthful bride."}, {"st": "23.6", "t": "When, Vasu, wilt thou love the laud? Now let the Channel bring the stream.<br>The juice is ready to ferment."}, {"st": "23.7", "t": "After the Seasons. Indra, drink the Soma from the Brahman’s gift:<br>Thy friendship is invincible!<br>S. O Indra, lover of the song, we are the singers of thy praise<br>O Soma-drinker, quicken us!"}, {"st": "23.9", "t": "O Indra, in each fight and fray give to our bodies manly strength:<br>Strong Lord, grant ever-conquering might!"}, {"st": "23.10", "t": "For so thou art the brave man’s friend; a hero, too, art thou, and strong:<br>So may thine heart be won to us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "24.1", "t": "Like kine unmilked we call aloud, hero, to thee, and sing thy praise,<br>Looker on heavenly light, Lord of this moving world, Lord, Indra, of what moveth not!"}, {"st": "24.2", "t": "That we may win us wealth and power we poets, verily, call on thee:<br>In war men call on thee, Indra, the hero’s Lord, in the steed’s race-course call on thee:"}, {"st": "24.3", "t": "To you will I sing Indra’s praise who gives good gifts as well we know;<br>The praise of Maghavan who, rich in treasure, aids his singers with wealth thousandfold."}, {"st": "24.4", "t": "As cows low to their calves in stalls, so with our songs we glorify<br>This Indra, even your wondrous God who checks attack, who takes delight in precious juice."}, {"st": "24.5", "t": "Loud singing at the sacred rite where Soma flows we priests invoke<br>With haste, that he may help, as the bard’s cherisher, Indra who findeth wealth for you"}, {"st": "24.6", "t": "With Plenty for his true ally the active man will gain the spoil.<br>Your Indra, much-invoked, I bend with song, as bends a wright his wheel of solid wood."}, {"st": "24.7", "t": "Drink, Indra, of the savoury juice, and cheer thee with our milky draught!<br>Be, for our weal, our friend and sharer of the feast, and let thy wisdom guard us well!"}, {"st": "24.8", "t": "For thou — come to the worshipper! — wilt find great wealth to make us rich.<br>Fill thyself full, O Maghavan, for gain of kine, full, Indra, for the gain of steeds!"}, {"st": "24.9", "t": "Vasishtha will not overlook the lowliest one among you all<br>Beside our Soma juice effused to-day let all the Maruts drink with eager haste!"}, {"st": "24.10", "t": "Glorify naught besides, O friends; so shall no sorrow trouble you!<br>Praise only mighty Indra when the juice is shed, and say your lauds repeatedly!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Indra"}, {"st": "25.1", "t": "No one by deed attains to him who works and strengthens evermore:<br>No, not by sacrifice, to Indra. praised of all, resistless, daring, bold in might."}, {"st": "25.2", "t": "He without ligature, before making incision in the neck,<br>Closed up the wound again, most wealthy Maghavan, who healeth the dissevered parts."}, {"st": "25.3", "t": "A thousand and a hundred steeds are harnessed to thy golden car:<br>Yoked by devotion, Indra, let the long-maned bays bring thee to drink the Soma juice!"}, {"st": "25.4", "t": "Come hither, Indra, with bay steeds, joyous, with tails like peacock’s plumes!<br>Let no men check thy course as fowlers stay the bird: pass o’er them as o’er desert lands!"}, {"st": "25.5", "t": "Thou as a God, O mightiest, verily blessest mortal man.<br>O Maghavan, there is no comforter but thou: Indra, I speak my words to thee."}, {"st": "25.6", "t": "O Indra, thou art far-renowned, impetuous Lord of power and might.<br>Alone, the never-conquered guardian of mankind, thou smitest<br>down resistless foes."}, {"st": "25.7", "t": "Indra for worship of the Gods, Indra while sacrifice proceeds,<br>Indra, as warriors in the battle-shock, we call, Indra that we may win the spoil."}, {"st": "25.8", "t": "May these my songs of praise exalt thee, Lord, who hast abundant wealth!<br>Men skilled in holy hymns, pure, with the hues of fire, have sung them with their lauds to thee."}, {"st": "25.9", "t": "These songs of ours exceeding sweet, these hymns of praise ascend to thee,<br>Like ever-conquering chariots that display their strength gain wealth and give unfailing help."}, {"st": "25.10", "t": "Even as the wild-bull, when he thirsts, goes to the desert’s watery pool,<br>Come to us quickly both at morning and at eve, and with the Kanvas drink thy fill!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "26.1", "t": "Indra, with all thy saving helps assist us, Lord of power and might!<br>For after thee we follow even as glorious bliss, thee, hero, finderout of wealth."}, {"st": "26.2", "t": "O Indra, Lord of light, what joys thou broughtest from the Asuras,<br>Prosper therewith, O Maghavan, him who lauds that deed, and those whose grass is trimmed for thee!"}, {"st": "26.3", "t": "To Aryaman and Mitra sing a reverent song, O pious one,<br>A pleasant hymn to Varuna who shelters us: sing ye a laud unto the Kings!"}, {"st": "26.4", "t": "Men with their lauds are urging thee, Indra, to drink the Soma first.<br>The Ribhus in accord have lifted up their voice, and Rudras sung thee as the first."}, {"st": "26.5", "t": "Sing to your lofty Indra, sing, Maruts, a holy hymn of praise<br>Let Satakratu, Vritra-slayer, slay the foe with hundred-knotted thunderbolt!"}, {"st": "26.6", "t": "To Indra sing the lofty hymn, Maruts! that slays the Vritras best,<br>Whereby the holy ones created for the God the light divine that ever wakes."}, {"st": "26.7", "t": "O Indra, give us wisdom as a sire gives wisdom to his sons<br>Guide us, O much-invoked, in this our way: may we still live and look upon the light!"}, {"st": "26.8", "t": "O Indra, turn us not away: be present with us at our feast<br>For thou art our protection, yea, thou art our kin: O Indra, turn us not away!"}, {"st": "26.9", "t": "We compass these like waters, we whose grass is trimmed and Soma pressed.<br>Here where the filter pours its stream, thy worshippers round<br>thee, O Vritra-slayer, sit."}, {"st": "26.10", "t": "All strength and valour that is found, Indra, in tribes of Nahushas,<br>And all the splendid fame that the Five Tribes enjoy, bring, yea, all manly powers at once!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "27.1", "t": "Yea, verily thou art a Bull, our guardian, rushing like a bull:<br>Thou, mighty one, art celebrated as a Bull, famed as a Bull both near and far."}, {"st": "27.2", "t": "Whether, O Sakra, thou be far, or, Vritra-slayer, near at hand,<br>Thence by heaven-reaching songs he who bath pressed the juice invites thee with thy long-maned steeds."}, {"st": "27.3", "t": "In the wild raptures of the juice sing to your hero with high laud, to him the wise,<br>To Indra glorious in his name, the mighty one, even as the hymn alloweth it!"}, {"st": "27.4", "t": "O Indra, give us for our weal a triple refuge, triply strong!<br>Bestow a dwelling-place on our rich lords and me, and keep thy dart afar from these!"}, {"st": "27.5", "t": "Turning, as ‘twere, to meet the Sun enjoy from Indra all good things!<br>When he who will be born is born with power we look to treasures as our heritage."}, {"st": "27.6", "t": "The godless mortal gaineth not this food, O thou whose life is long!<br>But one who yokes the bright-hued horses, Etasas; then Indra yokes his tawny steeds."}, {"st": "27.7", "t": "Draw near unto our Indra who must be invoked in every fight!<br>Come, thou most mighty Vritra-slayer, meet for praise, come to, libations and to hymns!"}, {"st": "27.8", "t": "Thine, Indra, is the lowest wealth, thou cherishest the midmost wealth,<br>Thou ever rulest all the highest: in the fray for cattle none resisteth thee."}, {"st": "27.9", "t": "Where art thou? Whither art thou gone? For many a place attracts thy mind.<br>Haste, warrior, fort-destroyer, Lord of battle’s din! haste, holy songs have sounded forth!"}, {"st": "27.10", "t": "Here, verily, yesterday we let the thunder-wielder drink his fill.<br>Bring him the juice poured forth in sacrifice to-day. Now range you by the glorious one!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "28.1", "t": "He who as sovran Lord of men moves with his chariots unrestrained,<br>The Vritra-slayer, vanquisher of fighting hosts, pre-eminent, is praised in song."}, {"st": "28.2", "t": "Indra, give us security from that whereof we are afraid<br>Help us, O Maghavan, let thy favour aid us thus; drive away foes and enemies!"}, {"st": "28.3", "t": "Strong pillar thou, Lord of the home! armour of Soma-offerers!<br>The drop of Soma breaketh all the strongholds down, and Indra is the Rishis’ friend."}, {"st": "28.4", "t": "Verily, Surya, thou art great; truly, Aditya, thou art great!<br>O most admired for greatness of thy majesty, God, by thy greatness thou art great!"}, {"st": "28.5", "t": "Indra! thy friend, when fair of form and rich in chariots, steeds, and kine,<br>Hath ever vital power that gives him strength, and joins the company with radiant men."}, {"st": "28.6", "t": "O Indra, if a hundred heavens and if a hundred earths were thine, — <br>No, not a hundred suns could match thee at thy birth, not both the worlds, O Thunderer!"}, {"st": "28.7", "t": "Though, Indra, thou art called by men eastward and west ward, north and south,<br>Thou chiefly art with Anava and Turvasa, brave champion urged by men to come."}, {"st": "28.8", "t": "Indra whose wealth is in thyself, what mortal will attack this man?<br>The strong will win the spoil on the decisive day through faith in thee, O Maghavan!"}, {"st": "28.9", "t": "First, Indra! Agni! hath this Maid come footless unto those with feet.<br>Stretching her head and speaking loudly with her tongue, she hath gone downward thirty steps."}, {"st": "28.10", "t": "Come, Indra, very near to us with aids of firmly-based resolve<br>Come, most auspicious, with thy most auspicious help; good kinsman, with good kinsmen come!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "29.1", "t": "Call to your aid the eternal one who shoots and none may shoot at him,<br>Inciter, swift, victorious, best of charioteers, unconquered, Tugriya’s strengthener!"}, {"st": "29.2", "t": "Let none, no, not thy worshippers, delay thee far away from us<br>Even from faraway come thou unto our feast, or listen if’ already here!"}, {"st": "29.3", "t": "For Indra Soma-drinker, armed with thunder, press the Soma juice;<br>Make ready your dressed meats: cause him to favour us! The giver blesses him who gives."}, {"st": "29.4", "t": "We call upon that Indra who, most active, ever slays the foe<br>With boundless spirit, Lord of heroes, manliest one, help thou and prosper us in fight!"}, {"st": "29.5", "t": "Ye rich in strength, through your great power vouchsafe us blessings day and night!<br>The offerings which we bring to you shall never fail gifts brought by us shall never fail."}, {"st": "29.6", "t": "Whenever mortal worshipper will sing a bounteous giver’s praise,<br>Let him with song inspired laud Varuna who supports the folk who follow varied rites."}, {"st": "29.7", "t": "Drink milk to Indra in the joy of Soma juice, Medhyatithi!<br>To golden Indra ever close to his bay steeds, the thunder-armed, the golden one!"}, {"st": "29.8", "t": "Both boons,-may Indra, hitherward turned listen to this prayer of ours,<br>And mightiest Maghavar, with thought inclined to us come near to drink the Soma juice!"}, {"st": "29.9", "t": "Not for an ample price dost thou, Stone-caster! give thyself away,<br>Not for a thousand, Thunderer! nor ten thousand, nor a hundred, Lord of countless wealth!"}, {"st": "29.10", "t": "O Indra, thou art more to me than sire or niggard brother is.<br>Thou and my mother, O good Lord, appear alike, to give me wealth abundantly."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "30.1", "t": "These Soma juice mixt with curd have been expressed for Indra here:<br>Come with thy bay steeds, Thunder-wielder, to our home, to drink them till they make thee glad!"}, {"st": "30.2", "t": "Indra, these Somas with their lauds have been prepared for thy delight.<br>Drink of the pleasant juice and listen to our songs; lover of song, reward the hymn!"}, {"st": "30.3", "t": "I call on thee, Sabardugha, this day, inspirer of the psalm.<br>Indra, the richly-yielding milch-cow who provides unfailing food in ample stream."}, {"st": "30.4", "t": "Indra, the strong and lofty hills are powerless to bar thy way<br>None stays that act of thine when thou wouldst fain give wealth to one like me who sings thy praise."}, {"st": "30.5", "t": "Who knows what vital power he wins, drinking beside the flowing juice?<br>This is the fair-cheeked. God who, joying in the draught, breaks down the castles in his strength."}, {"st": "30.6", "t": "What time thou castest from his seat and punishest the riteless man,<br>Strengthen for opulence, O Indra Maghavan, our plant desired by many a one!"}, {"st": "30.7", "t": "Let Tvashtar, Brahmanaspati, Parjanya guard our heavenly word,<br>Aditi with her sons, the brothers, guard for us the invincible, the saving word!"}, {"st": "30.8", "t": "Ne’er art thou fruitless, Indra, ne’er dost thou desert the worshipper:<br>But now, O Maghavan, thy bounty as a God is poured forth ever more and more."}, {"st": "30.9", "t": "Best slayer of the Vritras, yoke thy bay steeds, Indra, far away<br>Come with the high ones hither, Maghavan, to us, mighty, to, drink the Soma juice!"}, {"st": "30.10", "t": "O Thunderer, zealous worshippers gave thee drink this time yesterday:<br>So, Indra, listen here to him who offers lauds: come near unto, our dwelling-place!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2"}, {"st": "31.1", "t": "Advancing, sending forth her rays, the daughter of the Sky is seen.<br>The mighty one lays bare the darkness with her eye, the friendly Lady makes the light."}, {"st": "31.2", "t": "These morning sacrifices call you, Asvins, at the break of day.<br>For help have I invoked you rich in power and might: for, house by house, ye visit all."}, {"st": "31.3", "t": "Where are ye, Gods? What mortal man, O Asvins, glows with zeal for you,<br>Urging you with the crushing stone and with the stalk of Soma thus or otherwise?"}, {"st": "31.4", "t": "This sweetest Soma juice hath been expressed for you at morning rites.<br>Asvins, drink this prepared ere yesterday and give treasures to him who offers it!"}, {"st": "31.5", "t": "Let me not, still beseeching thee with might and sound of Soma drops,<br>Anger at sacrifice a fierce wild creature! Who would not beseech the almighty one!"}, {"st": "31.6", "t": "Adhvaryu, let the Soma flow, for Indra longs to drink thereof.<br>He even now hath yoked his vigorous bay steeds: the Vritraslayer hath come nigh."}, {"st": "31.7", "t": "Bring thou all this unto the good, O Indra, to the old and young!<br>For, Maghavan, thou art rich in treasures from of old, to be invoked in every fight."}, {"st": "31.8", "t": "If I, O Indra, were the lord of riches ample as thine own,<br>I would support the singer, God who scatterest wealth! and not abandon him to woe."}, {"st": "31.9", "t": "Thou in thy battles, Indra, art subduer of all hostile bands.<br>Father art thou, all-conquering, cancelling the curse, thou victor of the vanquisher!"}, {"st": "31.10", "t": "For in thy might thou stretchest out beyond the mansions of the sky.<br>The earthly region, Indra, comprehends thee not. Thou hast waxed mighty over all."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3"}, {"st": "32.1", "t": "Pressed is the juice divine with milk commingled: thereto hath Indra ever been accustomed.<br>We wake thee, Lord of bays, with sacrifices: mark this our laud in the wild joys of Soma!"}, {"st": "32.2", "t": "A home is made for thee to dwell in, Indra: O much-invoked one, with the men go thither!<br>Thou, that thou mayest guard us and increase us, givest us wealth and joyest in the Somas."}, {"st": "32.3", "t": "The well thou clavest, settest free the fountains, and gavest rest to floods that were obstructed.<br>Thou, Indra, laying the great mountain open, slaying the Ddnava, didst loose the torrents."}, {"st": "32.4", "t": "When we have pressed the juice we laud thee, Indra, most valorous! even about to win the booty.<br>Bring us prosperity, and by thy great wisdom, under thine own protection, may we conquer!"}, {"st": "32.5", "t": "Thy right hand have we grasped in ours, O Indra, longing, thou very Lord of wealth, for treasures.<br>Because we know thee, hero, Lord of cattle: vouchsafe us mighty and resplendent riches!"}, {"st": "32.6", "t": "Men call on Indra in the armed encounter that he may make the hymns they sing decisive.<br>Hero in combat and in love of glory, give us a portion of the stall of cattle!"}, {"st": "32.7", "t": "Like birds of beauteous wing the Priyamedhas, Rishis, imploring, have come nigh to Indra.<br>Dispel the darkness and fill full our vision: deliver us as men whom snares entangle!"}, {"st": "32.8", "t": "They gaze on thee with longing in their spirit, as on a strongwinged bird that mounteth sky-ward;<br>On thee with wings of gold, Varuna’s envoy, the Bird that hasteneth to the home of Yama."}, {"st": "32.9", "t": "First in the ancient time was Prayer engendered: Vena disclosed the bright ones from the summit,<br>Laid bare this world’s lowest and highest regions, womb of the existent and the non-existent."}, {"st": "32.10", "t": "They have prepared and fashioned for this hero words never matched, most plentiful, most auspicious,<br>For him the ancient, great, strong, energetic, the very mighty wielder of the thunder."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "33.1", "t": "The black drop sank in Ansumati’s bosom, advancing with ten thousand round about it.<br>Indra with might longed for it as it panted: the hero-hearted King laid down his weapons."}, {"st": "33.2", "t": "Flying in terror from the snort of Vritra all deities who were thy friends forsook thee.<br>So, Indra, with the Maruts be thy friendship: in all these battles thou shalt be the victor."}, {"st": "33.3", "t": "The old hath waked the young Moon from his slumber who runs his circling course with many round him.<br>Behold the God’s high wisdom in its greatness: he who died yesterday to-day is living."}, {"st": "33.4", "t": "Then, at thy birth, thou wast the foeman, Indra, of those the seven who ne’er had met a rival.<br>The hidden pair, heaven and the earth, thou foundest, and to the mighty worlds thou gavest pleasure."}, {"st": "33.5", "t": "A friend we count thee, sharp-edged, thunder-wielder, Steer strong of body, overthrowing many.<br>Thou, helping, causest pious tribes to conquer: Indra, I laud the, heavenly Vritra-slayer."}, {"st": "33.6", "t": "Bring to the wise, the great, who waxeth mighty your offerings, and make ready your devotion!<br>Go forth to many tribes as man’s controller!"}, {"st": "33.7", "t": "Call we on Maghavan, auspicious Indra, best hero in this fight where spoil is gathered,<br>Strong, listening to give us aid in battles, who slays the Vritras, wins and gathers riches!"}, {"st": "33.8", "t": "Prayers have been offered up-through love of glory: Vasishtha, honour Indra in the battle!<br>He who with fame extends through all existence hears words which I, his faithful servant, utter."}, {"st": "33.9", "t": "May the sweet Soma juices make him happy to cast his quoit that lies in depth of waters!<br>Thou from the udder which o’er earth is fastened hast poured the milk into the kine and herbage."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "34.1", "t": "This vigorous one whom deities commission, the conqueror of cars, the strong and mighty,<br>Swift, fleet to battle, with uninjured fellies, even Tarkshya for our weal will we call hither."}, {"st": "34.2", "t": "Indra the rescuer, Indra the helper, hero who listens at each invocation,<br>Sakra I call, Indra invoked of many. May Indra Maghavan accept our presents!"}, {"st": "34.3", "t": "Indra whose right hand wields the bolt we worship, driver of bay steeds seeking sundered courses.<br>Shaking his beard with might he hath arisen, terrible with his weapons, with his bounty."}, {"st": "34.4", "t": "The ever-slaying, bold and furious Indra, the bright bolt’s Lord, the strong, the great, the boundless,<br>Who slayeth Vritra and acquireth booty, giver of blessings, Maghavan the bounteous."}, {"st": "34.5", "t": "The man who lies in wait and fights against us, deeming himself a giant or a hero, — <br>By battle or with strength destroy him, Indra! With thy help, manly-souled! may we be victors!"}, {"st": "34.6", "t": "He whom men call when striving with their foemen, or speeding onward in array of battle,<br>Whom bards incite where heroes win the booty, or in the way to waters, He is Indra."}, {"st": "34.7", "t": "On a high car, O Parvata and Indra, bring pleasant viands, with brave heroes, hither!<br>Enjoy our presents, Gods, at sacrifices: wax strong by hymns, rejoice in our oblation!"}, {"st": "34.8", "t": "In ceaseless flow hath he poured forth his praises, as waters from the ocean’s depth, to Indra,<br>Who to his car on both its sides securely hath fixed the earth and heaven as with an axle."}, {"st": "34.9", "t": "May our friends turn thee hitherward to friendship! Mayst thou approach us even o’er many rivers!<br>May the Disposer, radiant in this mansion with special lustre, bring the father’s offspring!"}, {"st": "34.10", "t": "Who yokes to-day unto the pole of Order the strong and passionate steers of checkless spirit,<br>Health-bringing, bearing in their mouths no fodder? Long shall he live who richly pays their service."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Indra"}, {"st": "35.1", "t": "The singers hymn thee, they who chant the psalm of praise are lauding thee.<br>The Brahmans have exalted thee, O Satakratu, like a pole."}, {"st": "35.2", "t": "All sacred-songs have magnified Indra expansive as the sea,<br>Best of all warriors borne on cars, the Lord of heroes, Lord of strength."}, {"st": "35.3", "t": "This poured libation, Indra, drink, immortal, gladdening, excellent:<br>Streams of the bright have flowed to thee here at the seat of holy Law."}, {"st": "35.4", "t": "Stone-darting Indra, wondrous God, what wealth thou hast not given me here,<br>That bounty, treasure-finder! bring, filling full both thy hands, to us!"}, {"st": "35.5", "t": "O Indra, hear Tiraschi’s call, the call of him who serveth thee!<br>Satisfy him with wealth of kine and valiant offspring! Great art thou."}, {"st": "35.6", "t": "This Soma hath been pressed for thee, O Indra: bold one, mightiest, come!<br>May Indra-vigour fill thee full, as Surya fills mid-air with rays"}, {"st": "35.7", "t": "Come hither, Indra, with thy bays, come thou to Kanva’s eulogy!<br>Ye by command of yonder Dyaus, God bright by day! have gone to heaven."}, {"st": "35.8", "t": "Song-lover! like a charioteer come songs to thee when Soma flows.<br>Together, they have called to thee as mother-kine unto their calves."}, {"st": "35.9", "t": "Come now and let us glorify pure Indra with pure Sama hymn!<br>Let milk-blent juice delight him made stronger with pure, pure songs of praise!"}, {"st": "35.10", "t": "That which, most wealthy, makes you rich, in splendours most illustrious,<br>Soma is pressed: thy gladdening drink, Indra libation’s Lord! is this."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Indra. Dadhikravan"}, {"st": "36.1", "t": "Bring forth oblations to the God who knoweth all who fain would drink,<br>The wanderer, lagging not behind the hero, coming nigh with speed!"}, {"st": "36.2", "t": "To us the mighty, lying in all vital power, who resteth in the deep, who standeth in the east.<br>Drive thou the awful word away."}, {"st": "36.3", "t": "Even as a car to give us aid, we draw thee nigh to favour us,<br>Strong in thy deeds, quelling attack, Indra, Lord, mightiest! of the brave."}, {"st": "36.4", "t": "With powers of mighty ones hath he, the friend, the ancient, been equipped,<br>Through whom our father Manu made prayers efficacious with the Gods."}, {"st": "36.5", "t": "What time the swift and shining steeds, yoked to the chariots, draw them on,<br>Drinking the sweet delightful juice, there men perform their glorious acts."}, {"st": "36.6", "t": "Him for your sake I glorify as Lord of Strength who wrongeth none,<br>Indra the hero, mightiest, all-conquering and omniscient."}, {"st": "36.7", "t": "I with my praise have glorified strong Dadhikravan, conquering steed<br>Sweet may he make our mouths: may he prolong the days we have to live!"}, {"st": "36.8", "t": "Render of forts, the young, the wise, of strength unmeasured, was he born,<br>Sustainer of each sacred rite, Indra, the Thunderer, much-extolled."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "37.1", "t": "Offer the triple sacred draught to Indu hero-worshipper!<br>With hymn and plenty he invites you to complete the sacrifice."}, {"st": "37.2", "t": "Those whom they call the attendant pair of Kasyapa who knows the light,<br>Lords of each holy duty when the wise have honoured sacrifice."}, {"st": "37.3", "t": "Sing, sing ye forth your songs of praise, men, Priya-medhas, sing your songs:<br>Yea, let young children sing their lauds: yea, glorify our firm stronghold!"}, {"st": "37.4", "t": "To Indra must a laud be said, a joy to him who freely gives,<br>That Sakra may be joyful in our friendship and the juice we pour."}, {"st": "37.5", "t": "Your Lord of might that ne’er hath bent, that ruleth over all mankind,<br>I call, that he, as he is wont, may aid the chariots and the men."}, {"st": "37.6", "t": "Even he who is thine own, through thought of Heaven, of mortal man who toils,<br>He with the help of lofty Dyaus comes safe through straits of enmity."}, {"st": "37.7", "t": "Wide, Indra Satakratu, spreads the bounty of thine ample grace:<br>So, good and liberal giver, known to all men, send us splendid wealth!"}, {"st": "37.8", "t": "Bright Ushas, when thy times return, all quadrupeds and bipeds stir,<br>And round about flock winged birds from all the boundaries of heaven."}, {"st": "37.9", "t": "Ye Gods who yonder have your home amid the luminous realm of heaven,<br>What count ye right? what endless life? What is the ancient call on you?"}, {"st": "37.10", "t": "We offer laud and psalm wherewith men celebrate their holy rites.<br>They govern at the sacred place and bear the sacrifice to Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "38.1", "t": "Heroes of one accord brought forth and formed for kingship Indra who wins the victory in all encounters,<br>For power, in firmness, in the field, the great destroyer, fierce and exceeding strong, stalwart and full of vigour."}, {"st": "38.2", "t": "I trust in thy first wrathful deed, O Indra, when thou slewest Vritra and didst work to profit man;<br>When the two world-halves fled for refuge unto thee, and earth even trembled at thy strength, O Thunder-armed!"}, {"st": "38.3", "t": "Come all with might together to the Lord of heaven, the only one who is indeed the guestof men.<br>He is the first: to him who fain would come to us all pathways turn; he is in truth the only one."}, {"st": "38.4", "t": "Thine, Indra, praised of many, excellently rich, are we who trusting in thy help draw near to thee.<br>For none but thou, song-lover, shall receive our lauds: as Earth loves all her creatures, welcome this our hymn!"}, {"st": "38.5", "t": "High hymns have sounded forth the praise of Maghavan, supporter of mankind, of Indra meet for lauds;<br>Him who hath waxen mighty, much-invoked with prayers, immortal one whose praise each day is sung aloud."}, {"st": "38.6", "t": "In perfect unison have all your longing hymns that find the light of heaven sounded forth Indra’s praise.<br>As wives embrace their lord, the comely bridegroom, so they compass Maghavan about that he may help."}, {"st": "38.7", "t": "Make glad with songs that Ram whom many men invoke, worthy hymns of praise, Indra the sea of wealth;<br>Whose boons spread like the heavens, the - lover of mankind: sing praise to him the Sage, most liberal for our good!"}, {"st": "38.8", "t": "I glorify that Ram who finds the light of heaven, whose hundred strong and mighty ones go forth with him.<br>With prayers may I turn hither Indra to mine aid;-the car which like a swift steed hasteth to the call!"}, {"st": "38.9", "t": "Filled full of fatness, compassing all things that be, wide, spacious, dropping meath, beautiful in their form,<br>The heaven and the earth by Varuna’s decree, unwasting, rich in germs, stand parted each from each."}, {"st": "38.10", "t": "As like the Morning, thou hast filled, O Indra, both the earth. and heaven,<br>So as the mighty one, great King of all the mighty race of men, the Goddess mother brought thee forth, the blessed mother gave thee life."}, {"st": "38.11", "t": "Sing, with oblation, praise to him who maketh glad, who with. Rijisvan drove the dusky brood away!<br>Let us, desiring help, call him for friendship, him the strong, the Marut-girt, whose right hand wields the bolt!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. When Somas flow thou makest pure, Indra, thy mind that merits laud<br>For gain of strength that ever grows: for great is he.<br>2. Sing forth to him whom many men invoke, to him whom many laud:<br>Invite the potent Indra with your songs of praise<br>3. We sing this strong and wild delight of thine which conquer; in the fray,<br>Which, Caster of the Stone! gives room and shines like gold,<br>4. Whether thou drink the Soma by Vishnu’s or Trita Aptya’s side,<br>Or with the Maruts, Indra! quaff the following drops.<br>5. Come, priest, and of the savoury juice pour forth a yet more gladdening draught:<br>So is the hero praised who ever prospers us.<br>6. Pour out the drops for Indra; let him drink the meath of Soma juice!<br>He through his majesty sends forth his bounteous gifts.<br>7. Come, sing we praise to Indra, friends! the hero who deserves the laud,<br>Him who with none to aid o’ercomes all tribes of men.<br>8. Sing ye a psalm to Indra, sing a great song to the lofty Sage,<br>To him who maketh prayer, inspired who loveth laud!<br>9. He who alone bestoweth wealth on mortal man who offereth gifts<br>Is Indra only, potent Lord whom none resist.<br>10. Companions, let us learn a prayer to Indra, to the Thunderer,<br>To glorify your bold and most heroic friend!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Indra Adityas"}, {"st": "40.1", "t": "Indra, this might of thine I praise most highly for the sacrifice<br>That thou, O Lord of Power, dost slay Vritra with might"}, {"st": "40.2", "t": "For thee this Soma hath been pressed, in whose wild joy thou madest once<br>Sambara Divodasa’s prey: O Indra, drink!"}, {"st": "40.3", "t": "Come unto us, O Indra, dear, still conquering, unconcealable!<br>Wide as a mountain spread on all sides, Lord of heaven!"}, {"st": "40.4", "t": "Joy, mightiest Indra, that perceives, sprung from deep Soma draughts, whereby<br>Thou smitest down the greedy fiend,-that joy we crave!"}, {"st": "40.5", "t": "Adityas, very mighty ones, grant to our children and our seed<br>This lengthened term of life that they may live long days!"}, {"st": "40.6", "t": "Though knowest, Indra, Thunder-armed! how to avoid destructive powers,<br>As one secure from pitfalls each returning day."}, {"st": "40.7", "t": "Drive ye disease and strife away, drive ye away malignity:<br>Adityas, keep us far removed from sore distress!"}, {"st": "40.8", "t": "Drive Soma, Indra, Lord of bays! and let it cheer thee: the stone, like a well-guided courser,"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "41.1", "t": "Still, Indra, from all ancient time rivalless ever and companionless art thou:<br>Thou seekest friendship but in war."}, {"st": "41.2", "t": "Him who of old hath broucht to us this and that blessing, him I magnify for you,<br>Even Indra, O my friends, for help."}, {"st": "41.3", "t": "Fail not when marching onward: come hither, like-spirited, stay not far away<br>Ye who can tame even what is firm!"}, {"st": "41.4", "t": "Come hither to the dropping juice, O Lord of cornland. Lord of horses, Lord of kine:<br>Drink thou the Soma, Soma’s Lord!"}, {"st": "41.5", "t": "Hero, may we, with thee for friend, withstand the man who pants against us in his wrath,<br>In fight with people rich in kine!"}, {"st": "41.6", "t": "Yea, kin by common ancestry, the Maruts, even the oxen, close united friends!<br>Are licking one another’s back."}, {"st": "41.7", "t": "O Indra, bring great strength to us, bring valour, Satakratu, thou most active, bring<br>A hero conquering in war!"}, {"st": "41.8", "t": "So, Indra, friend of song, do we draw nigh to thee with longing; we have streamed to thee<br>Coming like floods that follow floods"}, {"st": "41.9", "t": "Sitting like birds beside thy meath, mingled with milk, which gladdeneth and exalteth thee,<br>Indra, to thee we sing aloud."}, {"st": "41.10", "t": "We call on thee, O matchless one! We, seeking help, possessing nothing firm ourselves,<br>Call on thee, wondrous, Thunder-armed."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "42.1", "t": "The juice of Soma thus diffused, sweet to the taste the bright cows drink,<br>Who travelling in splendour close to mighty Indra’s side rejoice, good in their own supremacy."}, {"st": "42.2", "t": "Thus hath the Soma, gladdening draught, produced the prayer that giveth joy:<br>Thou, mightiest, Thunder-armed, hast driven by force the Dragon from the earth, lauding thine own supremacy."}, {"st": "42.3", "t": "By men hath Indra been advanced, the Vritra-slayer, to joy and strength.<br>Him only we invoke for help in battles whether great or small: be he our aid in deeds of might!"}, {"st": "42.4", "t": "Unconquered strength is only thine, Indra, Stonecaster, Thunder-armed!<br>When thou with thy surpassing power smotest to death that guileful beast, lauding thine own supremacy."}, {"st": "42.5", "t": "Go forward, meet the foe, be bold; thy bolt of thunder is not checked!<br>Manliness, Indra, is thy strength. Slay Vritra, make the waters thine, lauding thine own supremacy!"}, {"st": "42.6", "t": "When war and battles are on foot, booty is offered to the bold.<br>Yoke thou thy wildly-rushing bays. Whom wilt thou slay, and whom enrich? Do thou, O Indra, make us rich!"}, {"st": "42.7", "t": "Well have they eaten and rejoiced; the friends have risen and passed away:<br>The sages luminous in themselves have praised thee with their latest hymn. Now, Indra, yoke thy two bay steeds!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "42.8", "t": "Graciously listen to our songs. Maghavan, be not negligent!<br>When wilt thou make us glorious? Make this, only this thine end and aim. Now, Indra! yoke thy two bay steeds."}, {"st": "42.9", "t": "Within the waters runs the Moon, he with the beauteous wings in heaven.<br>Ye lightnings with your golden wheels, men find not your abiding-place. Mark this my woe, ye Earth and Sky!"}, {"st": "42.10", "t": "To meet your treasure-bringing car, the mighty car most dear to us.<br>Asvins, the Rishi is prepared, your worshipper, with songs of praise. Lovers of sweetness, hear my call!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Agni and others"}, {"st": "43.1", "t": "O Agni, God, we kindle thee, refulgent, wasting not away,<br>That this more glorious fuel may send forth for thee its shine to heaven. Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"st": "43.2", "t": "With offerings of our own we choose thee, Agni, as our Hotar priest,<br>Piercing and brightly shining-at your glad carouse-served with trimmed grass at sacrifice. Thou waxest great."}, {"st": "43.3", "t": "O heavenly Dawn, awaken us to ample opulence to-day,<br>Even as thou didst waken us with Satyasravas, Vayya’s son, high born! delightful with thy steeds!"}, {"st": "43.4", "t": "Send us a mind that brings delight, send energy and mental power.<br>Then-at your glad carouse-let men joy in thy love, sweet juice! as kine in pasturage. Thou waxest great,"}, {"st": "43.5", "t": "Great, as his nature is, through power, terrible, he hath waxed in strength,<br>Lord of bay steeds, strong-jawed, sublime, he in joined hands for glory’s sake hath grasped his iron thunderbolt."}, {"st": "43.6", "t": "He, Indra, verily will mount the powerful car that finds the kine,<br>Who thinks upon the well-filled bowl, the tawny coursers’ harnesser. Now, Indra, yoke thy two bay steeds!"}, {"st": "43.7", "t": "I think of Agni who is kind, whom, as their home, the milch-kine seek:<br>Whom fleet-foot coursers seek as home, and strong enduring steeds as home. Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"st": "43.8", "t": "No peril, no severe distress, ye Gods, affects the mortal man<br>Whom Aryaman and Mitra lead, and Varuna, of one accord, beyond his foes."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "44.1", "t": "Flow forth, O Soma, flow thou onward, sweet to Indra’s Mitra’s, Pushan’s, Bhaga’s taste."}, {"st": "44.2", "t": "Run forth to battle, conquering the Vritras; thou speedest to quell the foes like one exacting debts."}, {"st": "44.3", "t": "Flow onward, Soma, as a mighty sea, as Father of the Gods, to every form."}, {"st": "44.4", "t": "Flow onward, Soma, flow for mighty strength, as a strong courser, bathed, to win the prize."}, {"st": "44.5", "t": "Fair Indu hath flowed on for rapturous joy, sage, for good fortune, in the waters’ lap."}, {"st": "44.6", "t": "In thee, effused. O Soma, we rejoice ourselves for great supremacy in fight:<br>Thou, Pavamana, enterest into mighty deeds."}, {"st": "44.7", "t": "Who are these radiant men in serried rank, Rudra’s young heroes, too, with noble steeds?"}, {"st": "44.8", "t": "Agni, with hymns may we now accomplish that which thou lovest,<br>Strength, like a horse, auspicious strength with service."}, {"st": "44.9", "t": "The strong youths have come forth to view, to show their strength, God Savitar’s quickening energy:<br>Ye warrior horsemen, win the heavens."}, {"st": "44.10", "t": "Soma, flow splendid with thy copious stream in due succession through the ample fleece."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · . Indra"}, {"st": "45.1", "t": "Giver from all sides, bring to us from every side, thou whom as strongest we entreat!"}, {"st": "45.2", "t": "This Brahman, comer at due time, named Indra, is renowned and praised."}, {"st": "45.3", "t": "The Brahmans with their hymns exalting Indra increased his strength that he might slaughter Ahi."}, {"st": "45.4", "t": "Anavas wrought a chariot for thy courser, and Tvashtar, much-invoked! the bolt that gitters:"}, {"st": "45.5", "t": "Rest, wealth to him who longs for wealth! the riteless stirs not his love nor wins his way to riches."}, {"st": "45.6", "t": "The cows are ever pure and all-supporting, the Gods are ever free from stain and blemish."}, {"st": "45.7", "t": "With all thy beauty come! The kine approaching with full udders follow on thy path."}, {"st": "45.8", "t": "May we, inhabiting a meath-rich dwelling, increase our wealth, and think of thee, O Indra!"}, {"st": "45.9", "t": "The Maruts with fair hymns chant out their praise-song: this Indra, famed and youthful, shouts accordant."}, {"st": "45.10", "t": "Sing to your Indra, mightiest Vritra-slayer, sing to the Sage the song that he accepteth!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Agni Indra"}, {"st": "46.1", "t": "Observant Agni hath appeared, oblation-bearer with his car."}, {"st": "46.2", "t": "O Agni, be our nearest friend, yea, our protector and our kind deliverer!"}, {"st": "46.3", "t": "Like wondrous Bhaga, Agni deals treasure among the mighty."}, {"st": "46.4", "t": "Far off or present even now, send forth thy shouting first of all!"}, {"st": "46.5", "t": "Dawn drives away her sister’s gloom, and through her excellence makes her retrace her path."}, {"st": "46.6", "t": "May we, with Indra and the Gods to aid us, bring these existing worlds to full completion!"}, {"st": "46.7", "t": "Like streams of water on their way, let bounties, Indra, flow from thee!"}, {"st": "46.8", "t": "With this may we obtain strength god-appointed, happy with brave sons through a hundred winters!"}, {"st": "46.9", "t": "With strength let Mitra, Varuna swell oblations; do thou prepare for us rich food, O Indra!"}, {"st": "46.10", "t": "Indra is King of all the world."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "47.1", "t": "At the Trikadrukas the great and strong enjoyed the barley-brew. With Vishnu did he drink the pressed-out Soma juice, even as he would.<br>That hath so heightened him the great, the wide to do his mighty work. So did the God attend the God, true Indu Indra who is true."}, {"st": "47.2", "t": "This God who sees for thousands of mankind, the light, the thought of poets, and the Law,<br>The brilliant one, hath sent forth hither all the Dawns: spotless, one-minded, zealous in their home they dwell, with thought upon the Steer."}, {"st": "47.3", "t": "Come to us, Indra, from afar, conducting us, as, to the gatherings, a Lord of heroes, as an archer King, the heroes’ Lord!<br>We come with gifts of pleasant food, with flowing juice, invoking thee, as sons invite a sire, that we may win the spoil, thee, bounteousest, for gain of spoil."}, {"st": "47.4", "t": "Loudly I call that Indra Maghavan, the mighty, resistless, evermore possessing many glories.<br>Holy, most liberal, may he lead us on to riches, through songs, and, thunder-armed make all our pathways pleasant!"}, {"st": "47.5", "t": "Heard be our prayer! In thought I honour Agni first: now straightway we elect this heavenly company, Indra and Vayu we elect.<br>For when our latest thought is raised and on Vivasvan centred well, then do our holy songs go forward on their way, our songs as ‘twere unto the Gods."}, {"st": "47.6", "t": "To Vishnu, to the mighty whom the Maruts follow, let your hymns born in song go forth, Evayamarut!<br>To the strong, very holy band adorned with bracelets, that rushes on in joy and ever roars for vigour!"}, {"st": "47.7", "t": "With this his golden splendour purifying him, be with his own allies subdues all enemies, as Sura with his own allies.<br>Cleansing himself with stream of juice he shines forth yellow-hued and red, when with the praisers he encompasses all, forms, with praisers having seven mouths."}, {"st": "47.8", "t": "I praise this God, parent of heaven and earth, exceeding wise, possessed of real energy, giver of treasure, thinker dear to all,<br>Whose splendour is sublime, whose light shone brilliant in, creation, who, wise and golden-handed, in his beauty made the sky.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [246, 245]]}, {"st": "47.9", "t": "Agni I deem our Hotar-priest, munificent wealth-giver, Son of Strength, who, knoweth all that is, even as the Sage who, knoweth all.<br>Lord of fair rites, a God with form erected turning to the Gods, he, when the flame hath sprung forth from the holy oil, the offered fatness, longs for it as it glows bright."}, {"st": "47.10", "t": "This, Indra! dancer! was thy hero deed, thy first and ancient work, worthy to be told forth in heaven,<br>Even thine who furtheredst life with a God’s own power, freeing the floods. All that is godless may he conquer with his might, and, Lord of Hundred Powers, find for us strength and food!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "48.1", "t": "High is thy juice’s birth: though set it heaven, on earth it hath obtained dread sheltering power and great renown."}, {"st": "48.2", "t": "In sweetest and most gladdening stream flow pure, O Soma, on thy way, pressed out for Indra, for his drink!"}, {"st": "48.3", "t": "Flow onward mighty with thy stream, inspiriting the Maruts’ Lord, winning all riches with thy power!"}, {"st": "48.4", "t": "Flow onward with that juice of thine most excellent, that brings delight, slaying the wicked, dear to Gods!"}, {"st": "48.5", "t": "Three several words are uttered: kine are lowing, cows who give the milk; the tawny-hued goes bellowing on."}, {"st": "48.6", "t": "For Indra girt by Maruts, flow, thou Indu, very rich in meath, to seat thee in the place of song!"}, {"st": "48.7", "t": "Strong, mountain-born, the stalk hath been pressed in the streams for rapturous joy. Hawk-like he settles in his home."}, {"st": "48.8", "t": "Gold-hued! as one who giveth strength flow on for Gods to drink, a draught for Vayu and the Marut host!"}, {"st": "48.9", "t": "Soma, the dweller on the hills, effused, hath flowed into the sieve. All-bounteous art thou in carouse."}, {"st": "48.10", "t": "The Sage of heaven whose heart is wise, when laid between both hands, with roars, gives us delightful powers of life."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "49.1", "t": "The rapture-shedding Somas have flowed forth in our assembly, pressed to glorify our liberal lords."}, {"st": "49.2", "t": "The Somas, skilled in song, the waves, have led the water forward, like buffaloes speeding to the woods."}, {"st": "49.3", "t": "Indu flow on, a mighty juice; glorify us among the folk: drive all our enemies away!"}, {"st": "49.4", "t": "For thou art strong by splendour: we, O Pavamana, call on thee, the brilliant looker on the light."}, {"st": "49.5", "t": "Indu, enlightener, dear, the thought of poets, hath flowed clearly, like a charioteer who starts the steed."}, {"st": "49.6", "t": "Through our desire of heroes, kine, and horses, potent Soma drops, brilliant and swift, have been effused.<br>God, working with mankind, flow on; to Indra go thy gladdening juice: to Vayu mount as Law commands!<br>From heaven hath Pavamana made, as ‘twere, the marvellous thunder, and the lofty light of all mankind."}, {"st": "49.9", "t": "Pressed for the gladdening draught the drops flow forth abundantly with song, flow onward with the stream of meath."}, {"st": "49.10", "t": "Reposing on the river’s wave, the Sage hath widely flowed around, bearing the bard whom many love."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "50.1", "t": "The Gods have come to Indu well-descended, beautified with milk, the active crusher of the foe."}, {"st": "50.2", "t": "Active, while being purified, he hath assailed all enemies: they deck the Sage with holy hymns."}, {"st": "50.3", "t": "Pouring all glories hither, he, effused, hath passed within the jar: Indu on Indra is bestowed."}, {"st": "50.4", "t": "From the two press-boards is the juice sent, like a car-horse, to the sieve: the steed steps forward to the goal."}, {"st": "50.5", "t": "Impetuous, bright, have they come forth, unwearied in their speed, like bulls, driving the black skin far away."}, {"st": "50.6", "t": "Soma, thou flowest chasing foes, finder of wisdom and delight: drive thou the godless folk afar!<br>Flow onward with that stream wherewith thou gavest splendour to the Sun, speeding the waters kind to man!"}, {"st": "50.8", "t": "Flow onward thou who strengthenedst Indra to slaughter Vritra who compassed and stayed the mighty floods!"}, {"st": "50.9", "t": "Flow onward, Indu, with this food for him who in thy wild delights battered the nine-and-ninety down!"}, {"st": "50.10", "t": "Flow, pressed, into the filter, speed the heavenly one who winneth wealth, who bringeth booty through our juice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "51.1", "t": "The tawny Bull hath bellowed, fair as mighty Mitra to behold: he gleams and flashes with the Sun."}, {"st": "51.2", "t": "We choose to-day that chariot-steed of thine, the strong, that brings us bliss, the guardian, the desire of all."}, {"st": "51.3", "t": "Adhvaryu, to the filter lead the Soma juice expressed with stones: make thou it pure for Indra’s drink."}, {"st": "51.4", "t": "Swift runs this giver of delight, even the stream of flowingjuice: Swift runs this giver of delight."}, {"st": "51.5", "t": "Pour hitherward, O Soma, wealth in thousands and heroic strength, and keep renown secure for us!<br>-6. The ancient living ones have come unto a newer resting-place. They made the Sun that he might shine."}, {"st": "51.7", "t": "Soma, flow on exceeding bright with loud roar to the reservoirs, resting in wooden vats, thy home!"}, {"st": "51.8", "t": "O Soma, thou, art strong and bright, potent, O God, with potent sway: thou, mighty one, ordainest laws."}, {"st": "51.9", "t": "For food, flow onward with thy stream, cleansed and made bright by sapient men: Indu. with sheen approach the milk!"}, {"st": "51.10", "t": "Soma, flow on with pleasant stream, strong and devoted to the Gods, our friend, unto the woollen sieve."}, {"st": "51.11", "t": "By this solemnity, Soma, thou, though great, hast been increased: in joy thou, verily actest like a bull!"}, {"st": "51.12", "t": "Most active and benevolent, this Pavamana sent to us for lofty friendship meditates."}, {"st": "51.13", "t": "Indu, to us for this great rite, bearing as ‘twere thy wave to Gods, unwearied, thou art flowing on."}, {"st": "51.14", "t": "Chasing our foemen, driving off the godless, Soma floweth on, going to Indra’s settled place."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "52.1", "t": "Cleansing thee, Soma, in thy stream, thou flowest in a watery robe: giver of wealth, thou sittest in the place of Law, O God, a fountain made of gold."}, {"st": "52.2", "t": "Hence sprinkle forth the juice effused, Soma, the best of sacred gifts, who, friend of man, hath run amid the water-streams! He hath pressed Soma out with stones."}, {"st": "52.3", "t": "Expressed by stones, O Soma, and urged through the long wool of the sheep, thou, entering the press-boards even as men a fort, gold-hued hast settled in the vats."}, {"st": "52.4", "t": "O Soma, — for the feast of Gods, river-like he hath swelled with surge, sweet with the liquor of the stalk, as one who wakes, into the vat that drops with meath."}, {"st": "52.5", "t": "Pressed out by pressers, Soma goes over the fleecy backs of sheep, goes, even as with a mare, in tawny-coloured stream, goes in a sweetly-sounding stream."}, {"st": "52.6", "t": "O Soma, Indu, every day thy friendship hath been my delight. Many fiends follow me help me, thou tawny-hued: pass on beyond these barriers!"}, {"st": "52.7", "t": "Deft-handed! thou when purified liftest thy voice amid the sea. Thou, Pavamana, makest riches flow to us, yellow, abundant, much desired."}, {"st": "52.8", "t": "The living drops of Soma juice pour, as they flow, the gladdening drink, intelligent drops above the station of the sea, exhilarating, dropping meath."}, {"st": "52.9", "t": "Soma, while thou art cleansed, most dear and watchful in the sheep’s long wool, most like to Angiras! thou hast become a sage. Sprinkle our sacrifice with mead!"}, {"st": "52.10", "t": "Soma, the gladdening juice, flows pressed for Indra with his Marut host: he hastens o’er the fleece with all his thousand streams: him, him the men make pure and bright."}, {"st": "52.11", "t": "Flow on, best winner of the spoil, to precious gifts of every sort! Thou art a sea according to the highest law, joy-giver, Soma! to the Gods"}, {"st": "52.12", "t": "Over the cleansing sieve have flowed the Pavamanas in a stream, girt by the Maruts, gladdening, steeds with Indra’s strength, for wisdom and for dainty food."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "53.1", "t": "Run onward to the reservoir and seat thee: cleansed by the men speed forward to the battle!<br>Making thee glossy like an able courser, forth to the sacred grass with reins they lead thee."}, {"st": "53.2", "t": "The God declares the deities’ generations, like Uaana, proclaiming lofty wisdom.<br>With brilliant kin, far-ruling, sanctifying, the wild boar, singing with his foot, advances."}, {"st": "53.3", "t": "Three are the voices that the car-steed utters: he speaks the lore of prayer, the thought of Order.<br>To the cows’ master come the cows inquiring: the hymns with eager longing come to Soma."}, {"st": "53.4", "t": "Made pure by this man’s urgent zeal and impulse, the God hath with his juice the Gods pervaded.<br>Pressed, singing, to the sieve he goes, as passes the Hotar to enclosures holding cattle."}, {"st": "53.5", "t": "Father of holy hymns Soma flows onward, the father of the earth, father of heaven;<br>Father of Agni, Surya’s generator, the father who begat Indra and Vishnu"}, {"st": "53.6", "t": "To him, praiseworthy, sacred tones have sounded, Steer of the triple height, the life-bestower.<br>Dwelling in wood, like Varuna, a river, lavishing treasure, he distributes blessings."}, {"st": "53.7", "t": "Guard of all being, generating creatures, loud roared the sea as highest law commanded.<br>Strong, in the filter, on the fleecy summit, pressed from the stone, Soma hath waxen mighty."}, {"st": "53.8", "t": "Loud neighs the tawny steed when started, settling deep in the wooden vessel while they cleanse him.<br>Led by the men he makes the milk his raiment; then shall he, of himself, engender worship."}, {"st": "53.9", "t": "This thine own Soma, rich in meath, O Indra, the Strong, hath flowed into the Strong One’s filter.<br>The swift steed, bounteous, giving hundreds, thousands, hath reached the sacred grass which never fails him."}, {"st": "53.10", "t": "Flow onward, Soma, rich in meath, and holy, enrobed in waters, on the fleecy summit!<br>Settle in vessels that are full of fatness, as cheering and most gladdening drink for Indra!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "54.1", "t": "In forefront of the cars forth goes the hero, the leader, seeking spoil: his host rejoices.<br>Soma endues his robe of lasting colours, and blesses, for his friends, their calls on Indra."}, {"st": "54.2", "t": "Thy streams have been poured forth with all their sweetness, when, cleansed thou passest through the woollen filter.<br>The race of kine thou cleansest, Pavamana! Thou didst beget: and speed the Sun with splendours."}, {"st": "54.3", "t": "Let us sing praises to the Gods: sing loudly, send ye the Soma forth for mighty riches!<br>Let him flow, sweetly-flavoured, through the filter: let the God Indu settle in the beaker!"}, {"st": "54.4", "t": "Urged on, the father of the earth and heaven hath gone forth like a car to gather booty.<br>Going to Indra, sharpening his weapons, and in his hands containing every treasure."}, {"st": "54.5", "t": "When, by the law of the Most High, in presence of heaven and earth, the fond mind’s utterance formed him.<br>Then, loudly lowing, came the cows to Indu, the chosen, wellloved master in the beaker."}, {"st": "54.6", "t": "Ten sisters, pouring out the rain together, the sage’s quickly-moving thoughts, adorn him.<br>Hither hath run the gold-hued child of Surya, and reached the vat like a fleet vigorous courser."}, {"st": "54.7", "t": "When beauties strive for him as for a charger, then strive the songs as people for the sunlight.<br>A mighty Sage, he flows enrobed in waters and hymns as ‘twere a stall that kine may prosper.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [154, 155], [156, 156]]}, {"st": "54.8", "t": "Strong Indu, bathed in milk, flows on for Indra, Soma exciting, strength, for his carousal.<br>He quells malignity and slays the demons, King of the homestead, he who gives us comfort."}, {"st": "54.9", "t": "Pour forth this wealth with this purification: flow onward to the yellow lake, O Indu!<br>Here, too, the bright one, wind-swift, full of wisdom, shall give a son to him who cometh quickly."}, {"st": "54.10", "t": "Soma, the mighty, when, the waters’ offspring, he chose the Gods, performed that great achievement.<br>He, Pavamana, granted strength to Indra: he, Indu, generated light in Surya."}, {"st": "54.11", "t": "As for a chariot-race, the skilful speaker, first hymn, inventor, hath with song been started.<br>The sisters ten upon the fleecy summit adorn the car-horse in the resting-places."}, {"st": "54.12", "t": "Hastening onward like the waves of waters our holy hymns are coming forth to Soma.<br>To him they go with lowly adoration, and, longing, enter him who longs to meet them."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "55.1", "t": "For first possession of your juice. for the exhilarating drink,<br>Drive ye away the dog, my friends, drive ye the long-tongued dog away!"}, {"st": "55.2", "t": "As Pushan. Fortune, Bhaga, comes this Soma while they make him pure.<br>He, Lord of all the multitude, hath looked upon the earth and heaven."}, {"st": "55.3", "t": "The Somas, very rich in sweets, for which the sieve is destined, flow<br>Effused, the source of Indra’s joy: may your strong juices reach the Gods!"}, {"st": "55.4", "t": "For us the Soma juices flow, the drops best furtherers of weal,<br>Effused as friends, without a spot, benevolent, finders of the. light."}, {"st": "55.5", "t": "Stream on us riches that are craved by hundreds, best at winning spoil,<br>Riches, O Indu, thousandfold, most splendid, that surpass the light!"}, {"st": "55.6", "t": "The guileless ones are singing praise to Indra’s well-beloved friend,<br>As, in the morning of its life, the mothers lick the new-born calf."}, {"st": "55.7", "t": "They for the bold and lovely one ply manly vigour like a bow;<br>Bright, glad, in front of songs they spread to form a vesture for the Lord."}, {"st": "55.8", "t": "Him with ths fleece they purify, brown, golden-hued, beloved of all,<br>Who with exhilarating juice goes forth to all the deities."}, {"st": "55.9", "t": "Let him, as mortal, crave this speech, for him who presses, of the juice,<br>As Bhrigu’s sons chased Makha, so drive ye the niggard hound away!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "56.1", "t": "Graciously-minded he is flowing on his way to win dear names o’er which the youthful one grows great.<br>The mighty and far-seeing one hath mounted now the mighty Surya’s car which moves to every side."}, {"st": "56.2", "t": "Spontaneous let our drops of Soma juice flow on, pressed out and tawny-coloured, mightily, to the Gods!<br>Still let our enemies, the godless, be in want, though filled with food; and let our prayers obtain success!"}, {"st": "56.3", "t": "Most beauteous of the beauteous, Indra’s thunderbolt, this Soma, rich in sweets, hath clamoured in the vat.<br>Dropping with oil, abundant, streams of sacrifice flow unto him, and milch-kine, lowing, with their milk."}, {"st": "56.4", "t": "Indu hath started forth for Indra’s settled place, and slights not, as a friend, the promise of his friend.<br>Soma comes onward like a youth with youthful maids, and gains the beaker by a course of hundred paths."}, {"st": "56.5", "t": "On flows the potent juice, sustainer of the heavens; the strength of Gods, whom men must hail with shouts of joy.<br>Thou, gold-hued, started like a courser by brave men, art lightly showing forth thy splendour in the streams."}, {"st": "56.6", "t": "Far-seeing Soma flows, the Steer, the Lord of hymns, the furtherer of days, of mornings, and of heaven.<br>Breath of the rivers, he hath roared into the jars, and with the help of sages entered Indra’s heart."}, {"st": "56.7", "t": "The three-times seven milch-kine in the loftiest heaven have for this Soma poured the genuine milky draught.<br>Four other beauteous creatures hath he made for his adornment when he waxed in strength through holy rites."}, {"st": "56.8", "t": "Flow on to indra, Soma, carefully effused: let sickness stay afar together with the fiend!<br>Let not the double-tongued delight them with thy juice: here be thy flowing drops laden with opulence!"}, {"st": "56.9", "t": "Even as a King hath Soma, red and tawny Bull, been pressed: the wondrous one hath bellowed to the kine.<br>While purified thou passest through the filtering fleece to seat thee hawk-like on the place that drops with oil."}, {"st": "56.10", "t": "The drops of Soma juice, like cows who yield their milk, have flowed forth, rich in meath, unto the diety,<br>And, seated on the grass, raising their voice, assumed the milk, the covering robe wherewith the address stream."}, {"st": "56.11", "t": "They balm him, balm him over, balm him thoroughly, caress the mighty strength and balm it with the meath.<br>They seize the flying Steer at the stream’s breathing-place: cleansing with gold they grasp the animal herein."}, {"st": "56.12", "t": "Spread is thy cleansing filter, Brahmanaspati: as prince thou enterest its limbs from every side.<br>The raw, whose mass hath not been heated, gains not this: they only which are dressed, which bear, attain to it."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "57.1", "t": "To Indra, to the mighty one, let these gold-coloured juices go,<br>Drops born as Law prescribes, that find the light of heaven!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "57.2", "t": "Flow vigilant for Indra, thou Soma, yea, Indu, run thou forth;<br>Bring hither splendid strength that finds the light of heaven!"}, {"st": "57.3", "t": "Sit down, O friends, and sing aloud to him who purifies himself.<br>Deck him for glory, like a child, with holy rites!"}, {"st": "57.4", "t": "Friends, hymn your Lord who makes him pure for rapturous<br>carouse: let them<br>Sweeten him, as a child, with lauds and sacred gifts!"}, {"st": "57.5", "t": "Breath of the mighty Dames, the Child, speeding the plan of’ sacrifice,<br>Surpasses all things that are dear, yea, from of old!"}, {"st": "57.6", "t": "In might, O Indu, with thy streams flow for the banquet of the Gods:<br>Rich in meath, Soma, in our beaker take thy seat!"}, {"st": "57.7", "t": "Soma, while filtered, with his wave flows through the long wool of the sheep,<br>Roaring, while purified, before the voice of song."}, {"st": "57.8", "t": "The speech is uttered for the Sage, for Soma being purified:<br>Bring meed as ‘twere to one who makes thee glad with hymns!"}, {"st": "57.9", "t": "Flow to us, Indu, very strong, effused, with wealth of kine and, steeds,<br>And do thou lay above the milk thy radiant hue!"}, {"st": "57.10", "t": "Voices have sung aloud to thee as finder-out of wealth for us:<br>We clothe the hue thou wearest with a robe of milk."}, {"st": "57.11", "t": "Gold-hued and lovely in his course through tangles of the wool he flows:<br>Stream forth heroic fame upon the worshippers!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [63, 62]]}, {"st": "57.12", "t": "On through the long wool of the sheep to the meath-dropping vat he flows:<br>The Rishis’ sevenfold quire hath sung aloud to him."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Decade 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. For Indra flow, thou Soma, on, as most inspiring drink, exceeding rich in sweets.<br>Great, most celestial, gladdening drink!<br>2. Make high and splendid glory shine hitherward, Lord of food, God, on the friend of Gods:<br>Unclose the cask of middle air!<br>3. Press ye and pour him, like a steed, laud-worthy, speeding through the region and the flood,<br>Who swims in water, dwells in wood!<br>4. Him, even this Steer who milks the heavens, him with a thousand streams, distilling rapturous joy,<br>Him who brings all things excellent.<br>5. Effused is he who brings good things, who brings us store of’ wealth and sweet refreshing food,<br>Soma who brings us quiet homes.<br>6. For, verily, Pavamana, thou, divine! endued with brightest splendour calling all<br>Creatures to immortality.<br>7. Effused, he floweth in a stream, best rapture-giver, in the longwool of the sheep,<br>Sporting, as ‘twere the waters’ wave.<br>8. He who from out the rocky cavern with his might took forth the red-refulgent cows — <br>Thou drewest to thyself the stall of kine and steeds: burst it,<br>brave Lord, like one in mail; yea, burst it, O brave Lord, like one in mail!"}, {"sp": "HDR", "t": "CHAPTER I"}, {"st": "", "t": "OM. GLORY TO the Samaveda! to Lord Ganesa glory! Om."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "59.1", "t": "Sing forth to Indu, O ye men, to him who now is purified,<br>Fain to pay worship to the Gods!<br>2, Together with thy pleasant juice the Atharvans have commingled. milk.<br>Divine, God-loving, for the God."}, {"st": "59.3", "t": "Bring health to cattle with thy flow, health to the people, health, to steeds,<br>Health, O thou King, to growing plants!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "60.1", "t": "Bright are these Somas blent with milk, with light that flashes brilliantly,<br>And form that shouteth all around."}, {"st": "60.2", "t": "Roused by his drivers and sent forth, the strong Steed hath come: nigh for spoil,<br>As warriors when they stand arrayed."}, {"st": "60.3", "t": "Specially, Soma, Sage, by day, coming together for our weal,<br>Like Surya, flow for us to see!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "61.1", "t": "The streams of Pavamana, thine, Sage, mighty one, have poured them forth,<br>Like coursers eager for renown."}, {"st": "61.2", "t": "They have been poured upon the Reece towards the meath-distilling vat:<br>The holy songs have rung aloud."}, {"st": "61.3", "t": "Like milch-kine coming home, the drops of Soma juice have reached the lake,<br>Have reached the shrine of sacrifice"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Agni"}, {"st": "62.1", "t": "Come, Agni, praised with song to feast and sacrificial offerings: sit<br>As Hotar on the holy grass!"}, {"st": "62.2", "t": "So, Angiras, we make thee strong with fuel and with holy oil.<br>Blaze high, thou youngest of the Gods!"}, {"st": "62.3", "t": "For us thou winnest, Agni, God, heroic strength exceeding great, Far-spreading and of high renown."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Mitra Varuna"}, {"st": "63.1", "t": "Varuna, Mitra, sapient pair, pour fatness on our pastures, pour<br>Meath on the regions of the air!<br>2, Gladdened by homage, ruling far, ye reign by majesty of might,<br>Pure in your ways, for evermore."}, {"st": "63.3", "t": "Lauded by Jamadagni’s song, sit in the shrine of sacrifice:<br>Drink Soma, ye who strengthen Law!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Indra"}, {"st": "64.1", "t": "Come, we have pressed theJuice for thee; O Indra, drink this Soma here:<br>Sit thou on this my sacred grass!"}, {"st": "64.2", "t": "O Indra, let thy long-maned bays, yoked by prayer, bring thee hitherward!<br>Give ear and listen to our prayers!"}, {"st": "64.3", "t": "We Soma-bearing Brahmans call thee Soma-drinker with thy friend,<br>We, Indra, bringing Soma juice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Indra Agni"}, {"st": "65.1", "t": "Indra and Agni, moved by songs, come to the juice, the precious dew:<br>Drink ye thereof, impelled by prayer!"}, {"st": "65.2", "t": "Indra and Agni, with the man who lauds comes visible sacrifice:<br>So drink ye both this flowing juice!"}, {"st": "65.3", "t": "With force of sacrifice I seek Indra, Agni who love the wise:<br>With Soma let them sate them here!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "66.1", "t": "High is thy juice’s birth: though set in heaven, on earth it hath obtained<br>Dread sheltering power and great renown."}, {"st": "66.2", "t": "Finder of room and freedom, flow for Indra whom we must adore,<br>For Varuna and the Marut host!"}, {"st": "66.3", "t": "Striving to win, with him we gain all riches from the enemy,<br>Yea, all the glories of mankind,"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "67.1", "t": "Cleansing thee, Soma, in thy stream, thou flowest in watery robe.<br>Giver of wealth, thou sittest in the place of Law, O God, a fountain made of gold."}, {"st": "67.2", "t": "He, milking for dear meath the heavenly udder, hath sat in the ancient gathering-place.<br>Washed by the men, far-sighted, strong, thou streamest to ther honourable reservoir."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "68.1", "t": "Run onward to the reservoir and seat thee: cleansed by the men speed forward to the battle.<br>Making thee glossy like an able courser, forth to the sacred grass with reins they lead thee."}, {"st": "68.2", "t": "Indu, the well-armed God is flowing onward, he who averts the curse and guards the homesteads.<br>Father, begetter of the Gods, most skilful, the buttress of the heavens and earth’s supporter."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Indra"}, {"st": "69.1", "t": "Like kine unmilked we call aloud, hero, to thee, and sing thy<br>praise,<br>Looker on heavenly light, Lord of this moving world, Lord, Indra! of what moveth not."}, {"st": "69.2", "t": "None other like to thee, of earth or of the heavens, hath been or ever will be born.<br>Desiring horses, Indra Maghavan! and kine, as men of might we call on thee."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Indra"}, {"st": "70.1", "t": "With what help will he come to us, wonderful, everwaxing friend?<br>With what most mighty company?"}, {"st": "70.2", "t": "What genuine and most liberal draught will spirit thee with juice to burst<br>Open e’en strongly-guarded wealth?"}, {"st": "70.3", "t": "Do thou who art protector of us thy friends who praise thee<br>With hundred aids approach us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "71.1", "t": "As cows low to their calves in stalls, so with our songs we glorify<br>This Indra, even your wondrous God who checks attack, who takes delight in precious juice."}, {"st": "71.2", "t": "Celestial, bounteous giver, girt about with might, rich, mountain-like, in pleasant things, — <br>Him swift we seek for foodful booty rich in kine, brought hundredfold and thousandfold."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "72.1", "t": "Loud-singing at the sacred rite where Soma flows, we priests invoke.<br>With haste, that he may help, as the bard’s cherisher. Indra who findeth wealth for you."}, {"st": "72.2", "t": "Whom, fair of cheek, in rapture of the juice, the firm resistless slayers hinder not:<br>Giver of glorious wealth to him who sings his praise, honouring him who toils and pours."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "73.1", "t": "In sweetest and most gladdening stream flow pure, O Soma, on thy way,<br>Pressed out for Indra, for his drink!"}, {"st": "73.2", "t": "Fiend-queller, friend of all men, he hath reached his shrine, his dwelling-place.<br>Within the iron-hammered vat."}, {"st": "73.3", "t": "Be thou best Vritra-slaver, best granter of room, most liberal:<br>Promote our wealthy princes’ gifts!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "74.1", "t": "For Indra flow, thou Soma, on, as most inspiring drink, most rich in sweets,<br>Great, most Celestial, gladdening drink!"}, {"st": "74.2", "t": "Thou of whom having drunk the Steer acts like a steer: having drunk this that finds the light,<br>He, excellently wise, hath come anear to food and booty, even as Etasa."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Indra"}, {"st": "75.1", "t": "To Indra, to the mighty let these golden-coloured juices go,<br>Drops born as Law prescribes, that find the light of heaven!"}, {"st": "75.2", "t": "This juice that gathers spoil flows, pressed, for Indra, for his maintenance.<br>Soma bethinks him of the conqueror, as he knows."}, {"st": "75.3", "t": "Yea, Indra in the joys of this obtains the grasp that gathers spoil,<br>And, winning waters, wields the mighty thunderbolt."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "76.1", "t": "For first possession of your juice, for the exhilarating drink,<br>Drive ye away the dog, my friends, drive ye the long-tongued dog away!"}, {"st": "76.2", "t": "He who with purifying stream, effused, comes flowing hitherward,<br>Indu, is like an able steed."}, {"st": "76.3", "t": "With prayer all-reaching let the men tend unassailable Soma: be-<br>The stones prepared for sacrifice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "77.1", "t": "Graciously-minded he is flowing on his way to win dear names o’er which the youthful one grows great.<br>The mighty and far-seeing one hath mounted now the mighty<br>Surya’s car which moves to every side."}, {"st": "77.2", "t": "The speaker, unassailable master of this prayer, the tongue of sacrifice, pours forth the pleasant meath.<br>As son be sets the name of mother and of sire in the far distance, in the third bright realm of heaven."}, {"st": "77.3", "t": "Sending forth flashes he hath bellowed to the jars, led by the men into the golden reservoir.<br>The milkers of the sacrifice have sung to him: Lord of three heights, thou shinest brightly o’er the Dawns."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Agni"}, {"st": "78.1", "t": "Sing to your Agni with each song, at every sacrifice for strength!<br>Come, let us praise the wise and everlasting God, even as a well-beloved friend:"}, {"st": "78.2", "t": "The Son of Strength; for is be not our gracious Lord? Let us serve him who bears our gifts!<br>In battles may he be our help and strengthener, yea, be the saviour of our lives!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 21 · Agni"}, {"st": "79.1", "t": "O Agni, come; far other songs of praise will I sing forth to thee.<br>Wax mighty with these Soma drops!"}, {"st": "79.2", "t": "Where’er thy mind applies itself, vigour preeminent hast thou:<br>There wilt thou gain a dwelling-place."}, {"st": "79.3", "t": "Not for a moment only lasts thy bounty, Lord of many men:<br>Our service therefore shalt thou gain."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 22 · Indra"}, {"st": "80.1", "t": "We call on thee, O matchless one. We, seeking help, possessing nothing firm ourselves.<br>Call on thee, wondrous, thunder-armed:"}, {"st": "80.2", "t": "On thee for aid in sacrifice, This youth of ours, the bold, the terrible, bath gone forth.<br>We therefore, we thy friends, Indra, have chosen thee, spoil winner, as our succourer."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 23 · Indra"}, {"st": "81.1", "t": "So, Indra, friend of song, do we draw near to thee with longing; we have streamed to thee<br>Coming like floods that follow floods."}, {"st": "81.2", "t": "As rivers swell the ocean, so, hero, our prayers increase thy might,<br>Though of thyself, O Thunderer, waxing day by day."}, {"st": "81.3", "t": "With holy song they bind to the broad wide-yoked car the bay steeds of the quickening God,<br>Bearers of Indra, yoked by word."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Indra"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Invite ye Indra with a song to drink your draught of Soma juicel<br>All-conquering Satakratu, most munificent of all who live!<br>2. Lauded by many, much-invoked, leader of song renowned of old:<br>His name is Indra, tell it forth!<br>3. Indra, the dancer, be to us the giver of abundant wealth:<br>The mighty bring it us knee-deep!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "83.1", "t": "Sing ye a song, to make him glad, to Indra, Lord of tawny steeds,<br>The Soma-drinker, O my friends!"}, {"st": "83.2", "t": "To him, the bounteous, say the laud, and let us glorify, as men<br>May do, the giver of true gifts!"}, {"st": "83.3", "t": "O Indra, Lord of boundless might, for us thou seekest spoil and kine,<br>Thou seekest gold for us, good Lord!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "84.1", "t": "This, even this, O Indra, we implore: as thy devoted friends,<br>The Kanvas praise thee with their hymns."}, {"st": "84.2", "t": "Naught else, O Thunderer, have I praised in the skilled singer’s eulogy;<br>On thy laud only have I thought."}, {"st": "84.3", "t": "The Gods seek him who presses out the Soma; they desire not sleep:<br>They punish sloth unweariedly"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "85.1", "t": "For Indra, lover of carouse, loud be our songs about the juice:<br>Let poets sing the song of praise"}, {"st": "85.2", "t": "We summon Indra to the draught, in whom all glories rest, in whom<br>The seven communities rejoice."}, {"st": "85.3", "t": "At the Trikadrukas the Gods span sacrifice that stirs the mind:<br>Let our songs aid and prosper it!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "86.1", "t": "Here, Indra, is thy Soma draught, made pure upon the sacred grass:<br>Run hither, come and drink thereof!"}, {"st": "86.2", "t": "Strong-rayed! adored with earnest hymns! this juice is shed for thy delight:<br>Thou art invoked, Akhandala!"}, {"st": "86.3", "t": "To Kundapayya, grandson’s son, grandson of Sringavrish! to thee,<br>To him have I addressed my thought."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Indra"}, {"st": "87.1", "t": "Indra, as one with mighty arm, gather for us with thy right hand,<br>Manifold and nutritious spoil!"}, {"st": "87.2", "t": "We know thee mighty in thy deeds, of mighty bounty, mighty wealth.<br>Mighty in measure, prompt to aid."}, {"st": "87.3", "t": "Hero when thou wouldst give thy gifts, neither the Gods nor mortal men<br>Restrain thee like a fearful bull."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Indra"}, {"st": "88.1", "t": "Hero, the Soma being shed, I pour the juice for thee to drink:<br>Sate thee and finish thy carouse!"}, {"st": "88.2", "t": "Let not the fools, or those who mock, beguile thee when they seek thine aid:<br>Love not the enemy of prayer!"}, {"st": "88.3", "t": "Here let them cheer thee well supplied with milk to great munificence:<br>Drink as the wild bull drinks the lake!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Indra", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Here is the Soma juice expressed: O Vasu, drink till thou art full!<br>Undaunted God, we give it thee!<br>2. Washed by the men, pressed out with stones, strained through the filter made of wool,<br>’Tis like a courser bathed in streams.<br>3. This juice have we made sweet for thee like barley, blending it with milk.<br>Indra, I call thee to our feast."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra"}, {"st": "90.1", "t": "So, Lord of affluent gifts, this juice hath been expressed for thee with strength:<br>Drink of it, thou who lovest song!"}, {"st": "90.2", "t": "Incline thy body to the juice which suits thy godlike nature well:<br>Thee, Soma-lover! let it cheer!"}, {"st": "90.3", "t": "O Indra, let it enter both thy flanks, enter thy head with prayer,<br>With bounty, hero! both thine arms!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Indra"}, {"st": "91.1", "t": "O Come ye hither, sit ye down; to Indra sing ye forth your song,<br>Companions, bringing hymns of praise,"}, {"st": "91.2", "t": "Laud Indra, richest of the rich, who ruleth over noblest wealth,<br>Beside the flowing Soma juice!"}, {"st": "91.3", "t": "May he stand near us in our need with all abundance, for our wealth:<br>With strength may he come nigh to us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Indra"}, {"st": "92.1", "t": "In every need, in every fray we call, as friends to succour us,<br>Indra, the mightiest of all."}, {"st": "92.2", "t": "I call him, mighty to resist, the hero of our ancient home,<br>Thee whom my sire invoked of old."}, {"st": "92.3", "t": "If he will hear us, let him come with succour of a thousand kinds,<br>With strength and riches, to our call!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Indra"}, {"st": "93.1", "t": "When Somas flow thou makest pure, Indra, thy mind that merits laud,<br>For gain of strength that ever grows: for great is he."}, {"st": "93.2", "t": "In heaven’s first region, in the seat of Gods, is he who brings success,<br>Most glorious, prompt to save, who wins the waterfloods."}, {"st": "93.3", "t": "Him I invoke, to win the spoil, even mighty Indra for the fray.<br>Be thou most near to us for bliss, a friend to aid!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Agni"}, {"st": "94.1", "t": "With this mine homage I invoke Agni for you, the Son of Strength.<br>Dear, wisest envoy, skilled in noble sacrifice, immortal, messanger of all."}, {"st": "94.2", "t": "His two red horses, all-supporting, let him yoke: let him, well-worshipped, urge them fast!<br>Then hath the sacrifice good prayers and happy end, the heavenly gift of wealth to men."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Dawn"}, {"st": "95.1", "t": "Advancing, sending forth her rays, the daughter of the Sky is seen.<br>The mighty one lays bare the darkness with her eye, the friendly Lady makes the light."}, {"st": "95.2", "t": "The Sun ascending, the refulgent star, pours down his beams. together with the Dawn.<br>O Dawn, at thine arising, and, the Sun’s, may we attain the share allotted us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Asvins"}, {"st": "96.1", "t": "These morning sacrifices call you, Asvins, at the break of day.<br>For help have I invoked you rich in power and might: for, house by house, ye visit all."}, {"st": "96.2", "t": "Ye, heroes, have bestowed wonderful nourishment: send it to him whose songs are sweet.<br>One-minded, both of you, drive your car down to us: drink yethe savoury Soma juice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "97.1", "t": "After his ancient splendour, they, the bold, have drawn the bright milk from<br>The Sage who wins a thousand spoils."}, {"st": "97.2", "t": "In aspect he is like the Sun: he runneth forward to the lakes: Seven currents flowing to the sky."}, {"st": "97.3", "t": "He, while they purify him, stands high over all things that exist Soma, a God as Surya is."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "98.1", "t": "By generation long ago this God, engendered for the Gods,<br>Flows tawny to the straining cloth."}, {"st": "98.2", "t": "According to primeval plan this poet hath been strengthened by,<br>The sage as God for all the Gods."}, {"st": "98.3", "t": "Shedding the ancient fluid thou art poured into the cleansing sieve:<br>Roaring, thou hast produced the Gods.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "99.1", "t": "Bring near us those who stand aloof: strike fear into our enemy:<br>O Pavamana, find us wealth!"}, {"st": "99.2", "t": "To him the active, nobly born."}, {"st": "99.3", "t": "Sing ye your songs to him, O men!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "100.1", "t": "The Somas skilled in song, the waves have led the water forward, like<br>Buffaloes speeding to the woods."}, {"st": "100.2", "t": "With stream of sacrifice the brown bright drops have flowed with strength in store<br>Of kine into the wooden vats."}, {"st": "100.3", "t": "To Indra, Vayu. Varuna to Vishnu and the Maruts let<br>The Soma juices flow expressed."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "101.1", "t": "O Soma, for the feast of Gods, river-like he hath swelled with surge,<br>Sweet with the liquor of the stalk, as one who wakes, into the vat that drops with meath."}, {"st": "101.2", "t": "Like a dear son how must be decked, the bright and shining one hath clad him in his robe.<br>Men skilful at their work drive him forth, like a car, into the rivers from their hands."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 21 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "102.1", "t": "The rapture-shedding Somas have flowed forth in our assembly, pressed.<br>To glorify our liberal lords."}, {"st": "102.2", "t": "Now like a swan hemaketh all the company sing each his hymm<br>He like steed is bathed in milk."}, {"st": "102.3", "t": "And Trita’s maidens onward urge the tawny-coloured with the stones,<br>Indu for Indra, for his drink."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 22 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "103.1", "t": "Herewith flow on, thou friend of Gods! Singing, thou runnest round the sieve oni every side.<br>The streams of meath have been effused."}, {"st": "103.2", "t": "Lovely, gold-coloured, on he flows."}, {"st": "103.3", "t": "For him who presses, of the juice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "104.1", "t": "Soma, as leader of the song, flow onward with thy wondrous aid.<br>For holy lore of every sort!"}, {"st": "104.2", "t": "Do thou as leader of the song, stirring the waters of the sea,<br>Flow onward, known to all mankind!"}, {"st": "104.1", "t": "O Soma, O thou Sage, these worlds stand ready to enhance thy might:<br>The milch-kine run for thy behoof."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "105.1", "t": "Indu, flow on, a mighty juice; glorify us among the folk:<br>Drive all our enemies away!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [76, 75]]}, {"st": "105.2", "t": "And in thy friendship, Indu, most sublime and glorious, may we<br>Subdue all those who war with us!"}, {"st": "105.3", "t": "Those awful weapons which thou hast, sharpened at point to strike men down — <br>Guard us therewith from every foe!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "106.1", "t": "O Soma, thou art strong and bright, potent, O God, with potent sway,"}, {"st": "106.2", "t": "Steer-strong thy might is like a steer’s, steer-strong the wood, steer-strong the juice:<br>A steer indeed, O Steer, art thou."}, {"st": "106.3", "t": "Thou, Indu, as a vigorous horse, hast neighed together steeds and kine:<br>Unbar for us the doors to wealth!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "107.1", "t": "For thou art strong by splendour: we, O Pavamana call on thee,<br>The brilliant looker on the light."}, {"st": "107.2", "t": "When thou art sprinkled with the streams, thou reachest, purified by men,<br>Thy dwelling in the wooden vat."}, {"st": "107.3", "t": "Do thou, rejoicing, nobly-armed! pour upon us heroic strength.<br>O Indu, come thou hitherward!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "108.1", "t": "We seek to win thy friendly love, even Pavamana’s flowing o’er<br>The limit of the cleansing sieve."}, {"st": "108.2", "t": "With those same waves which in their stream o’erflow the purifying sieve,<br>Soma, be gracious unto us!"}, {"st": "108.3", "t": "O Soma, being purified, bring us from all sides-for thou canst-<br>Riches and food with hero sons!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Agni"}, {"st": "109.1", "t": "Agni we choose as envoy, skilled performer of this holy rite,<br>Hotar, possessor of all wealth."}, {"st": "109.2", "t": "With constant calls they invocate Agni, Agni, Lord of the house,<br>Oblation-bearer, much-beloved"}, {"st": "109.3", "t": "Bring the Gods hither, Agni, born for him who trims the Sacred grass:<br>Thou art our Hotar, meet for praise!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Mitra Varuna"}, {"st": "110.1", "t": "Mitra and Varuna we call to drink the draught of Soma juice,<br>Those born endowed with holy strength."}, {"st": "110.2", "t": "Those who by Law uphold the Law, Lords of the shining light of Law,<br>Mitra I call, and Varuna."}, {"st": "110.3", "t": "Let Varuna be our chief defence, let Mitra guard us with all aids,<br>Both make us rich exceedingly!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Indra"}, {"st": "111.1", "t": "Indra the singers with high praise, Indra reciters with their lauds,<br>Indra the choirs have glorified."}, {"st": "111.2", "t": "Indra is close to his two bays, with chariot ready at his word,<br>Indra the golden, thunder-armed."}, {"st": "111.3", "t": "Help us in battles Indra, in battles where thousand spoils are gained,<br>With awful aids, O awful one!"}, {"st": "111.4", "t": "Indra raised up the son aloft in heaven, that he may see afar:<br>He burst the mountain for the kine."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra-Agni"}, {"st": "112.1", "t": "To Indra and to Agni we bring reverence high and holy hymn,<br>And, craving help, soft words with prayer."}, {"st": "112.2", "t": "For all these holy singers thus implore these twain to succour them,<br>And priests that they may win them strength."}, {"st": "112.3", "t": "Eager to laud you, we with songs invoke you, bearing sacred food,<br>Fain for success in sacrifice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "113.1", "t": "Flow onward, mighty with thy stream, inspiriting the Marut’s Lord,<br>Winning all riches with thy power!"}, {"st": "113.2", "t": "I send thee forth to battle from the press, O Pavamana, strong,<br>Sustainer, looker on the light!"}, {"st": "113.3", "t": "Acknowledged by this song of mine, flow, tawnycoloured, with thy stream:<br>Incite to battle thine ally!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "114.1", "t": "A Red Bull bellowing to the kine, thou goest, causing the heavens and earth to roar and thunder.<br>A shout is heard like Indra’s in the battle: thou flowest on, sending this voice before thee."}, {"st": "114.2", "t": "Swelling with milk, abounding in sweet juices, urging the meathrich plant thou goest onward.<br>Making loud clamour, Soma Pavamana, thou flowest when thou art effused for Indra."}, {"st": "114.3", "t": "So flow thou on inspiriting, for rapture, turning the weapon of the water’s holder!<br>Flow to us wearing thy resplendent colour, effused and eager for the kine. O Soma!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Indra"}, {"st": "115.1", "t": "That we may win us wealth and power we poets verily, call on thee:<br>In war men call on thee, Indra, the hero’s Lord, in the steed’s race-course call on thee"}, {"st": "115.2", "t": "As such, O wonderful, whose hand holds thunder, praised as mighty, Caster of the Stone!<br>Pour on us boldly, Indra, kine and chariot-steeds, ever to be the conqueror’s strength!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "116.1", "t": "To you will I sing Indra’s praise who gives good gifts, as we I we know;<br>The praise of Maghavan who, rich in treasure, aids his singers with wealth thousandfold."}, {"st": "116.2", "t": "As with a hundred hosts, he rushes boldly on, and for the offerer slays his foes.<br>As from a mountain flow the water-brooks, thus flow his gifts who feedeth many a one.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "117.1", "t": "O Thunderer, zealous worshippers gave thee drink this time yesterday:<br>So, Indra, listen here to him who offers lauds: come near unto our dwelling-place!"}, {"st": "117.2", "t": "Lord of bay steeds, fair-helmed, rejoice thee: thee we seek. Here the disposers wait on thee.<br>Thy glories, meet for praise! are highest by the juice, O Indra, lover of the song."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "118.1", "t": "Flow onward with that juice of thine most excellent, that brings delight,<br>Slaying the wicked, dear to Gods!"}, {"st": "118.2", "t": "Killing the foeman and his hate, and daily winning spoil and strength,<br>Gainer art thou of steeds and kine."}, {"st": "118.3", "t": "Red-hued, be blended with the milk that seems to yield its lovely breast,<br>Falcon-like resting in thine home!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "119.1", "t": "As Pashan, Fortune, Bhaga, comes this Soma while they make him pure.<br>He, Lord of all the multitude, hath looked upon the earth and heaven."}, {"st": "119.2", "t": "The dear cows sang in joyful mood together to the gladdening drink.<br>The drops as they are purified, the Soma juices, make the paths."}, {"st": "119.3", "t": "O Pavamana, bring the juice, the mightiest, worthy to be famed,<br>Which the Five Tribes have over them, whereby we may win opulence!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "120.1", "t": "Far-seeing Soma flows, the Steer, the Lord of hymns, the furtherer of days, of mornings, and of heaven.<br>Breath of the rivers, he hath roared into the jars, and with the help of sages entered Indra’s heart."}, {"st": "120.2", "t": "On, with the sages, flows the poet on his way, and guided by the men, hath streamed into the vats.<br>He, showing Trita’s name, hath caused the meath to flow, increasing Vayu’s strength to make him Indra’s friend."}, {"st": "120.3", "t": "He, being purified, hath made the mornings shine, and it is he who gave the rivers room to flow.<br>Making the three-times seven pour out the milky stream, Soma, the cheerer, yields whate’er the heart finds sweet."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Indra"}, {"st": "121.1", "t": "For so thou art the brave man’s friend; a hero, too, art thou, and strong:<br>So may thy heart be won us!"}, {"st": "121.2", "t": "So hath the offering. wealthiest Lord, been paid by all the worshippers.<br>So dwell thou, Indra, even with us!"}, {"st": "121.3", "t": "Be not thou like a slothful priest, O Lord of spoil and strength: rejoice<br>In the pressed Soma blent with milk!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Indra"}, {"st": "122.1", "t": "All sacred songs have magnified Indra expansive as the sea.<br>Best of all warriors borne on cars, the Lord of heroes, Lord of strength."}, {"st": "122.2", "t": "Lord of might, Indra, may we ne’er, strong in thy friendship, be afraid!<br>We glorify with praises thee, the never conquered conqueror."}, {"st": "122.3", "t": "The gifts of Indra from of old, his saving succours never fail,<br>When to his worshippers he gives the boon of booty rich in kine."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "123.1", "t": "These rapid Soma-drops have been poured through the purifying sieve.<br>To bring us all felicities."}, {"st": "123.2", "t": "Dispelling manifold mishap, giving the courser’s progeny,<br>Yea, and the warrior steed’s, success."}, {"st": "123.3", "t": "Bringing prosperity to kine, they pour perpetual strengthening food<br>On us for noble eulogy."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "124.1", "t": "King Pavamana is implored with holy songs, on man’s behalf,<br>To travel through, the realm of air."}, {"st": "124.2", "t": "Pressed for the banquet of the Gods, O Soma, bring us might, and speed,<br>Like beauty for a’brilliant show!"}, {"st": "124.3", "t": "Bring us, O Indu, hundredfold increase of kine, and noble steeds.<br>The gift of fortune for our help!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "125.1", "t": "With sacrifice we seek to thee fair cherisher of manly might<br>In mansons of the lofty heavens."}, {"st": "125.2", "t": "Drink gladdening, crusher of the bold, praiseworthy, with most mighty sway,<br>Destroyer of a hundred forts."}, {"st": "125.3", "t": "Hence riches came to thee, the King, O sapient one: the strong-winged bird,<br>Unwearied, brought thee from the sky."}, {"st": "125.4", "t": "And now, sent forth, he hath attained to mighty power and majesty,<br>Active and ready to assist."}, {"st": "125.5", "t": "That each may see the light, the bird brought us the guard of Law, the friend<br>O fall, the speeder through the air."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "126.1", "t": "For food, flow onward with thy stream, cleansed and made bright by sapient men:<br>Indu, with sheen approach the milk!"}, {"st": "126.2", "t": "While thou art cleansed, song-lover. bring comfort and vigourto the folk,<br>Poured, tawny one! on milk and curds!"}, {"st": "126.3", "t": "Purified for feast of Gods, go thou to Indra’s resting-place,<br>Resplendent, furthered by the strong!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Agni"}, {"st": "127.1", "t": "By Agni Agni is inflamed, Lord of the house, wise, young, who bears<br>Our gifts: the ladle is his mouth."}, {"st": "127.2", "t": "God, Agni, be his sure defence who, lord of sacrificial gifts.<br>Worshippeth thee the messenger."}, {"st": "127.3", "t": "Be gracious, brilliant Godl to him who, rich in sacred gifts, would fain<br>Call Agni to the feast of Gods!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Mitra Varuna"}, {"st": "128.1", "t": "Mitra of holy strength I call, and foe-destroying Varuna,<br>Who perfect prayer with offered oil."}, {"st": "128.2", "t": "By Law, O Mitra, Varuna, Law-strengtheners who cleave to Law,<br>Have ye obtained your lofty power."}, {"st": "128.3", "t": "The Sages, Mitra, Varuna, of wide dominion, mighty ones,<br>Bestow on us effectual strength."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Maruts"}, {"st": "129.1", "t": "So mayst thou verily be seen coming with fearless Indra: both<br>Of equal splendour, bringing bliss!"}, {"st": "129.2", "t": "Thereafter they, as is their wont, resumed the state of new-born babes,<br>Taking their sacrificial name."}, {"st": "129.3", "t": "Thou, Indra, with the rapid Gods who shatter even what is firm,<br>Even in the cave didst find the cows."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Indra-Agni"}, {"st": "130.1", "t": "I call the twain whose deed wrought here hath all been famed in ancient time:<br>Indra and Agni harm us not!"}, {"st": "130.2", "t": "The strong, the scatterers of the foe, Indra and Agni we invoke:<br>May they be kind to one like me:"}, {"st": "130.3", "t": "Ye slay our Arya foes, O Lords of heroes, slay our Dasa foes:<br>Ye drive all enemies away."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "131.1", "t": "The living drops of Soma juice pour, as they flow the gladdening drink,<br>Intelligent drops above the station of the sea, exhilarating, dropping meath."}, {"st": "131.2", "t": "May Pavamana, King and God, speed with his wave over the sea the lofty rite!<br>Do thou by Mitra’s and by Varuna’s decree flow furthering the lofty rite:"}, {"st": "131.3", "t": "Far-seeing, lovely, guided by the men, the God whose habitation is the sea!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "132.1", "t": "Three are the voices that the car-steed utters: he speaks the lore of prayer, the thought of Order.<br>To the cows’ master come the cows inquiring: the hymns with eager longing come to Soma."}, {"st": "132.2", "t": "To Soma come the cows, the milch-kine longing, to Soma sages with their hymns inquiring.<br>Soma, effused, is purified and lauded: our hymns and Trishtup songs unite in Soma."}, {"st": "132.3", "t": "Thus, Soma, as we pour thee into vessels, while thou art purified, flow for our welfare!<br>Pass into Indra. with great joy and rapture: make the voice swell, and generate abundance!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Indra"}, {"st": "133.1", "t": "O Indra, if a hundred heavens and if a hundred earths were thine, — <br>No, not a hundred suns could match thee at thy birth, not both the worlds, O Thunderer."}, {"st": "133.2", "t": "Thou, hero, hast performed thy hero deeds with might, yea, all with strength, O strongest one.<br>Maghavan, help us to a stable full of kine, O Thunderer, with wondrous aids!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Indra"}, {"st": "134.1", "t": "We compass thee like water, we whose grass is trimmed and Soma pressed.<br>Here where the filter pours its stream, thy worshippers round thee, O Vritra-slayer, sit."}, {"st": "134.2", "t": "Men, Vasu! by the Soma with lauds call thee to the foremost place.<br>When cometh he athirst unto the juice as home, O Indra, like a bellowing bull?"}, {"st": "134.3", "t": "O valiant hero, boldly win thousandfold spoil with Kanva’s sons!<br>O active Maghavan, with eager prayer we crave the yellowhued with store of kine."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "135.1", "t": "With Plenty for his true ally the active man will gain the spoil.<br>Your Indra, much-invoked, I bend with song, as bends a wright his wheel of solid wood."}, {"st": "135.2", "t": "They who bestow great riches love not paltry praise: wealth comes not to the niggard churl.<br>Light is the task to give, O Maghavan, to one like me on the decisive day."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "136.1", "t": "Three several words are uttered: kine are lowing cows. who give the milk:<br>The tawny-hued goes bellowing on."}, {"st": "136.2", "t": "The young and sacred mothers of the holy rite have uttered praise,<br>Embellishing the Child of Heaven."}, {"st": "136.3", "t": "From every side, O Soma, for our profit, pour thou forth four seas.<br>Filled full of riches thousandfold!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "137.1", "t": "The Somas, very rich in sweets, for which the sieve is distined,<br>flow Effused, the source of Indra’s joy: may you strong juices reach the Gods!"}, {"st": "137.2", "t": "Indu flows on for Indra’s sake,-thus have the deities declared.<br>The Lord of Speech exerts himself, controller of all power and might."}, {"st": "137.3", "t": "Inciter of the voice of song, with thousand streams the ocean flows.<br>Even Soma, Lord of opulence, the friend of Indra, day by day."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "138.1", "t": "SPREAD is thy cleansing filter, Brahmanaspati: as prince thou enterest its limbs from every side.<br>The raw; whose mass bath not been heated. gains not this: they only which are dressed, which bear, attain to it."}, {"st": "138.2", "t": "High in the seat of heaven is placed the scorcher’s sieve: its, threads are standing separate, glittering with light.<br>The swift ones favour him who purifieth this: with brilliancy they mount up to the height of heaven."}, {"st": "138.3", "t": "The foremost spotted Steer bath made the Mornings shine: he bellows, fain for war, among created things.<br>By his high wisdom have the mighty Sages wrought: the Fathers who behold mankind laid down the germ."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Agni"}, {"st": "139.1", "t": "Sing forth to him, the holy, most munificent, sublime with his refulgent glow,<br>To Agni, ye Upastutas"}, {"st": "139.2", "t": "Worshipped with gifts, enkindled, splendid, Maghavan shall win<br>himself heroic fame:<br>And will not his more plentiful benevolence come to us with abundant strength?"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Indra"}, {"st": "140.1", "t": "We sing this strong and wild delight of thine which conquers in the fray,<br>Which, Caster of the Stone! gives room and shines like gold."}, {"st": "140.2", "t": "Wherewith thou foundest shining lights for Ayu and for Manu’s sake:<br>Now joying in this sacred grass thou beamest forth.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [109, 108]]}, {"st": "140.3", "t": "This day too singers of the hymn praise, as of old, this might of thine:<br>Win thou the waters every day, thralls of the strong!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Indra"}, {"st": "141.1", "t": "O Indra, hear Tirschi’s call, the call of him who serveth thee.<br>Satisfy him with wealth of kine and valient offspring! Great art thou."}, {"st": "141.2", "t": "For he, O Indra, hath produced for thee the newest gladdening song,<br>A hymn that springs from careful drop thought, ancient and full of sacred truth."}, {"st": "141.3", "t": "That Indra will we laud whom songs and hymns of praise have magnified.<br>Striving to win, we celebrate his many deeds of hero might."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "142.1", "t": "Fleet as swift steeds thy cows celestial have been poured, O Pavamana, with the milk into the vat.<br>Sages who make thee bright, O friend whom Rishis love, have shed continuous streams from out the realm of air."}, {"st": "142.2", "t": "The beams of Pavamana, sent from earth and heaven his ensigns who is ever stedfast, travel round.<br>When on the sieve the golden-hued is cleansed he rests within the jars as one who seats him in his place."}, {"st": "142.3", "t": "O thou who seest all things, sovran as thou art and passing strong, thy rays encompass every form.<br>Pervading with thy natural powers thou flowest on, and as the whole world’s Lord, O Soma, thou art King."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "143.1", "t": "From heaven hath Pavamana, made, as ‘twere, the marvellous thunder, and<br>The lofty light of all mankind."}, {"st": "143.2", "t": "The gladdening and auspicious juice of thee, O Pavamana, King!<br>Flows o’cr the woollen straining-cloth."}, {"st": "143.3", "t": "Thy juice, O Pavamana, sends its rays abroad like splendid skill,<br>Like lustre, all heaven’s light, to see.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "144.1", "t": "Impetuous, bright, have they come forth, unwearied in their speed, like bulls,<br>Driving the black skin far away."}, {"st": "144.2", "t": "May we attain the bridge of bliss, leaving the bridge of woe behind:<br>The riteless Dasa may we quell!"}, {"st": "144.3", "t": "The mighty Pavamana’s roar is heard as ‘twere the rush of rain<br>The lightning-Rashes move in heaven."}, {"st": "144.4", "t": "Indu, pour out abundant food with store of cattle and of gold,<br>Of heroes, Soma! and of steeds!"}, {"st": "144.5", "t": "Flow onward, dear to all mankind fi full the mighty heaven and earth,<br>As Dawn, as Surya with his beams"}, {"st": "144.6", "t": "On every side, O Soma, flow round us with thy protecting stream,<br>As Rasa flows around the world!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "145.1", "t": "Flow on, O thou of lofty thought, flow swift in thy beloved form,<br>Saying, I go where dwell the Gods."}, {"st": "145.2", "t": "Preparing what is unprepared, and bringing store of food to man,<br>Make thou the rain descend from heaven"}, {"st": "145.3", "t": "Even here is he who, swift of course, hath with the river’s wave Rowed down.<br>From heaven upon the straining cloth."}, {"st": "145.4", "t": "With might. producing glare, the juice enters the purifying sieve,<br>Far-seeing, sending forth its light."}, {"st": "145.5", "t": "Inviting him from far away, and even from near at hand, the juice<br>For Indra is poured forth as meath."}, {"st": "145.6", "t": "In union they have sung the hymn: with stones they urge the golden-hued,<br>Indu for Indra, for his drink."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "146.1", "t": "The glittering maids send Sdra forth, the glorious sisters, closeallied,<br>Send Indu forth, their mighty Lord."}, {"st": "146.2", "t": "Pervade, O Pavamana, all our treasures with repeated light,<br>Pressed out, O God thyself, for Gods!"}, {"st": "146.3", "t": "Pour on us, Pavamana! rain, as service and fair praise for Gods:<br>Pour forth unceasingly for food!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Agni"}, {"st": "147.1", "t": "The watchful guardian of the people hath been born, Agni, the very strong, for fresh prosperity.<br>With oil upon his face. with high heaven-touching flame, he shineth splendidly, pure, for the Bharatas."}, {"st": "147.2", "t": "O Agni, the Angirasas discovered thee what time thou layest hidden, fleeing back from wood to wood.<br>Thou by attrition art produced as conquering might, and men, O Angiras, call thee the Son of Strength."}, {"st": "147.3", "t": "The men enkindle Agni in his threefold seat, ensign of sacrifice, the earliest bousehold-priest.<br>With Indra and the Gods together on the grass let the wise priest sit to complete the sacrifice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Mitra-Varuna"}, {"st": "148.1", "t": "This Soma hath been pressed for you, Low-strengtheners, Mitra, Varuna!<br>List, list ye here to this may call!"}, {"st": "148.2", "t": "Both Kings who never injure aught have come to their sublimest home,<br>The thousand-pillared, firmly based."}, {"st": "148.3", "t": "Worshipped with fat libation. Lords of gifts, Adityas, sovran Kings,<br>They wait on him whose life is true."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Indra"}, {"st": "149.1", "t": "Armed with the bones of dead Dadhyach, Indra with unresisted. might<br>The nine-and-ninety Vritras slew."}, {"st": "149.2", "t": "He, searching for the horse’s head that in the mountains lay concealed,<br>Found it in Saryandvdn lake."}, {"st": "149.3", "t": "Then straight they recognized the mystic name of the creative Steer.<br>There in the mansion of the Moon."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra Agni"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. As rain from out the cloud, for you, Indra and Agni, from my thought<br>This noblest praise hath been produced.<br>2. Indra and Agni, listen to the singer’s call: accept his songs.<br>Fulfil, ye mighty Lords, his prayers!<br>3. Give us not up to indigence, ye heroes, Indra, Agni, nor<br>To Slander and reproach of men!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "151.1", "t": "Gold-Hued! as one who giveth strength flow on for Gods to drink, a draught<br>For Vayu and the Marut host!"}, {"st": "151.2", "t": "The Steer shines brightly with the Gods, dear Sage in his appointed home.<br>Even Pavamana unbeguiled."}, {"st": "151.3", "t": "O Pavamana, sent by prayer, roaring about thy dwelling-place,<br>Ascend to Vayu as Law bids!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "152.1", "t": "O Soma, Indu, every day thy friendship hath been my delight.<br>Many fiends follow me; help me, thou tawny-hued: pass on beyond these barriers!"}, {"st": "152.2", "t": "Close to thy bosom am I. Soma, day and night draining the milk, O golden hued.<br>Surya himself refulgent with his glow have we, as birds, o’ertaken in his course."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "153.1", "t": "Active, while being purified, he hath assailed all enemies: They deck the Sage with holy hymns."}, {"st": "153.2", "t": "The Red hath mounted to his shrine; strong Indra hath approached the juice:<br>In his firm dwelling let him rest!"}, {"st": "153.3", "t": "O Indu, Soma, send us now great opulence from every side:<br>Pour on us treasures thousandfold!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "154.1", "t": "Drink Soma, Indra Lord of bays! and let it cheer thee: the stone, like a well-guided courser,<br>Directed by the presser’s arms bath pressed it."}, {"st": "154.2", "t": "So let the draught of joy, thy dear companion, by which, O Lord of bays, thou slayest Vritras,<br>Delight thee, Indra, Lord of princely treasures!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "154.3", "t": "Mark closely, Maghavan, the word I utter, this eulogy recited by Vasislitha:<br>Accept the prayers I offer at thy banquet!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "155.1", "t": "Heroes of one accord brought forth and formed for kingship<br>Indra who wins the victory in all encounters,<br>For power, in firmness, in the field, the great destroyer, fierce and exceeding strong, stalwart and full of vigour."}, {"st": "155.2", "t": "The holy sages form a ring, to view and sing unto the Ram.<br>Inciters, very brilliant, from all deceit, are with your chariters nigh to hear."}, {"st": "155.3", "t": "Bards joined in song to Indra so that he might drink the Soma juice.<br>The Lord of light, that he whose laws stand fast might aid with power and with the help he gives."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Indra"}, {"st": "156.1", "t": "He who as sovran Lord of men moves with his chariots unrestrained,<br>The Vritra-slayer, conqueror of all fighting hosts, preeminent, is praised in song.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [129, 128]]}, {"st": "156.2", "t": "Honour that Indra, Puruhanman! for his aid, him in whose hand of old the fair<br>Sustaining bolt of thunder, mighty like the God, like Surya, was deposited!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "157.1", "t": "The Sage of heaven whose heart is wise, when laid between both hands, with roars,<br>Gives us delightful powers of life."}, {"st": "157.2", "t": "He, the bright son, when born, illumed his parents who had sprung to life,<br>Great Son, great strengtheners of Law."}, {"st": "157.3", "t": "On, onward to a glorious home, free from all guile and dear to. men,<br>Flow with enjoyment to our praise!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "158.1", "t": "For, verily, Pavamana, thou, divine! endued with brightest splendour, calling all<br>Creatures to immortality."}, {"st": "158.4", "t": "With whom Dadhyach Navagva opened fastened doors, by whom the sages gained their wish,<br>By whom they won the fame of lovely Amrita in the felicity of Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "159.1", "t": "Soma, while filtered, with his wave flows through the long wool of the sheep,<br>Roaring, while purified, before the voice of song."}, {"st": "159.2", "t": "With prayers they cleanse the mighty steed, sporting in wood, above the fleece:<br>Our hymns, intoned, have praised him of the triple height."}, {"st": "159.3", "t": "He hath been hastened to the jars, bountiful, like an eager horse,<br>And, lifting up his voice, while filtered, glided on."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "160.1", "t": "Father of holy hymns, Soma flows onward, the father of the earth, father of heaven.<br>Father of Agni, Surya’s generator, the father who begat Indra and Vishnu."}, {"st": "160.2", "t": "Brahman of Gods, the leader of the poets, Rishi of sages, chief of savage creatures,<br>Falcon amid the vultures, axe of forests, over the cleansing sieve goes Soma singing."}, {"st": "160.3", "t": "He, Soma Pavamana, like a river, hath stirred the wave of voice, our songs and praises<br>Beholding these inferior powers, the hero, well knowing, takes his stand among the cattle."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Agni"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Hither, for powerful kinship, I call Agni, him who prospers you,<br>Most frequent at our solemn rites.<br>2. That through this famed one’s power he may stand by us, even as Tvasbtar comes<br>Unto the forms that must be shaped.<br>3. This Agni is the Lord supreme above all glories’ mid the Gods:<br>May he come nigh to us with strength."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 21 · Indra"}, {"st": "162.1", "t": "This poured libation, Indra drink, immortal, gladdening, excellent!<br>Streams of the bright have flowed to thee here at the seat of holy Law."}, {"st": "162.2", "t": "When, Indra, thou dost guide thy bays, there is no better charioteer:<br>None hath surpassed thee in thy might, none with good steeds o’ertaken thee."}, {"st": "162.3", "t": "Sing glory now to Indra, say to him your solemn eulogies!<br>The drops poured forth have made him glad: pay reverence to his noblest might!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Indra"}, {"st": "163.1", "t": "Indra, be pleased: drive forward, hero, striker of thy bays!<br>Fair, like a sage, delighting in the meath, drink of the juice for rapturous joy."}, {"st": "163.2", "t": "O Indra, fill thy belly anew with meath that seems to flow from heaven.<br>The sweet-voiced raptures of this juice have come, as ‘twere to heaven. to thee."}, {"st": "163.3", "t": "Indra, victorious, Mitra-like, smote, like a Yati, Vritra dead.<br>As Bhrigu quelled his foes, he cleft Vala in Soma’s rapturous joy."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "164.1", "t": "Winner of gold and gear and cattle flow thou on, set as impregner, Indu! ‘mid the worlds of life!<br>Rich in brave men art thou, Soma, who winnest all: these holy singers wait upon thee with song."}, {"st": "164.2", "t": "O Soma, thou beholdest men from every side: O Pavamana, Steer, thou wanderest through these.<br>Pour out upon us wealth in treasure and in gold: may we have strength to live among the things that be!"}, {"st": "164.3", "t": "Thou passest to these worlds as sovran Lord thereof, O Indu, harnessing thy tawny well-winged mares.<br>May they pour forth for thee milk and oil rich in sweets:<br>O Soma, let the folk abide in thy decree!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "165.1", "t": "The streams of Pavamana, thine, finder of all I have been ettused,<br>Even as Surya’s rays of light."}, {"st": "165.2", "t": "Making the light that shines from heaven thou flowest on to every form,<br>Soma, thou swellest like a sea."}, {"st": "165.3", "t": "Shown forth thou sendest out thy voice, O Pavamana, with a roar.<br>Like Surya, God, as Law commands."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "166.1", "t": "Hitherward have the Somas streamed, the drops while they are purified:<br>When blent, in waters they are raised."}, {"st": "166.2", "t": "The milk hath run to meet them like floods rushing down a precipice:<br>They come to Indra, being cleansed."}, {"st": "166.3", "t": "O Soma Pavamana, thou flowest as Indra’s gladdener: The men have seized and lead thee forth."}, {"st": "166.4", "t": "Thou, Indu, when, expressed by stones, thou runnest to the filter, art<br>Ready for Indra’s high decree."}, {"st": "166.5", "t": "Victorious, to be hailed with joy, O Soma, flow delighting men,<br>As the supporter of mankind!"}, {"st": "166.6", "t": "Flow on, best Vritra-slayer; flow meet to be hailed with joyful lauds,<br>pure, purifying, wonderful"}, {"st": "166.7", "t": "Pure, purifying, is he called, Soma effused and full of sweets,<br>Slayer of sinners, dear to Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "167.1", "t": "The Sage hath robed him in the sheep’s wool for the banquet of the Gods,<br>Subduing all our enemies."}, {"st": "167.2", "t": "For he, as Pavamana, sends thousandfold riches in the shape<br>Of cattle to the worshippers."}, {"st": "167.3", "t": "Thou graspest all things with thy mind, and purifiest thee with thoughts:<br>As such, O Soma, find us fame!"}, {"st": "167.4", "t": "Pour on us lofty glory, send sure riches to our liberal lords:<br>Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"st": "167.5", "t": "As thou art cleansed, O wondrous steed, O Soma, thou hast entered, like<br>A pious king, into the songs,"}, {"st": "167.6", "t": "He, Soma, like a courser in the floods invincible, made bright<br>With hands, is resting in the press."}, {"st": "167.7", "t": "Disporting, like a liberal chief, thou goest. Soma to the sieve,<br>Lending the laud heroic strength."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "168.1", "t": "Pour on us with thy juice all kinds of corn, each sort of nourishment!<br>And, Soma, all felicities!"}, {"st": "168.2", "t": "As thine, O Indu, is the praise, and thine what springeth from, the juice,<br>Seat thee on the dear sacred grass!"}, {"st": "168.3", "t": "And, finding for us steeds and kine, O Soma, with thy juice flow on<br>Through days that fly most rapidly!"}, {"st": "168.4", "t": "As one who conquers, ne’er subdued, attacks and slays the enemy,<br>Thus, vanquisher of thousands! flow!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "169.1", "t": "Thou, Indu, with thy streams that drop sweet juices, which were poured for help,<br>Hast settled in the cleansing sieve."}, {"st": "169.2", "t": "So flow thou onward through the fleece, for Indra flow to be his drink,<br>Seating thee in the shrine of Law!"}, {"st": "169.3", "t": "As giving room and freedom, as most sweet, pour butter forth and milk,<br>O Soma, for the Angirasas!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Agni"}, {"st": "170.1", "t": "Thy glories are, like lightnings from the rainy cloud, visible, Agni, like the comings of the Dawns,<br>When, loosed to wander over plants and forest trees, thou crammest by thyself thy food into thy mouth."}, {"st": "170.2", "t": "When, sped and urged by wind, thou spreadest thee abroad, soon piercing through thy food according to thy will,<br>The hosts, who ne’er decayest, eager to consume, like men on chariots, Agni! strive on every side."}, {"st": "170.3", "t": "Agni, the Hotar-priest who fills the assembly full, waker of wisdom, chief controller of the thought-<br>Thee, yea, none other than thyself, doth man elect priest of the holy offering, great and small, alike."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Mitra-Varuna"}, {"st": "171.1", "t": "Even far and wide, O Varuna and Mitra, doth your help extend:<br>May I obtain your kind good-will!"}, {"st": "171.2", "t": "True Gods, may we completely gain food and a dwelling place from you:<br>Ye Mitras, may we be your own!"}, {"st": "171.3", "t": "Guard us, ye Mitras, with your guards, save us, ye skilled to save: may we<br>Subdue the Dasyus by ourselves!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Arising in thy might, thy jaws thou shookest Indra, having drunk<br>The Soma which the press had shed.<br>2. Indra, both world gave place to thee as thou wast fighting, when thou wast<br>The slayer of the Dasyu hosts.<br>3. From Indra, have I measured out a song eight-footed with nine parts,<br>Delicate, strengthening the Law."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Indra-Agni"}, {"st": "173.1", "t": "Indra and Agni, these our songs of praise have sounded forth to you:<br>Ye who bring blessings! drink the juice"}, {"st": "173.2", "t": "Come, Indra, Agni, with those teams, desired of many, which ye have,<br>O heroes, for the worshipper"}, {"st": "173.3", "t": "With those to his libation poured, ye heroes, Indra, Agni, come:<br>Come ye to drink the Soma-juice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "174.1", "t": "Soma, flow on exceeding bright with loud roar to the reservoirs,<br>Resting in wooden vats thy home!"}, {"st": "174.2", "t": "Let water winning Somas flow to Indra, Vayu, Varuna,<br>To Vishnu and Marut host!"}, {"st": "174.3", "t": "Soma, bestowing food upon our progeny, from every side<br>Pour on us riches thousandfold."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "175.1", "t": "Pressed out by pressers Soma goes over the fleecy backs of sheep,<br>Goes even as with a mare in tawny-coloured stream, goes in a sweetly-sounding stream."}, {"st": "175.2", "t": "Down to the water Soma, rich in kine, bath flowed with cows, with cows that have been milked.<br>They have approached the mixing-vessels as a sea: the cheerer streams for the carouse."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "176.1", "t": "O Purifying Soma, bring to us the wondrous treasure, meet.<br>For lauds, that is in earth and heaven!"}, {"st": "176.2", "t": "Cleansing the lives of men, thou, Steer, bellowing on the sacred grass,<br>Gold-hued, hast settled in thy home."}, {"st": "176.3", "t": "For ye twain, Indra, Soma, are Lords of heaven’s light, Lords of the kine:<br>Prosper, as mighty ones, our prayers"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "177.1", "t": "By men hath Indra been advanced, the Vritra-sIayer, to joy and strength.<br>Him only we invoke for help in battles whether great or small be he our aid in deeds or might!"}, {"st": "177.2", "t": "For, hero, thou art like a host, art giver of abundant spoil.<br>Strengthening e’en the feeble, thou aidest the sacrificer, thou givest great wealth to him who pours."}, {"st": "177.3", "t": "When war and battles are on foot, booty is offered to the bold.<br>Yoke thou thy wildly-rushing bays! Whom wilt thou slay, and whom enrich? Do thou, O Indra, make us rich!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Indra"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. The juice of Soma thus diffused, sweet to the taste, the bright cows drink,<br>Who travelling in splendour close to mighty Indra’s side rejoice, good in their own supremacy.<br>2. Craving his touch the dappled kine mingle the Soma with their milk.<br>The milch-kine dear to Indra send forth his death dealing thunder-bolt, good in their own supremacy.<br>3. With veneration, passing wise, they honour his victorious might.<br>They follow close his many laws to win them due preeminence, good in their own supremacy."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "179.1", "t": "Strong, mountain-born, the stalk hath been pressed in the streams for rapturous joy.<br>Hawk-like he settles in his home."}, {"st": "179.2", "t": "Fair is the juice beloved of Gods, washed in the waters, pressed by men:<br>The milch kine sweeten it with milk"}, {"st": "179.3", "t": "Then, like a steed, have they adorned the inciter for eternal life,<br>The meath’s juice at the festival."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "180.1", "t": "Make high and splendid glory shine hitherward, Lord of food, God, on the friend of Gods<br>Unclose the cask of middle air"}, {"st": "180.2", "t": "Roll onward from the press, O mighty one, effused, as kings, supporter of the tribes<br>Pour on us rain from heaven, send us the water’s flow, urging our thoughts to win the spoil!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "181.1", "t": "Breath of the mighty Dames, the Child, speeding the plan of sacrifice,<br>Surpasses all things that are dear, yea, from of old."}, {"st": "181.2", "t": "The place that is concealed hath gained a share of Trita’s pressing-stones,<br>By the seven laws of sacrifice, even that dear place."}, {"st": "181.3", "t": "He hath sent forth unto the heights the three, in stream, as Trita’s wealth:<br>He who is passing wise measures his pathways out."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "182.1", "t": "Flow to the filter with thy stream, effused, to win us spoil and wealth,<br>Soma exceeding rich in meath for Indra, Vishnu, and the Gods"}, {"st": "182.2", "t": "The hymns that know not guile, caress thee, golden-coloured, in the sieve.<br>As mothers, Pavamana, lick the new-born calf, as Law commands."}, {"st": "182.3", "t": "Lord of great sway, thou liftest thee above the heavens, above the earth.<br>Thou, of Pavamana, hast assumed thy coat of mail with majesty."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "183.1", "t": "Strong Indu, bathed in milk, flows on for Indra, Soma exciting strength, for his carousal.<br>He quells malignity and slays the demons, King of the homestead, he who gives us comfort."}, {"st": "183.2", "t": "Then in a stream he flows, milked out with press-stones, mingled with sweetness, through the fleecy filter — <br>Indu rejoicing in the love of Indra, the God who gladdens for the God’s enjoyment."}, {"st": "183.3", "t": "He flows, as he is cleansed, to sacred duties, a God bedewing Gods with his own juices.<br>Indu hath, clothed in powers that suit the season, on the raised fleece engaged the ten swift fingers."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 21 · Agni"}, {"st": "184.1", "t": "O Agni, God, we kindle thee, refulgent, wasting not away,<br>That this more glorious fuel may send forth for thee its shine to heaven. Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"st": "184.2", "t": "To thee the splendid, Lord of light! bright! wondrous! prince of men! is brought.<br>Oblation with the holy verse, O Agni, bearer of our gifts! Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"st": "184.3", "t": "Thou heatest both the ladles in thy mouth, O brilliant prince of men!<br>So fill us also in our hymns abundantly, thou Lord of Strength. Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 22 · Indra"}, {"st": "185.1", "t": "Sing ye a psalm to Indra; sing a great song to the lofty Sage,<br>To him who maketh prayer, inspired, who loveth laud."}, {"st": "185.2", "t": "Thou, Indra, art the conqueror: thou gavest splendour to the Sun.<br>Maker of all things, thou art mighty and All-God."}, {"st": "185.3", "t": "Radiant with light thou wentest to the sky, the luminous realm of -heaven.<br>The Gods, O Indra, strove to win thy friendly love."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 23 · Indra"}, {"st": "186.1", "t": "This Soma hath been pressed for thee, O Indra, bold one, mightiest, come!<br>May Indra vigour fill thee full, as Surya fills mid-air with rays"}, {"st": "186.2", "t": "Slayer of Vritra, mount thy car! The bay steeds have been yoked by prayer.<br>May, with its voice, the pressing-stone draw thine attention hitherward!"}, {"st": "186.3", "t": "His pair of tawny coursers bring Indra, resistless in his might.<br>Hither to Rishis’ songs of praise and sacrifice performed by men."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "187.1", "t": "Light of the sacrifice, he pours delicious meath, most wealthy, father and begetter of the Gods.<br>He, gladdening, best of cheerers, juice that Indra loves, enriches with mysterious treasure earth and heaven.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "187.2", "t": "The Lord of heaven, the vigorous and far-seeing one, flowsshouting to the beaker with his thousand streams.<br>Coloured like gold he rests in seats where Mitra dwells, the Steer made beautiful by rivers and by sheep."}, {"st": "187.3", "t": "As Pavamana thou flowest before the streams: thou goest on, before the hymn, before the kine.<br>Thou sharest mighty booty in the van of war Soma, well-armed, thou art pressed out by men who press."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "188.1", "t": "Through our desire of heroes, kine, and horses, vigorous Somadrops,<br>Brilliant and swift, have been effused."}, {"st": "188.2", "t": "They, beautified by holy men and purified in both the hands,<br>Are flowing through the fleecy cloth."}, {"st": "188.3", "t": "These Soma juices shall pour forth all treasures for the worshipper,<br>From heaven and earth and firmament."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "189.1", "t": "Flow, Soma, Indu, dear to Gods, swift through the purifying sieve,<br>And enter Indra in thy strength", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "189.2", "t": "As mighty food speed hitherward, Indu, as a most splendid steer:<br>Sit in thy place as one with power"}, {"st": "189.3", "t": "The well-loved meath was made to flow, the stream of the creative juice:<br>The Sage drew waters to himself."}, {"st": "189.4", "t": "The mighty waters, yea, the floods accompany thee mighty one,<br>When thou wilt clothe thee with the milk."}, {"st": "189.5", "t": "The lake is brightened in the floods. Soma, our friend, heaven’s prop and stay,<br>Falls on the purifying cloth."}, {"st": "189.6", "t": "The tawny Bull hath bellowed. fair as mighty Mitra to behold<br>He gleams and flashes with the Sun."}, {"st": "189.7", "t": "Songs, Indra, active in their might, are beautified for thee, wherewith<br>Thou deckest thee for rapturous joy."}, {"st": "189.8", "t": "To thee who givest ample room we pray, to win the wild delight,<br>That Thou mayst have exalted praise,"}, {"st": "189.9", "t": "Winner of kine Indu, art thou, winner of heroes, steeds, and spoil:<br>Primeval soul of sacrifice."}, {"st": "189.10", "t": "Pour on us, Indu! Indra-strength with a full stream of sweetness, like<br>Parianya, sender of the rain!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "190.1", "t": "O Soma Pavamana, be victorious, win us high renown; And make us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.2", "t": "Win thou the light, win heavenly light, and, Soma, all felicities;<br>And make us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.3", "t": "Win skilful strength and mental power! O Soma, drive away our foes;<br>And make us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.4", "t": "Ye purifiers, purify Soma for Indra, for his drink;<br>Make thou us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.5", "t": "Give us our portion in the Sun through thine own mental power and aids;<br>And make us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.6", "t": "Through thine own mental power and aids long may we look upon the Sun:<br>Make thou us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.7", "t": "Well-weaponed Soma, pour to us a stream of riches doubly great;<br>And make us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.8", "t": "As one victorious unsubdued in battle, pour forth wealth to us:<br>And make us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.9", "t": "With offerings, Pavamana! men have strengthened thee as Law commands:<br>Make thou us better than we are!"}, {"st": "190.10", "t": "O Indu, bring us wealth in steeds brilliant and quickening all life;<br>And make us better than we are!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "191.1", "t": "Swift runs this giver of delight, even the stream of flowing juice:<br>Swift runs this giver of delight."}, {"st": "191.2", "t": "The Morning knows all precious things, the Goddess knows her grace to man:<br>Swift runs this giver of delight."}, {"st": "191.3", "t": "We have accepted thousands from Dhvasra’s and Purusbanti’s hands:<br>Swift runs this giver of delight."}, {"st": "191.4", "t": "From whom we have accepted thus thousands and three-times ten besides:<br>Swift runs this giver of delight."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "192.1", "t": "Forth with his stream who gladdens best these Soma juices have been poured,<br>Lauded with songs for mighty strength."}, {"st": "192.2", "t": "Thou flowest to enjoy the milk, and bringest valour, being, cleansed:<br>Winning the spoil flow hitherward"}, {"st": "192.3", "t": "And, hymned by Jamadagni, let all nourishment that kine supply,<br>And general praises, flow to us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Agni"}, {"st": "193.1", "t": "For Jatavedas, worthy of our praise, will we frame with our mind this eulogy as ‘twere a car.<br>For good, in his assembly, is this care of ours. Let us not, in thy friendship, Agni, suffer harm!"}, {"st": "193.2", "t": "We will bring fuel and prepare our sacred gifts, reminding thee at each successive holy time.<br>Fulfil our thoughts that we may lengthen out our lives<br>Let us not, in thy friendship, Agni, suffer harm!"}, {"st": "193.3", "t": "May we have power to kindle thee! Fulfil our prayers in thee the Gods eat the presented sacrifice.<br>Bring hither the Adityas, for we long for them! Let us not, in thy friendship, Agni, suffer harm!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Mitra, Varuna, Aryaman"}, {"st": "194.1", "t": "Soon as the Sun hath risen I sing to you, to Mitra, Varuna,<br>And Aryaman who slays the foe."}, {"st": "194.2", "t": "With wealth of gold may this my song bring unmolested might; may this,<br>Sages! obtain the sacrifice!"}, {"st": "194.3", "t": "May we be thine, God Varuna, and with our princes, Mitra, thine:<br>May we gain food and heavenly light!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra"}, {"st": "195.1", "t": "Drive all our enemies away, smite down the foes who press around,<br>And bring the wealth for which we long:"}, {"st": "195.2", "t": "Of which the world shall know forthwith as given by thee abundantly:<br>Bring us the wealth for which we long:"}, {"st": "195.3", "t": "O Indra, that which is concealed in strong firm place precipito us:<br>Bring us the wealth for which we long!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Indra-Agni"}, {"st": "196.1", "t": "Yea, ye are priests of sacrifice, winners in war and holy works<br>Indra and Agni, mark this well!"}, {"st": "196.2", "t": "Bountiful, riders on the car, slayers of Vritra unsubdued, Indra and Agni, mark this well!"}, {"st": "196.3", "t": "The men with pressing-stones have pressed this meath of yours which gives delight:<br>Indra and Agni, mark this well!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "197.1", "t": "For Indra girt by Maruts, flow, thou Indu, very rich in meath,<br>To seat thee in the place of song!"}, {"st": "197.2", "t": "Sage: who know the lore of speech deck thee, the strong sustainer, well:<br>Men make thee bright and beautiful."}, {"st": "197.3", "t": "Let Mitra, Varuna, Aryaman drink Pavamana’s juice, yea, thine.<br>Sage! let the Maruts drink thereof."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "198.1", "t": "Deft-handed! thou when purified liftest thy voice amid the sea.<br>Thou, Pavamana makest riches flow to us, yellow, abundant, much-desired."}, {"st": "198.2", "t": "Made pure, as Pavamana, in the sheep’s long wool, the Steer bath bellowed in the vat.<br>Thou flowest, Soma Pavamana! balmed with ‘milk unto the meeting-place of Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "199.1", "t": "Him here, the offspring of the sea, the ten swift fingers beautify:<br>With the Adityas is he seen."}, {"st": "199.2", "t": "With Indra and with Vayu he, effused, flows onward with the beams<br>Of Surya to the cleansing sieve."}, {"st": "199.3", "t": "Flow rich in sweets and lovely for our Bhaga, Vayu, Pushan, fair<br>For Mitra and for Varuna!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "200.1", "t": "With Indra splendid feasts be ours, rich in all strengthening things, wherewith,<br>Wealthy in food, we may rejoice!"}, {"st": "200.2", "t": "Like thee, thyself, for singers yoked, thou movest, as it were besought,<br>Bold one, the axle of the car,"}, {"st": "200.3", "t": "That, Satakratu, thou, to serve and please thy praisers, as it were,<br>Stirrest the axle with thy strength."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Indra"}, {"st": "201.1", "t": "As a good cow to him who milks, we call the doer of good deeds,<br>To our assistance day by day."}, {"st": "201.2", "t": "Come thou to our libations, drink of Soma, Soma-drinker! yea,<br>The rich one’s rapture giveth kine."}, {"st": "201.3", "t": "So may we be acquainted with thine innermost benevolence:<br>Neglect us not; come hitherward!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Indra"}, {"st": "202.1", "t": "As, like the Morning, thou has filled, O Indra, both the earth and heaven,<br>So as the mighty one, great King of all the mighty race of men, the Goddess mother brought thee forth, the blessed mother gave thee life."}, {"st": "202.2", "t": "Thou bearest in thine hand a lance like a long hook, great counsellor.<br>As with his foremost foot a goat, draw down the branch O Maghavan. The Goddess mother brought thee forth, the blessed mother gave thee life."}, {"st": "202.3", "t": "Relax that mortal’s stubborn strength whose heart is bent on wickedness.<br>Trample him down beneath thy feet who watches for and aims at us. The Goddess mother brought thee forth, the blessed mother gave thee life."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "203.1", "t": "Soma, the dweller on the hills, effused, hath flowed into the sieve.<br>All-bounteous art thou in carouse."}, {"st": "203.2", "t": "Thou art a holy bard, a Sage; the meath offspring of thy sap:<br>All bounteous art thou in carouse."}, {"st": "203.3", "t": "All-deities of one accord have come that they may drink of thee:<br>All-bounteous art thou in carouse.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [6, 7], [25, 25]]}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "204.1", "t": "Effused is he who brings good things, who brings us store of wealth, and sweet refreshing food,<br>Soma who brings us quiet homes:"}, {"st": "204.2", "t": "He whom our Indra and the Marut host shall drink, Bhaga shall drink with Aryaman,<br>By whom we bring to us Mitra and Varuna, and Indra for our great defence."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "205.1", "t": "Friends, hymn your Lord who makes him pure for rapturous carouse: let them<br>Sweeten him, as a child, with lauds and sacred gifts"}, {"st": "205.2", "t": "Like as a calf with mother cows, so Indu is urged forth and sent,<br>Glorified by our hymns;, the god-delighting juice."}, {"st": "205.3", "t": "Effectual help to power is he. he is a banquet for the troop,<br>He who hath been effused, more rich in meath, for Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "206.1", "t": "For us the Soma juices flow, the drops best furtherers of weal,<br>Effused as friends, without a spot, benevolent, finders of the light."}, {"st": "206.2", "t": "These Soma juices, skill.ed in song, purified, blent with milk and curd,<br>Hastening on and firmly set in oil resemble beauteous suns."}, {"st": "206.3", "t": "Effused by means of pressing-stones, upon the oxhide visible,<br>They, treasure-finders, have announced food unto us from every side."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 21 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "207.1", "t": "Pour forth this wealth with this purification: flow onward to the yellow lake, O Indu!<br>Here, too, the bright one, wind-swift, full of wisdom, shall give a son to him who cometh quickly."}, {"st": "207.2", "t": "Flow on for us with this purification to the famed ford of thee whose due is glory!<br>May the foe-queller shake us down, for triumph, like a tree’s ripe fruit, sixty thousand treasures!"}, {"st": "207.3", "t": "Eagerly do we pray for those two exploits, at the blue lake and Prisana, wrought in battle.<br>He sent our enemies to sleep and slew them, and turned away the foolish and unfriendly."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 22 · Agni"}, {"st": "208.1", "t": "O Agni, be our nearest friend, yea, our protector and our kind deliverer!"}, {"st": "208.2", "t": "As gracious Agni, famed for treasures, come, and, most resplendent, give us store of wealth!"}, {"st": "208.3", "t": "To thee then, O most bright, O radiant God, we come with prayer for happiness for our friends."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 23 · Indra"}, {"st": "209.1", "t": "May we, with Indra and the Gods to aid us, bring these existing worlds to full completion!"}, {"st": "209.2", "t": "Our sacrifice, our bodies, and our offspring, let Indra with the Adityas-form and finish!"}, {"st": "209.3", "t": "With the Adityas, with the band of Maruts, let Indra send us medicines to heal us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 24 · Indra"}, {"st": "210.1", "t": "SING TO your Indra, mightiest Vritra-slayer, sing to the Sage the song that he accepteth!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "211.1", "t": "The God declares the deities’ generations, like Usana, proclaiming lofty wisdom.<br>With brilliant kin far-ruling, sanctifying, the wild boar, singing with his foot, advances."}, {"st": "211.2", "t": "The swans, the Vrishagnas from anear us, restless, have brought their clamour to our dwelling — <br>Friends come to Pavamana, meet for praises-and sound in concert their resistless music."}, {"st": "211.3", "t": "He takes the swiftness of the great Far strider: cows low as, ‘twere to him who sports at pleasure.<br>He with the sharpened horns brings forth abundance: the silvery shines by night, by day the golden."}, {"st": "211.4", "t": "Like cars that thunder on their way, like coursers eager for renown,<br>Have Soma drops flowed forth for wealth."}, {"st": "211.5", "t": "Forth have they rushed from holding hands, like chariots that are urged to speed,<br>Like joyful songs of singing-men."}, {"st": "211.6", "t": "The Somas deck themselves with milk as kings are graced with eulogies,<br>And, with seven priests, the sacrifice."}, {"st": "211.7", "t": "Pressed for the gladdening draught the drops flow forth abundantly with song,<br>Flow with the stream of savoury juice."}, {"st": "211.8", "t": "Winning Vivasvan’s glory and speeding the light of Dawn, the suns,<br>Pass through the openings of the cloth."}, {"st": "211.9", "t": "The singing-men of ancient time open the doors of sacred songs — <br>The men who bring the mighty One."}, {"st": "211.10", "t": "In close society have come the priests, the sevenfold brotherhood,<br>Filling the station of the One."}, {"st": "211.11", "t": "He makes us kin with Gods, he joins the Sun, for seeing, with mine eye;<br>I milk the Sage’s offspring forth."}, {"st": "211.12", "t": "The Sun beholdeth with his eye the heaven’s dear quarter which the priests<br>Have set within the sacred cell."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "212.1", "t": "Forth on their way the glorious drops have flowed for maintenance of Law,<br>Knowing what suits this worshipper."}, {"st": "212.2", "t": "Down in the mighty waters sinks the stream of Meath, most excellent,<br>Oblation best of all in worth."}, {"st": "212.3", "t": "About the holy place the Steer, true, guileless, noblest, hath sent forth,<br>Continuous voices in the wood."}, {"st": "212.4", "t": "When the Sage, purging manly deeds and lofty wisdom flows, around,"}, {"st": "212.5", "t": "When purified, he sits enthroned as King over the warring clans.<br>What time the sages speed him on."}, {"st": "212.6", "t": "Most dear, gold-coloured, in the fleece he sinks, and settles in the wood:<br>The singer is besieged with song."}, {"st": "212.7", "t": "He goes to Indra, Vayu, and the Asvins with the rapturous joy,<br>To whomsoe’er his power delights."}, {"st": "212.8", "t": "The waves of pleasant Soma flow to Bhaga, Mitra, Varuna,<br>Well knowing, through his mighty powers."}, {"st": "212.9", "t": "Gain for us, O ye Heaven and Earth, riches of Meath to win us strength:<br>Gain for us treasures and renown."}, {"st": "212.10", "t": "We choose to-day that chariot-steed of thine, the strong, that brings us bliss,<br>The guardian, the desire of all;"}, {"st": "212.11", "t": "The excellent, the gladdener, the Sage with heart that understands.<br>The guardian, the desire of all;"}, {"st": "212.12", "t": "Who for ourselves, O thou most wise, is wealth and fair intelligence,<br>The guardian, the desire of all."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Agni"}, {"st": "213.1", "t": "Agni Vaisvanara, born in course of Order, the messenger of earth, the head of heaven,<br>The Sage, the Sovran, guest of men, our vessel fit for their mouth, the Gods have generated."}, {"st": "213.2", "t": "To thee, immortal! when to life thou springest all the Gods sing for joy as to their infant.<br>They by thy mental powers were made immortal, Vaisvdnara when thou shonest from thy parents."}, {"st": "213.3", "t": "Him have they praised, mid-point of sacrifices, great cistern of libations, seat of riches.<br>Vaisvanara, conveyer of oblations, ensign of worship, have the Gods engendered."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Mitra-Varuna"}, {"st": "214.1", "t": "Sing forth unto your Varuna and Mitra with a song inspired:<br>They, mighty Lords, are lofty law."}, {"st": "214.2", "t": "Full springs of fatness, sovran Kings, Mitra and Varuna, the twain,<br>Gods glorified among the Gods,"}, {"st": "214.3", "t": "So help ye us to riches, great celestial and terrestrial wealth!<br>Vast is your sway among the Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "215.1", "t": "O Indra marvellously bright, come, these libations long for thee,<br>Thus by fine fingers purified!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [77, 76]]}, {"st": "215.2", "t": "Urged by the holy singer, sped by song, come nigh, O Indra, to<br>The sacrificing suppliant’s pravers!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "215.3", "t": "Approach, O Indra, basting thee, Lord of bay horses, to our prayers:<br>In our libation t ake delight!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Indra-Agni"}, {"st": "216.1", "t": "Glorify him who compasses all forests with his glowing Dame,<br>And leaves them blackened by his tongue."}, {"st": "216.2", "t": "He who gains Indra’s grace by fire enkindled, finds as easy way<br>Over the floods to splendid wealth."}, {"st": "216.3", "t": "Give us, ye twain, swift steeds to bring Indra and Agni, and bestow<br>Abundant food with wealth on us."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "217.1", "t": "Indu hath started forth for Indra’s settled place, and slights not, as a friend, the promise of his friend.<br>Soma comes onward like a youth with youthful maids, and gains the beaker by a course of hundred paths."}, {"st": "217.2", "t": "Your hymns of pleasant sound, praiseworthy, fond of lauds, have come into the hall enclosed for sacrifice.<br>Singers have hymned the golden-coloured as he sports, and milchkine have come near to meet him with their milk,"}, {"st": "217.3", "t": "O Soma, Indu, while they cleanse thee, with thy wave pour orb us plentiful accumulated food,<br>Which, ceaseless, thrice a day shall yield us hero power enriched. with store of nourishment, and strength, and meath."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Indra"}, {"st": "218.1", "t": "No one by deed attains to him who works and strengthensevermore:<br>No, not by sacrifice, to Indra praised of all, resistless, daring, bold in might;"}, {"st": "218.2", "t": "The powerful conqueror, invincible in war, him at whose birth the mighty ones,<br>The kine who spread afar, sent their loud voices out, heavens, earths sent their loud voices out."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Soma Vaisvanara"}, {"st": "219.1", "t": "Sit down, O friends, and sing aloud to him who purifies himself:<br>Deck him for glory, like a child, with holy rites"}, {"st": "219.2", "t": "Loose him who bringeth household wealth, even as a calf with. mother kine,<br>Him who bath double strength, strong, god-delighting juice!"}, {"st": "219.3", "t": "Purify him who gives us power, most blissful one, that he may be<br>A banquet for the troop, Mitra, and Varuna!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "220.1", "t": "The Strong hath flowed forth in a thousand streams, flowed through the filter and the sheep’s long wool."}, {"st": "220.2", "t": "With ceaseless genial flow the Strong hath run, purified by the waters, blent with milk."}, {"st": "220.3", "t": "Pressed out with stones, directed by the men, go forth, O Soma, into Indra’s throat!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "221.1", "t": "The Soma juices which have been expressed afar or near at hand,<br>Or there on Saryanavan’s bank,"}, {"st": "221.2", "t": "Those pressed among Arjikas, pressed among the active, in, men’s homes,<br>Or pressed among the Fivefold Tribes —"}, {"st": "221.3", "t": "May these celestial drops, expressed, pour forth upon us, as they flow,<br>Rain from the heavens and hero strength!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Agni"}, {"st": "222.1", "t": "May Vatsa draw thy mind away even from thy loftiest dwelling-place!<br>Agni, I yearn for thee with song."}, {"st": "222.2", "t": "Thou art alike in many a place: through all the regions thou art Lord.<br>In fray and fight we call on thee."}, {"st": "222.3", "t": "When we are seeking spoil we call Agni to help us in the strife,<br>Giver of wordrous gifts in war."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "", "t": "1, O Indra, bring great strength to us, bring valour, Satakratu, thou most active, bring<br>A hero conquering in war!<br>2. For, gracious Satakratu, thou hast ever been a mother and a sire to us,<br>So now for bliss we pray to thee.<br>3. To thee, strong! much-invoked! who showest forth thy strength, made very mighty! do I speak:<br>So grant thou us heroic power!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "224.1", "t": "Stone-Darting Indra, wonderous God, what wealth thou hast not given me here,<br>That bounty, treasure-finder! bring, filling full both thy hands, to us!"}, {"st": "224.2", "t": "Bring what thou deemest worth the wish, O Indra that which is in heaven!<br>So may we know thee as thou art a giver boundless in thy gifts!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "224.3", "t": "Thy lofty spirit famed in all the regions as appeasable, — <br>With this thou rendest even things firm, Stone-darter! so to win thee strength."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "225.1", "t": "The Maruts with their troop adorn and brighten, even at his birth, the Sage, the lovely infant.<br>By songs a poet, and a Sage by wisdom, Soma goes singing through the cleansing filter."}, {"st": "225.2", "t": "Light-winner, Rishi-minded, Rishi-maker, hymned in a thousand hymns, leader of sages,<br>Eager to gain his third form, mighty, Soma is, like Viraj, resplendent as a singer."}, {"st": "225.3", "t": "Hawk seated in the press, bird wide-extended, the banner seeking kine and wielding weapons,<br>Uniting with the sea, the wave of waters, the mighty tells his fourth form and declares it."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "226.1", "t": "Obeying Indra’s dear desire these Soma juices have flowed forth<br>Increasing his heroic might."}, {"st": "226.2", "t": "Laid in the press and flowing pure to Vayu and the Asvins, may<br>These give us great heroic strength."}, {"st": "226.3", "t": "Soma, as thou art purified, incite to bounty Indra’s heart,<br>To seat him in the shrine of Gods!"}, {"st": "226.4", "t": "The ten swift fingers deck thee forth seven ministers impel thee on,<br>The sages have rejoiced in thee."}, {"st": "226.5", "t": "When through the filter thou art poured we clothe thee with a robe of milk,<br>To be a rapturous feast for Gods."}, {"st": "226.6", "t": "When purified within the jars, Soma bright-red and golden-hued,<br>Hath veiled him in a milky dress."}, {"st": "226.7", "t": "Flow onward to our wealthy lords. Drive all our enemies away:<br>O Indu, pass into thy friend!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "226.8", "t": "May we obtain thee, Indra’s drink, who viewest men and findest light,<br>Gain thee and progeny and food!"}, {"st": "226.9", "t": "Send down the rain from heaven and make splendour upon the earth! Give us,<br>O Soma, victory in war!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "227.1", "t": "Poured through the fleece in thousand streams purified Soma floweth to,<br>Indra’s and Vayu’s meeting-place."}, {"st": "227.2", "t": "Sing forth, ye men who long for help, to Pavamana, to the Sage,<br>Effused to entertain the Gods!"}, {"st": "227.3", "t": "The Soma drops with thousand powers are purified to win us strength,<br>Hymned to become the feast of Gods."}, {"st": "227.4", "t": "Yea, as thou flowest bring great store of food that we may win us strength:<br>Indu, bring splendid manly might"}, {"st": "227.5", "t": "Like coursers by their drivers urged, they were poured forth, to win us strength,<br>Swift through the woollen straining-cloth."}, {"st": "227.6", "t": "May they in flowing give us wealth in thousands, and heroic power, — <br>These godlike Soma drops effused!"}, {"st": "227.7", "t": "The roaring Soma drops flow on, like milch-kine lowing to, their calves:<br>They have run forth from both the hands."}, {"st": "227.8", "t": "Beloved by Indra, bringing joy, roaring as thou art purified,<br>Drive all our enemies away."}, {"st": "227.9", "t": "As Pavamanas, driving off the godless, looking on the light,<br>Sit in the place of sacrifice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "228.1", "t": "The Soma drops, exceeding rich in sweets, to Indra have been poured,<br>Shed with the stream of sacrifice."}, {"st": "228.2", "t": "Sages have called to Indra, like cows, milch-kine, lowing to their calves,<br>Called him to drink the Soma juice."}, {"st": "228.3", "t": "In the stream’s wave wise Soma dwells, distilling rapture, in his. seat,<br>Resting upon a wild cow’s hide."}, {"st": "228.4", "t": "Far-sighted Soma, Sage and bard, is worshipped in the central point,<br>Of heaven, the straining-cloth of wool."}, {"st": "228.5", "t": "In close embracement Indu holds Soma when poured within the: jars.<br>And on the purifying sieve."}, {"st": "228.6", "t": "Indu sends forth a voice on high, up in the region of the sea.<br>Stirring the cask that drops with meath."}, {"st": "228.7", "t": "The tree whose praises never fail dwells in the stream of holy milk,<br>Urged onward by its human friend."}, {"st": "228.8", "t": "O Pavamana bring us wealth bright with a thousand splendours; yea,<br>O Indu, give us ready help!"}, {"st": "228.9", "t": "Sage, poet, poured with all his stream, Soma is driven, far away,<br>To the dear places of the sky."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "229.1", "t": "Loud as a river’s roaring wave thy powers have lifted up themselves:<br>Urge on thine arrow’s sharpened point!"}, {"st": "229.2", "t": "At thine effusion upward rise three voices fresh and strong, when thou.<br>Flowest upon the fleecy ridge."}, {"st": "229.3", "t": "On to the fleece they urge with stones the dear, the goldencoloured one,<br>Even Pavamana dropping meath."}, {"st": "229.4", "t": "Flow with thy current to the sieve, O Sage, best giver of delight,<br>To seat these in the shrine of song!"}, {"st": "229.5", "t": "Best giver of delight, flow on anointed with the milk for balm,<br>And enter into Indra’s throat!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "230.1", "t": "Flow onward, Indu, with this food for him who in thy wild delights,<br>Battered the nine-and-ninety down."}, {"st": "230.2", "t": "Smote swiftly forts, and Sambara, then Yadu and that Turvasa,<br>For pious Divodasa’s sake!"}, {"st": "230.3", "t": "Finder of horses, pour on us horses and wealth in kine and gold,<br>And Indu, food in boundless store!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "231.1", "t": "Chasing our foemen, driving off the godless, Soma floweth on,<br>Going to Indra’s settled place."}, {"st": "231.2", "t": "O Pavamana, hither bring great riches, and destroy our foes:<br>O Indu, grant heroic fame!"}, {"st": "231.3", "t": "A hundred obstacles have ne’er checked thee when rain to give thy boons,<br>When, being cleansed, thou combatest."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "232.1", "t": "Flow onward with that stream wherewith thou gavest splendour to the sun,<br>Speeding the waters kind to man!"}, {"st": "232.2", "t": "He, Pavamana, high o’er man, yoked the Sun’s courser Etasa,<br>To travel through the realm of air."}, {"st": "232.3", "t": "Yea, those bay steeds he harnessed to the chariot that the Sun might come:<br>Indu, he said, is Indra’s self."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Agni"}, {"st": "233.1", "t": "Associate with fires, make your God Agni envoy at sacrifice, best skilled in worship,<br>Established firm among mankind, the holy flame-crowned and fed with oil, the purifier!"}, {"st": "233.2", "t": "Like a steed neighing eager for the pasture, when he hath stepped forth from the great enclosure:<br>Then the wind following blows upon his splendour, and, straight, the path is black which thou hast travelled."}, {"st": "233.3", "t": "From thee, a bull but newly born, O Agni, the kindled everlasting flames rise upward.<br>Aloft to heaven as ruddy smoke thou mountest: Agni, thou speedest to the Gods as envoy."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Indra"}, {"st": "234.1", "t": "We make this Indra very strong to strike the mighty Vritra dead:<br>A vigorous hero shall he be."}, {"st": "234.2", "t": "This Indra, made for giving gifts, is stablished, mightiest, in strength,<br>Bright, meet for Soma, famed in song."}, {"st": "234.3", "t": "By song, as ‘twere’ the powerful bolt which none may parry, was prepared:<br>Strong and invincible he grew."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Adhvaryu, to the filter lead the Soma-juice expressed with stones:<br>Make thou it pure for Indra’s drink!<br>2. These Gods and all the Marut host, Indu! enjoy this juice of thine,<br>This Pavamana’s flowing meath.<br>3. Pour out for Indra, Thunder-armed, the milk of heaven, the Soma’s juice,<br>Most excellent, most rich in sweets!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "236.1", "t": "On flows the potent juice, sustainer of the heavens, the strength of Gods, whom men must hail with shouts of joy,<br>Thou, gold-hued, started like a courser by brave men, art lightly showing forth thy splendour in the streams."}, {"st": "236.2", "t": "He takes his weapons, like a hero, in his hands, fain to win light, car-borne, in forays for the kine.<br>Indu, while stimulating Indra’s might, is urged forward and balmed by sages skilful in their task."}, {"st": "236.3", "t": "Soma, as thou art purified with flowing wave, exhibiting thy strength enter thou Indra’s throat.<br>Make both worlds stream for us, as lightning doth the clouds: mete out exhaustless powers for us through this our prayer!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "237.1", "t": "Though, Indra, thou art called by men eastward and westward, north and south,<br>Thou chiefly art with Anava and Turvasa, brave champion! urged by men to come."}, {"st": "237.2", "t": "Or, Indra, when with Ruma, Rusama, Syavaka, and Kripa thou rejoicest thee,<br>Still do the Kanvas, bringing prayer, with hymns of praise O Indra, draw thee hither: come!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "238.1", "t": "Both boons,-may, Indra, hitherward turned, listen to this prayer of ours.<br>And mightiest Maghavan with thought inclined to us come near to drink to Soma juice!"}, {"st": "238.2", "t": "For him, strong, independent ruler, Heaven and Earth have fashioned forth with power and might.<br>Thou seatest thee as first among thy peers in place, for thy soul longs for Soma juice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "239.1", "t": "God, working with mankind flow on; to Indra go thy gladdening juice:<br>To Vayu mount as Law commands!"}, {"st": "239.2", "t": "O Soma Pavamana, thou pourest out wealth that may be famed:<br>O Indu, pass into the lake!"}, {"st": "239.3", "t": "Soma, thou flowest chasing foes, finder of wisdom and delight:<br>Drive thou the godless folk afar!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "240.1", "t": "Stream on us riches that are craved by hundreds, best at winning spoil,<br>Riches, O Indu, thousandfold, most splendid, that surpass the light!"}, {"st": "240.2", "t": "May we, O Vasu, be most near to this thy bounty, food, and wealth!<br>Desired by many men, and in thy favour, O resistless one!"}, {"st": "240.3", "t": "Effused, this Indu hath flowed on, distilling rapture, to the fleece.<br>He streams erect to sacrifice, as ‘twere with splendour, seeking kine."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "241.1", "t": "Flow onward, Soma, as a mighty sea, as Father of the Gods, to every form!"}, {"st": "241.2", "t": "Flow on, O Soma, radiant for the Gods, blissful to heaven and earth and living things!"}, {"st": "241.3", "t": "Thou art, bright juice, sustainer of the sky: flow, mighty, in accordance with true law!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Agni"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. I laud your most beloved guest, like a dear friend,<br>O Agni, him!<br>Who, like a chariot, wins us wealth.<br>2. Whom as a Sage who merits praise the Gods have, from the olden time,<br>Established among mortal men.<br>3. Do thou, most youthful God, protect the men who offer, hear their songs,<br>And of thyself preserve their seed!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Indra"}, {"st": "243.1", "t": "Come unto us, O Indra, dear, still conquering, unconcealable<br>Wide as a mountain spread on all sides, Lord of heaven."}, {"st": "243.2", "t": "O truthful Soma-drinker, thou art mightier than both the worlds.<br>Thou strengthenest him who pours’libation, Lord of heaven."}, {"st": "243.3", "t": "For thou art he, O Indra, who upholdeth all our fortresses,<br>The Dasyu’s slayer, man’s sustainer, Lord of heaven."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Indra"}, {"st": "244.1", "t": "Render of forts, the young, the wise, of strength unmeasured, was he born,<br>Sustainer of each sacred rite, Indra, the Thunderer, much extolled,"}, {"st": "244.2", "t": "Thou wielder of the stone, didst burst the cave of Vala rich in kine.<br>The Gods came pressing to thy side, and free from terror aided thee."}, {"st": "244.3", "t": "They glorified with hymns of praise Indra who reigneth by his might,<br>Whose bounteous gifts in thousands come, yea, even more abundantly."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "245.1", "t": "Guard of all being, generating creatures, loud roared the sea as highest law commanded.<br>Strong in the filter, on the fleecy summit, pressed from the stone, Soma hath waxen mighty."}, {"st": "245.2", "t": "Make Vayu glad, for furtherance and bounty: cheer Varuna and Mitra, as they cleanse thee!<br>Gladden the Gods, gladden the host of Maruts: make Heaven and Earth rejoice, O God, O Soma!"}, {"st": "245.3", "t": "Soma, the mighty, when, the water’s offspring, he chose the Gods, performed that great achievement.<br>He, Pavamana, granted strength to Indra: he, Indu, generated strength in Surya."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "246.1", "t": "Here present this immortal God flies, like a bird upon her wings,<br>To settle in the vats of wood."}, {"st": "246.2", "t": "Praised by the sacred bards, this God dives into waters, and bestows<br>Rich gifts upon the worshipper."}, {"st": "246.3", "t": "He. like a warrior going forth with heroes, as he flows along.<br>Is fain to win all precious boons."}, {"st": "246.4", "t": "This God as he is flowirig on speeds like a car and gives his aid:<br>He lets his voice be heard of all."}, {"st": "246.5", "t": "This God, while flowing, is adorned, gold-coloured, for the spoil, by men<br>Devout and skilled in holy songs."}, {"st": "246.6", "t": "This God, made ready with the hymn runs swiftly through the winding ways,<br>Inviolable as he flows."}, {"st": "246.7", "t": "A way he rushes with his stream, across the regions, into heaven,<br>And roars as he is flowing on."}, {"st": "246.8", "t": "While flowing, meet for sacrifice, he hath gone up to heaven, across<br>The regions, never overthrown."}, {"st": "246.9", "t": "By generation long ago, this God, engendered for the Gods,<br>Flows tawny to the straining-cloth."}, {"st": "246.10", "t": "This Lord of many holy laws, even at his birth engendering strength,<br>Effused, flows onward in a stream."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "247.1", "t": "Through the fine fingers, with the song, this hero comes with rapid cars,<br>Going to Indra’s settled place."}, {"st": "247.2", "t": "In holy thought he ponders much for the great service of theGods,<br>Where the immortals have their seat."}, {"st": "247.3", "t": "Men beautify him in the vats, him worthy to be beautified,<br>Him who brings forth abundant food."}, {"st": "247.4", "t": "He is deposited and led along the consecrated path<br>When zealous men are urging him,"}, {"st": "247.5", "t": "He moves, a vigorous steed, adorned with beauteous rays of shining gold,<br>He who is Sovran of the streams."}, {"st": "247.6", "t": "He brandishes his horns on high, and whets them, bull who leads the herd,<br>Doing with might heroic deeds."}, {"st": "247.7", "t": "He, over places rough to pass bringing rich treasures, closely pressed.<br>Descends into the reservoirs."}, {"st": "247.8", "t": "Him, even him the golden-hued, well armed, best giver of delight,<br>Ten fingers urge to run his course."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "248.1", "t": "This Bull, this chariot robes him in the sheep’s long wool as heproceeds.<br>To war that wins a thousand spoils."}, {"st": "248.2", "t": "The dames of Trita with the stones urge forth this goldencoloured one,<br>Indu to Indra for his drink."}, {"st": "248.3", "t": "He like a falcon settles down amid the families of men,<br>Like lover speeding to his love."}, {"st": "248.4", "t": "This young exhilarating juice looks downward from its place in heaven,<br>This Soma drop that pierced the sieve."}, {"st": "248.5", "t": "Pressed for the draught, this tawny juice flows forth intelligent, calling out,<br>Unto the well-beloved place."}, {"st": "248.6", "t": "Him, here, the gold-decked skilful ten cleanse carefully, who make him bright.<br>And beauteous for the gladdening draught."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "249.1", "t": "Urged by the men, this vigorous steed, Lord of the mind omniscient,<br>Flies to the long wool of the sheep."}, {"st": "249.2", "t": "Within the filter hath he flowed, this Soma for the Gods effused.<br>Entering all their essences."}, {"st": "249.3", "t": "He shines in beauty there, this God, immortal, in his dwellingplace,<br>Foe-slayer, dearest to the Gods."}, {"st": "249.4", "t": "Directed by the sisters ten, bellowing on his way this Steer<br>Runs onward to the wooden vats."}, {"st": "249.5", "t": "This Pavamana, gladdening drink within the purifying sieve,<br>Gave splendour to the Sun in heaven."}, {"st": "249.6", "t": "Unconquerable Lord of speech, dwelling beside Viavasvan, he<br>Mounts up together with the Sun."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "250.1", "t": "This Sage, exalted by our lands, flows to the purifying sieve,<br>Scattering foes as he is cleansed."}, {"st": "250.2", "t": "Giver of strength, winner of light, for Indra and for Vayu he<br>Is poured upon the filtering-cloth."}, {"st": "250.3", "t": "The men conduct him, Soma, Steer, omniscient the head of heaven.<br>Effused into the vats of wood."}, {"st": "250.4", "t": "Longing for kine, longing for gold hath Indu Pavamana roared,<br>Still conqueror, never overcome."}, {"st": "250.5", "t": "To Indra in the firmament this mighty tawny Steer hath flowed<br>This Indu, being purified."}, {"st": "250.6", "t": "This Soma being purified flows mighty and invincible, Slayer of sinners, dear to Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "251.1", "t": "This Soma, strong effused for draught, flows to the purifying sieve,<br>Slaying the fiends, loving the Gods."}, {"st": "251.2", "t": "Far sighted, tawny-coloured, he flows to the sieve intelligent,<br>Bellowing to his place of rest."}, {"st": "251.3", "t": "This vigorous Pavamana runs forth to the luminous realm of heaven,<br>Fiend-slayer, through the sheep’s long wool."}, {"st": "251.4", "t": "This Pavamana, up above on Trita’s ridge, hath made the Sun,<br>Together with the Sisters, shine."}, {"st": "251.5", "t": "Effused, this Soma, Steer, who slays Vritra, room-giver, unbeguiled,<br>Hath gone as ‘twere to win the spoil."}, {"st": "251.6", "t": "Urged by the sage upon his way, this God speeds forward to the: vats,<br>Indu to Indra, giving boons."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "252.1", "t": "The man who reads the essence stored by saints, the Pavamana hymns,<br>Tastes food completely purified, made sweet by Matarisvan’s touch."}, {"st": "252.2", "t": "Whoever reads the essence stored by saints, the Pavamana hymns,<br>For him Sarasvat! pours forth water and butter, milk and meath."}, {"st": "252.3", "t": "Yea, for the Pavamanas flow richly, drop fatness, bring us weal, — <br>Amrit deposited among the Brahmans, essence stored by saints."}, {"st": "252.4", "t": "So may the Pavamana hymns bestow on us this world and that,<br>And gratify our hearts’ desires’-the Goddesses combined with Gods!"}, {"st": "252.5", "t": "The purifying flood wherewith Gods ever purify themselves, — <br>With that, in thousand currents, may the Pavamanas make us clean!"}, {"st": "252.6", "t": "The Pavamana hymns bring weal: by these man goes to Paradise,<br>And, eating pure and holy food, attains to immortality."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Agni"}, {"st": "253.1", "t": "We with great reverence have approached the Youngest, who hath shone forth well kindled in his dwelling,<br>Wondrously bright between wide earth and heaven, well worshipped, looking forth in all directions."}, {"st": "253.2", "t": "Through his great might o’ercoming all misfortunes, praised in the house is Agni Jatavedas.<br>May he preserve us from disgrace and trouble, both us who laud him and our wealthy princes!"}, {"st": "253.3", "t": "O Agni, thou art Varuna and Mitra: Vasishthas! with their holy hymns exalt thee.<br>With thee be most abundant gain of treasure!<br>Do ye preserve us evermore with blessing!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Indra"}, {"st": "254.1", "t": "Indra, great in his power and might, and like Parjanya rich in rain.<br>Hath been increased by Vatsa’s lauds."}, {"st": "254.2", "t": "Since Kanvas have with lauds made him completer of the sacrifice,<br>Words are their own appropriate arms."}, {"st": "254.3", "t": "When priests who magnify the Son of holy law present their gifts,<br>Sages with Order’s hymn of praise."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "255.1", "t": "Of gold-hued Pavamana, great destroyer, radiant streams have flowed,<br>Swift streams of him whose gleams are swift."}, {"st": "255.2", "t": "Best rider of the chariot, praised with fairest praise ‘mid beauteous ones,<br>Gold gleaming with the Marut host,"}, {"st": "255.3", "t": "Penetrate, Pavamana, best at winning booty, with thy rays,<br>Giving the Singer hero strength!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "256.1", "t": "Hence sprinkle forth the juice effused, Soma, the best of sacred gifts,<br>Who, friend of man, hath run among the water-streams He hath pressed Soma out with stones."}, {"st": "256.2", "t": "Now, being purified, flow hither through the fleece, invincible and more odorous!<br>We joy in thee in waters when thou art effused, blending thee still with juice and milk."}, {"st": "256.3", "t": "Pressed out for all to see, delighting Gods, Indu, far-seeing one, is mental power."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "257.1", "t": "Even as a King hath Soma, red and tawny Bull, been pressed the wondrous one hath bellowed to the kine.<br>While purified thou passest through the filtering fleece to seat thee hawk-like in the place that drops with oil."}, {"st": "257.2", "t": "Parjanya is the sire of the leaf-bearing Bull: on mountains, in earth’s centre hath he made his home.<br>The waters have flowed forth, the Sisters, to the kine: he meets the pressing-stones at the beloved rite."}, {"st": "257.3", "t": "To glory goest thou, a Sage with ordering skill, like a groomed steed thou rushest forward to the prize.<br>Be gracious to us, Soma, driving off distress! Thou goest, clothed in butter, to a robe of state."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "258.1", "t": "Turning as ‘twere to meet the Sun, enjoy from Indra all good things!<br>When he who will be born is born with power we look to treasures as our heritage."}, {"st": "258.2", "t": "Praise him who sends us wealth, prompt with his liberal boons Good are the gifts that Indra gives.<br>He is not wroth with one who satisfies his wish: he instigates, his mind to give."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Indra"}, {"st": "259.1", "t": "Indra, give us security from that whereof we are afraid<br>Help us, O Maghavan, let thy favour aid us thus drive away foes and enemies!"}, {"st": "259.2", "t": "For thou, O liberal Lord of ample bounty, art the ruler of our house and home.<br>So, Indra Maghavan, thou lover of the song, we with pressed Soma call on thee."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "260.1", "t": "Thou, Soma, hast a running stream, sweet-toned most strong at sacrifice:<br>Flow bounteously bestowing wealth"}, {"st": "260.2", "t": "Thou most delightful, when effused, running, the best of gladdeners, art<br>Indu, still conquering, ne’er subdued."}, {"st": "260.3", "t": "Do thou, poured forth by pressing-stones, flow hither uttering a roar,<br>And bring us brightly-glorious strength!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "261.1", "t": "In might, O Indu, with thy streams flow for the banquet of the Gods:<br>Rich in meath, Soma, in our beaker take thy seat!"}, {"st": "261.2", "t": "Thy drops that swim in water have exalted Indra to delight<br>The Gods have drunk thee up for immortality."}, {"st": "261.3", "t": "Stream opulence to us, ye drops of Soma, pressed and purified<br>Pouring down rain from heaven in floods, and finding light!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "262.1", "t": "Him with the fleece they purify, brown, golden-hued beloved of all,<br>Who with exhilarating juice goes forth to all the deities"}, {"st": "262.2", "t": "Whom, bright with native splendour, crushed between the preesing-stones, a friend.<br>Whom Indra dearly loves, the waves and ten companions dip and bathe"}, {"st": "262.3", "t": "For Vritra-slaying Indra, thou, Soma, art poured that he may drink,<br>And for the guerdon-giving man, the hero sitting in his seat."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "263.1", "t": "Flow onward Soma, flow for mighty strength, as a strong courser, bathed, to win the prize."}, {"st": "263.2", "t": "The pressers clarify this juice of thine, the Soma for delight and lofty fame."}, {"st": "263.3", "t": "They deck the gold-hued infant, newly-born, even Soma, Indu, in the sieve, for Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "264.1", "t": "The Gods have come to Indu well-descended, beautified with milk,<br>The active crusher of the foe."}, {"st": "264.2", "t": "Even as mother cows their calf, so let our praise-songs strengthen him,<br>Yea, him who winneth Indra’s heart!"}, {"st": "264.3", "t": "Soma, pour blessings on our kine, pour forth the food that streams with milk:<br>Increase the sea, praiseworthy one!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 21 · Indra"}, {"st": "265.1", "t": "Hitherward! they who light the flame and straightway trim the sacred grass,<br>Whose friend is Indra ever young."}, {"st": "265.2", "t": "Large is their fuel, much their laud, wide is their splinter from the stake,<br>Whose friend is Indra ever young."}, {"st": "265.3", "t": "Unquelled in fight the hero leads his army with the warrior chiefs,<br>Whose friend is Indra ever young."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 22 · Indra"}, {"st": "266.1", "t": "He who alone bestoweth wealth on mortal man who offereth gifts,<br>Is Indra only, potent Lord whom none resist."}, {"st": "266.2", "t": "Whoever with the Soma pressed draws thee away from many men,-<br>Verily Indra gains thereby tremendous power."}, {"st": "266.3", "t": "When willhe trample, like a weed, the man who hath no gift for him?<br>When, verily, will Indra hear our songs of praise?"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 23 · Indra"}, {"st": "267.1", "t": "The singers hymn thee, they who chant the psalm of praise are lauding thee.<br>The Brahmans have exalted thee, O Satakratu, like a pole.<br>2, When thou wast climbing ridge from ridge, he looked upon the toilsome task:<br>Indra takes notice of that wish, and the Ram hastens with his troop."}, {"st": "267.3", "t": "Harness thy pair of strong bay steeds, long-maned, whose bodies fill the girths.<br>And, Indra, Soma drinker, come to listen to our songs Of praise!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "268.1", "t": "Agni, well kindled bring the Gods for him who offers holy gifts;<br>And worship them, pure Hotar-priest!"}, {"st": "268.2", "t": "O Sage, Tanunapat, present our sacrifice to Gods to-day,<br>Sweet to the taste, that they may help!"}, {"st": "268.3", "t": "Dear Narasansa, sweet of tongue, presenter of oblations, I<br>Invoke to this our sacrifice."}, {"st": "268.4", "t": "Agni, on thy most easy car, entreated, hither bring the Gods!<br>Manus-appointed Priest art thou."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Adityas"}, {"st": "269.1", "t": "So when the Sun hath risen to-day may sinless Mitra, Aryaman, Bhaga, and Savitar send us forth!"}, {"st": "269.2", "t": "May this our home be guarded well: forward, ye bounteous, on the way, Who bear us safely o’er distress!"}, {"st": "269.3", "t": "Yea, Aditi, and those great Kings whose statute is inviolate, Are sovrans of a vast domain."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "270.1", "t": "Let Soma juices make thee glad! Display thy bounty, Thunderer:<br>Drive off the enemies of prayer!"}, {"st": "270.2", "t": "Crush with thy foot the niggard churls who bring no gifts! mighty art thou:<br>There is not one to equal thee."}, {"st": "270.3", "t": "Thou art the Lord of Somas pressed, Somas unpressed are also thine:<br>Thou art the Sovran of the folk."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "271.1", "t": "True object of our hymns, Sage, watchful Soma hath settled in the press as they refine him.<br>Him the Adhvaryus, paired and eager, follow, leaders of sacrifice and skilful-handed."}, {"st": "271.2", "t": "He, purified and bringing gifts to Surya, hath filled full heaven and earth, and hath disclosed them.<br>He by whose dear help heroes gain their wishes will yield the precious meed as to a victor."}, {"st": "271.3", "t": "He, being cleansed, the strengthener and increaser, bountiful Soma helped us his lustre,<br>Wherein our sires of old who knew the footsteps found light and sought the kine within the mountain."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "272.1", "t": "Glorify naught besides, O friends, so shall no sorrow trouble you!<br>Praise only mighty Indra, when the juice is shed, and say your lauds repeatedly!"}, {"st": "272.2", "t": "Even him, the swift one, like a bull who rushes down men’s conqueror, bounteous like a cow;<br>Him who is cause of both, of enmity and peace, to both sides most munificent."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Indra"}, {"st": "273.1", "t": "These songs of our exceeding sweet, these hymns of praise ascend to thee,<br>Like ever-conquering chariots that display their strength, gain wealth and give unfailing help."}, {"st": "273.2", "t": "The Bhrigus are like suns, like Kanvas, and have gained each thing whereon their thought was bent.<br>The living men of Priyamedha’s race have sun g exalting Indra with their lauds."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "274.1", "t": "Run forth to battle conquering the Vritras! thou Speedest to quell the foe like one exacting debts."}, {"st": "274.2", "t": "Thou Pavamana, didst beget the Sun with might, and rain in the supporting sky,<br>Hasting to us with plenty vivified with milk."}, {"st": "274.3", "t": "For, Soma, we rejoice ourselves in thee effused for great supremacy in fight;<br>Thou, Pavamana, enterest into mighty deeds."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "275.1", "t": "Flow forth, O Soma, flow thou onward, sweet to Indra’s,<br>Mitra’s, Pushan’s, Bhaga’s taste!"}, {"st": "275.2", "t": "So flow thou on as bright celestial juice, flow to the vast immortal dwelling-place!"}, {"st": "275.3", "t": "Let Indra drink, O Soma, of thy juice for wisdom, and all deities for strength!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "276.1", "t": "Even as the beams of Surya, urging men to speed, they issue forth together, gladdening as they flow,<br>These swift outpourings in long course of holy rites: no form save only Indra shows itself so pure."}, {"st": "276.2", "t": "The thought is deeply fixed, the savoury juice is shed; the tongue with joyous sound is stirring in the mouth:<br>And Pavamana, like the shout of those who press, the drop, rich in sweet juice, is flowing through the fleece."}, {"st": "276.3", "t": "The bull is bellowing; the cows are coming nigh: the Goddesses approach the God’s own resting-place.<br>Onward hath Soma pressed through the sheep’s fair bright fleece, and hath, as ‘twere, endued a garment newly washed."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Agni"}, {"st": "277.1", "t": "From the two fire-sticks have the men engendered, with thought, urged by the hand, the glorious Agni,<br>Far-seen, with pointed flame, Lord of the Homestead."}, {"st": "277.2", "t": "The Vasus set that Agni in the dwelling, fair to behold, for help, from every quarter:<br>Who, in the house for ever, must be honoured."}, {"st": "277.3", "t": "Shine thou before us, Agni, well-enkindled, with flame, most youthful God, that never fadeth!<br>To thee come goods and treasures all together."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Surya"}, {"st": "278.1", "t": "This spotted Bull hath come and sat before the mother in the east,<br>Advancing to his father heaven."}, {"st": "278.2", "t": "As expiration from his breath, his radiance penetrates within<br>The Bull shines out through all the sky."}, {"st": "278.3", "t": "Song is bestowed upon the Bird: it reigns supreme through thirty realms.<br>Throughout the days at break of morn."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "279.1", "t": "Chant we a hymn to Agni while we go to sacrifice, to him<br>Who hears us even from afar!"}, {"st": "279.2", "t": "Who from of old, in carnage, when the folk were gathered, hath preserved.<br>His household for the worshipper."}, {"st": "279.3", "t": "May that most blissful Agni guard our wealth and all ourfamily.<br>And keep us safe from pain and grief"}, {"st": "279.4", "t": "Yea, let men say, Agni is born, even he who slayeth Vritra, he,<br>Who winneth wealth in every fight!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Agni"}, {"st": "280.1", "t": "Harness, O Agni, O thou God, thy steeds which are most excellent!<br>The fleet ones bring the rapidly."}, {"st": "280.2", "t": "Come hither, bring the Gods to us to taste the sacrificial feast,<br>To drink the draught of Soma juice!"}, {"st": "280.3", "t": "O Agni of the Bharatas, flame splendid with unfading might<br>Shine forth and gleam, eternal one!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "281.1", "t": "Let him, as mortal, crave this speech for him who presses of the juice!<br>As Bhrigu’s sons chased Makha, so drive ye the niggard hound away."}, {"st": "281.2", "t": "The kinsman hath endued his robe even as a son is clasped in arms.<br>He went, as lover to a dame, to take his station suitor-like."}, {"st": "281.3", "t": "That hero who produces strength, he who hath propped both worlds apart,<br>Gold-hued, hath wrapped him in the sieve to settle, priest-like, in his place."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "282.1", "t": "Still, Indra, from all ancient time rivalless ever and companionless art thou:<br>Thou seekest friendship but in war."}, {"st": "282.2", "t": "Thou findest not the wealthy man to be thy friend: those scorn thee who are flown with wine.<br>What time thou thunderest and gatherest, then thou, even as a father, art invoked."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "283.1", "t": "A thousand and a hundred steeds are harnessed to thy golden car:<br>Yoked by devotion, Indra, let the long-maned bays bring thee to drink the Soma juice!"}, {"st": "283.2", "t": "Yoked to thy chariot wrought of gold, may thy two bays with, peacock tails.<br>Convey thee hither, steeds with their white backs, to quaff sweet juice that makes us eloquent!"}, {"st": "283.3", "t": "So drink, thou lover of the song, as the first drinker, of this juice.<br>This the outpouring of the savoury sap prepared is good and meet to gladden thee."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "284.1", "t": "Press ye and pour him, like a steed, laud-worthy, speeding through the region and the flood,<br>Who swims in water, dwells in wood"}, {"st": "284.2", "t": "The Steer with thousand streams who poureth out the rain, dear to the race of deities;<br>Who, born in Law, hath waxen mighty by the Law, King, God, and lofty ordinance."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Agni"}, {"st": "285.1", "t": "Served with oblation, kindled, bright, through love of song, may Agni, bent<br>On riches, smite the Vritras dead"}, {"st": "285.2", "t": "His father’s father, shining in his mother’s ever-lasting side,<br>Set on the seat of sacrifice!"}, {"st": "285.3", "t": "O active Jatavedas, bring devotion that wins progeny, Agni, that it may shine to heaven!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "286.1", "t": "Made pure by this man’s urgent zeal and impulse, the God hath with his juice the Gods pervaded.<br>Pressed, singing, to the sieve he goes, as passes the Hotar to enclosures holding cattle.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "286.2", "t": "Robed in fair raiment meet to wear in combat, a mighty Sage pronouncing invocations,<br>Roll onward to the press-boards as they cleanse thee, far-seeing at the feast of Gods and watchful!"}, {"st": "286.3", "t": "Dear, he is brightened on the fleecy summit, a prince among us, nobler than the noble.<br>Roar out as thou art purified, run forward! Do ye preserve us evermore with blessings!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra"}, {"st": "287.1", "t": "Come now and let us glorify pure Indra with pure Sama hymn!<br>Let milk-blent juice delight him made stronger with pure, pure songs of praise!"}, {"st": "287.2", "t": "O Indra, come thou pure to us, with pure assistance pure thyself!<br>Pure, send thou riches down to us, and, meet for Soma! pure, rejoice!"}, {"st": "287.3", "t": "O Indra, pure, vouchsafe us wealth, and, pure enrich the worshipper!<br>Pure, thou dost strike the Vritras dead, and strivest pure, to win the spoil."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Agni"}, {"st": "288.1", "t": "Eager for wealth we meditate Agni’s effectual laud to-day,<br>Laud of the God who touches heaven."}, {"st": "288.2", "t": "May Agni who is Hotar-priest among mankind accept our songs,<br>And worship the celestial folk!"}, {"st": "288.3", "t": "Thou, Agni, art spread widely forth, Priest dear and excellent through thee<br>Men make the sacrifice complete."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "289.1", "t": "To him, praiseworthy, sacred tones have sounded, Steer of the triple height, the life-bestower.<br>Dwelling in wood, like Varuna, a river, lavishing treasure, he distributes blessings."}, {"st": "289.2", "t": "Great conqueror, warrior girt, Lord of all heroes, flow on thy way as he who winneth riches:<br>With sharpened arms, with swift bow, never vanquished in battle, vanquishing in fight the foemen!"}, {"st": "289.3", "t": "Giving security, Lord of wide dominion, send us both heaven and earth with all their fulness!<br>Striving to win the Dawns, the light, the waters, and cattle, call to us abundant booty!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Indra"}, {"st": "290.1", "t": "O Indra, thou art far-renowned, impetuous Lord of power and might.<br>Alone, the never-conquered guardian of mankind, thou smitest down resistless foes."}, {"st": "290.2", "t": "As such we seek thee now, O Asura, the most wise, craving thy bounty as our share<br>Thy sheltering defence is like an ample cloak. So may thy favours reach to us."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Agni"}, {"st": "291.1", "t": "Thee have we chosen, skilfullest in sacrifice, immortal, Priest, among the Gods,<br>Best finisher of this holy rite:"}, {"st": "291.2", "t": "The Waters’ Child, the blessed brightly-shining one, Agni whose, light is excellent.<br>May he by sacrifice win us in heaven the grace of Mitra, Varuna, and the Floods!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Agni"}, {"st": "292.1", "t": "Lord of all food is he, the man whom thou protectest in the fight,<br>Agni, and urgest to the fray."}, {"st": "292.2", "t": "Him, whosoever he may be, no one may vanquish, mighty one!<br>Nay, very glorious wealth is his."}, {"st": "292.3", "t": "May he who dwells with all mankind conquer in fight with steeds of war,<br>With sages may he win the spoil."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "293.1", "t": "Ten sisters, pouring out the rain together, the sage’s quickly<br>moving thoughts, adorn him.<br>Hither hath run the gold-hued Child of Surya, and reached the vat like a fleet vigorous courser."}, {"st": "293.2", "t": "Even as a youngling shouting with his mothers, the bounteous Steer hath flowed along with waters.<br>As youth to damsel, so with milk he hastens on to the settled meeting-place, the beaker."}, {"st": "293.3", "t": "Yea, swollen is the udder of the milch-cow; thither in streams. comes very sapient Indu.<br>The kine make ready, as with new-washed treasures, the head and chief with milk within the vessels."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Indra"}, {"st": "294.1", "t": "Drink, Indra, of the savoury juice, and cheer thee, with our milky draught!<br>Be, for our weal, our friend and sharer of the feast, and let thy wisdom guard us well!"}, {"st": "294.2", "t": "In thy kind grace and favour may we still be strong: cast us not down before the foe!<br>With manifold assistance guard and succour us, and stablish us in thy good-will!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "295.1", "t": "The three-times seven milch-kine in the loftiest heaven have for this Soma poured the genuine milky draught.<br>Four other beauteous creatures hath he made for his adornment when he waxed in strength through holy rites."}, {"st": "295.2", "t": "Enjoying lovely Amrit by his wisdom he divided, each apart from other, earth and heaven.<br>He gladly wrapped himself in the most lucid floods, when through their glory they-found the God’s resting-place."}, {"st": "295.3", "t": "May those his brilliant rays be ever free from death, inviolate for both classes of created things — <br>Rays wherewith powers of men and Gods are purified! Yea, even for this have sages welcomed him as King."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "296.1", "t": "Lauded with song, to feast him, flow to Vayu, flow purified to Varuna and Mitra!<br>Flow to the song inspiring car-borne hero, to mighty Indra, him who wields the thunder!"}, {"st": "296.2", "t": "Pour on us garments that shall clothe us meetly, send, purified, milch-kine, abundant yielders!<br>God Soma, send us cbariot-drawing horses that they may bring us treasures bright and golden!"}, {"st": "296.3", "t": "Send to us in a stream celestial riches, send us when thou art cleansed, what earth containeth,<br>So that thereby we may acquire possessions and Rishihood in Jamadagni’s manner!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Indra"}, {"st": "297.1", "t": "When thou, unequalled Maghavan, wast born to smite the Vritras dead,<br>Thou spreadest out the spacious earth and didst support and prop the heavens."}, {"st": "297.2", "t": "Then was the sacrifice produced for thee, the laud, and song of joy.<br>In might thou art above this All, all that now is and yet shall be."}, {"st": "297.3", "t": "Raw kine thou filledst with ripe milk. Thou madest Surya rise to heaven.<br>Heat him as milk is heated with pure Sdma hymns, great joy to him who loves the song!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Indra"}, {"st": "298.1", "t": "Rejoice: thy glory hath been quaffed, Lord of bay steeds! as ‘twere the bowl’s enlivening mead.<br>Thine, Steer, is Indu, Steer, the Strong, best winner of a thousand spoils."}, {"st": "298.2", "t": "Let our strong drink, most excellent, exhilarating, come to thee,<br>Victorious, Indra! bringing gain, immortal conquering in fight!"}, {"st": "298.3", "t": "Thou, hero, winner of the spoil, urgest to speed the car of man.<br>Burn, like a vessel with the flame, the riteless Dasyu, conqueror!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "299.1", "t": "Pour down the rain upon us, pour a wave of waters from the sky.<br>And plenteous store of wholesome food!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [100, 99]]}, {"st": "299.2", "t": "Flow onward with that stream of thine, whereby the cows have come to us.<br>The kine of strangers to our home."}, {"st": "299.3", "t": "Dearest to Gods in sacred rites, pour on us fatness with thy stream,<br>Pour down on us a flood of rain!"}, {"st": "299.4", "t": "To give as vigour, with thy stream run through the fleecy straining-cloth!<br>For verily the Gods will hear."}, {"st": "299.5", "t": "Onward hath Pavamana flowed and beaten off the Rakshasas.<br>Flashing out splendour as of old."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "300.1", "t": "Bring forth oblations to the God who knoweth all, who fain would drink.<br>The wanderer, lagging not behind the hero, coming nigh with, speed!"}, {"st": "300.2", "t": "With Somas go ye nigh to him chief drinker of the Soma’s. juice:<br>With beakers to the impetuous God, to Indra with the flowing, drops!"}, {"st": "300.3", "t": "What time with Somas, with the drops effused,, ye come beforethe God,<br>Full wise, he knows the hope of each, and, bold one strikes this. foe and that."}, {"st": "300.4", "t": "To him, Adhvaryu! yea, to him give offerings of the juiceexpressed!<br>Will he not keep us safely from the spiteful curse of each, presumptuous high-born foe?"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "301.1", "t": "Sing ye a song to Soma brown of hue, of independent might,<br>The Red, who reaches up to heaven!"}, {"st": "301.2", "t": "Purify Soma when effused with stones which hands move rapidly,<br>And pour the sweet milk in the meath."}, {"st": "301.3", "t": "With humble homage draw ye nigh; blend the libation with the curds:<br>To Indra offer Indu up"}, {"st": "301.4", "t": "Soma, foe-queller, strong and swift, doing the will of Gods, pour forth,<br>Prosperity upon our kine"}, {"st": "301.5", "t": "Heart-knower, Sovran of the heart, thou art effused, O Soma, Tthat,<br>Indra. may drink thee and rejoice."}, {"st": "301.6", "t": "O Soma Pavamana, give us riches and heroic strength, Indu, with Indra. our ally!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Surya, thou mountest up to meet the hero famous for his wealth,<br>Who hurls the bolt and works for men;<br>2. Him who with might of both his arms broke nine-and-ninety castles down,<br>Slew Vritra and smote Ahi dead.<br>3. This Indra is our gracious friend. He sends, like a full-streaming cow,<br>Riches in horses, kine, and corn."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Surya"}, {"st": "303.1", "t": "May the bright God drink glorious Soma-mingled meath, giving<br>the sacrifices lord unbroken life<br>He who, wind-urged, in person guards our offspring well, nourishes them with food and shines o’er many a land."}, {"st": "303.2", "t": "Radiant, as high Truth, cherished, best at winning strength, Truth based upon the statute that supports the heavens,<br>He rose, a light that kills Vritras and enemies, best slayer of the Dasyus, Asuras, and foes."}, {"st": "303.3", "t": "This light, the best of lights, supreme, all conquering, winner of riches, is exalted with high laud.<br>All-lighting, radiant, mighty as the Sun to see, he spreadeth wide unshaken victory and strength."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Indra"}, {"st": "304.1", "t": "O Indra, give us wisdom as a sire gives wisdom to his sons,<br>Guide us, O much-invoked, in this our way: may we still live and look upon the light!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "304.2", "t": "Grant that no mighty foes, unknown, malevolent unhallowed, tread us to the ground!<br>With thine assistance, hero, may we pass through all the waters that are rushing down!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Indra"}, {"st": "305.1", "t": "Protect us, Indra, each to-day, each to morrow, and each following day!<br>Through all the days shalt thou, Lord of the brave, preserve our singers both by day and night!"}, {"st": "305.2", "t": "A crushing warrior, passing rich, is Maghavan, endowed with all heroic strength.<br>Thine arms, O Satakratu, are exceeding strong, those arms,<br>which grasp the thunderbolt."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Sarasvan"}, {"st": "306.1", "t": "We call upon Sarasvan as unmarried men who long for wives,<br>As bounteous men who yearn for sons."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Sarasvati"}, {"st": "307.1", "t": "Yea, she most dear amid dear streams-seven-sistered, loved with foundest love.<br>Sarasvati, hath earned our praise."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Svitar. Brahmapaspati. Agni"}, {"st": "308.1", "t": "May we attain that excellent glory of Savitar the God: So may he stimulate our prayers!"}, {"st": "308.2", "t": "O Brahmanaspati, make thou Kakshivan Ausija a loud Chanter of flowing Soma juice!"}, {"st": "308.3", "t": "Agni, thou pourest life: send down upon us food and vigorous strength;<br>Drive thou misfortune far away!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Mitra-Varuva"}, {"st": "309.1", "t": "So help ye us to riches, great celestial and terrestrial wealth<br>Vast is your sway among the Gods!"}, {"st": "309.2", "t": "Carefully tending Law with law they have attained their vigorous might:<br>Both Gods, devoid of guile, wax strong."}, {"st": "309.3", "t": "With rainy skies and streaming floods, Lords of the food that falls in dew,<br>A lofty seat have they attained."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Indra"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. They who stand round him as he moves harness the bright, the ruddy steed:<br>The lights shining in the sky.<br>2. On both sides to the car they yoke the two bay coursers dear to him,<br>Brown, bold, who bear the hero on.<br>3. Thou, making light where no light was, and form, O men where form was not,<br>Wast born together with the Dawns."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "311.1", "t": "For thee this Soma is effused. O Indra: drink of this juice; for thee the stream is flowing — <br>Soma, which thou thyself hast made and chosen, even Indu for thy special drink to cheer thee!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [56, 55]]}, {"st": "311.2", "t": "Like a capacious car hath it been harnessed, the mighty, to acquire abundant treasures.<br>Then in the sacrifice they shouted lauding all triumphs won by Nahus in the battle."}, {"st": "311.3", "t": "Flow onward like the potent band of Maruts, like that celestial host which none revileth!<br>Quickly be gracious unto us like waters, like sacrifice victorious, thousand-fashioned!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Agni"}, {"st": "312.1", "t": "O Agni, thou hast been ordained Hotar of every sacrifice, By Gods, among the race of men.<br>So with sweet-sounding tongues for us sacrifice nobly in this rite:<br>Bring thou the Gods and worship them"}, {"st": "312.3", "t": "For, as disposer, Agni, God, most wise in sacrifices, thou Knowest straightway the roads and paths."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Agni"}, {"st": "313.1", "t": "Immortal, Hotar-priest, and God, with wondrous power heleads the way,<br>Urging the congregations on."}, {"st": "313.2", "t": "Strong, he is set on deeds of strength. He is led forth in holy rites,<br>Sage who completes the sacrifice."}, {"st": "313.3", "t": "Excellent, he was made by thought. The germ of beings have gained.<br>Yea, and the Sire of active power."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Agni"}, {"st": "314.1", "t": "Pour on the juice the heated milk which hasteneth to heaven and. earth;<br>Bestow the liquid on the Bull!"}, {"st": "314.2", "t": "These know their own abiding-place: like calves beside themother cows,<br>They come together with their kin."}, {"st": "314.3", "t": "Devouring in their greedy jaws, they make sustaining food irb heaven,<br>For Indra, Agni, homage, light."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Indra"}, {"st": "315.1", "t": "In all the worlds That was the best and highest whence sprang the mighty one, of splendid valour,<br>As soon as he is born he smites his foemen, he in whom all<br>who lend him aid are joyful foe"}, {"st": "315.2", "t": "Grown mighty in his strength, of ample vigour, he as a strikes fear into the Dasa,<br>Eager to win the breathing and the breathless. All sang thy praise at banquet and oblation."}, {"st": "315.3", "t": "All concentrate on thee their mental vigour, what time these, once or twice, are thine assistants.<br>Blend what is sweeter than the sweet with sweetness: win quickly with our meath that meath in battle."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Indra"}, {"st": "316.1", "t": "At the Trikadrukas the great and strong enjoyed the barley-brew. With Vishnu did he drink the pressed-out Soma juice, even as he would.<br>That hath so heightened him the great, the wide, to do his mighty work. So may the God attend the God, true Indu Indra who is true!"}, {"st": "316.2", "t": "Brought forth together with wisdom and potent strength thou grewest great: with hero deeds subduing the malevolent, most swift in act;<br>Giving prosperity and lovely wealth to him who praiseth thee.<br>So may the God attend the God, true Indu Indra who is true!"}, {"st": "316.3", "t": "So he resplendent in the battle overcame Krivi by might. He with his majesty bath filled the earth and heaven, and waxen strong.<br>One share of the libation bath he swallowed down: one share he left. Enlighten us! So may the God attend the God, true Indu Indra who is true!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Indra"}, {"st": "317.1", "t": "Praise, even as he is known, with song Indra the guardian of the kine,<br>The Son of Truth, Lord of the brave,"}, {"st": "317.2", "t": "Hither have his bay steeds been sent, red steeds are on the sacred grass<br>Where we in concert sing our songs."}, {"st": "317.3", "t": "For Indra, thunder-armed, the kine have yielded mingled milk and meath,<br>What time he found them in the vault."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "318.1", "t": "Draw near unto our Indra who must be invoked in every fight!<br>Come, thou most mighty Vritra-slayer, meet for praise come to<br>libations and to hymns."}, {"st": "318.2", "t": "Thou art the best of all in sending bounteous gifts, true art thou, lordly in thine act.<br>We claim alliance with the very glorious one, yea, with the<br>mighty Son of Strength.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [48, 47], [68, 66]]}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. They have drained forth from out the great depth of the sky the old divine primeval milk that claims the laud:<br>They lifted up their voice to Indra at his birth.<br>2. Then, beautifully radiant, certain heavenly ones proclaimed their kinship with him as they looked thereon:<br>Savitar opens, as it were, the fold of heaven.<br>3. And now that thou, O Pavamana, art above this earth and heaven and all existence in thy might,<br>Thou shinest like a bull supreme among the herd."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Agni"}, {"st": "320.1", "t": "O Agni, graciously announce this our good fortune to the Gods,<br>And this our newest hymn of praise!"}, {"st": "320.2", "t": "Thou dealest gifts, resplendent one! nigh, as with wave of Sindhu, thou<br>Swift strearnest to the worshipper."}, {"st": "320.3", "t": "Give us a share of wealth most high, a share of wealth most near to us,<br>A share of wealth that is between."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "321.1", "t": "I from my Father have obtained deep knowledge of eternal Law;<br>I was born like unto the Sun."}, {"st": "321.2", "t": "After the ancient manner I, like Kanva, beautify my songs,<br>And Indra’s self gains power thereby."}, {"st": "321.3", "t": "Whatever gishis have not praised thee, Indra, or have praised thee, wax<br>Mighty indeed when praised by me!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Agni"}, {"st": "322.1", "t": "Agni, produced by strength, do thou with all thy fires accept our prayer:<br>With those that are with Gods, with those that are with men exalt our songs!"}, {"st": "322.2", "t": "Forth come to us with all his fires that Agni, whose the mighty are,<br>Come, fully girt about with wealth for us and for our kith and kin!"}, {"st": "322.3", "t": "Do thou, O Agni, with thy fires strengthen our prayer and sacrifices:<br>Incite them to bestow their wealth to aid our service of the Gods!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "323.1", "t": "Some, the men of old whose grass was trimmed addressed the hymn to thee for mighty strength and for renown:<br>So, hero, urge us onward to heroic power’"}, {"st": "323.2", "t": "All round about hast thou with glory pierced for us as ‘twere a never-failing well for men to drink,<br>Borne on thy way as ‘twere in fragments from both arms."}, {"st": "323.3", "t": "Thou didst produce him, deathless one! for mortal man, for maintenance of Law and lovely Amrita:<br>Thou evermore hast moved making wealth flow to us."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Indra"}, {"st": "324.1", "t": "Pour out the drops f or Indra; let him drink the meath of Soma Juice!<br>He through his majesty sends forth his bounteous gifts."}, {"st": "324.2", "t": "I spake to the bay coursers’ Lord, to him who grants the boon. of wealth:<br>Now hear the son of Asva as he praises thee?"}, {"st": "324.3", "t": "Never was any hero born before thee mightier than thou:<br>None certainly like thee in riches and in praise."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra"}, {"st": "325.1", "t": "Thou wishest for thy kine a bull, lord of thy cows whom none may kill,<br>For those who long for his approach, for those who turn away from him."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Agni"}, {"st": "326.1", "t": "The God who giveth wealth accept the full libation poured to him!<br>Pour ye it out, then fill the vessel full again, for so the God regardeth you!"}, {"st": "326.2", "t": "The Gods made him the Hotar-priest of sacrifice, oblationbearer, passing wise.<br>Agni gives wealth and valour to the worshipper, to man who offers up his gifts."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Agni"}, {"st": "327.1", "t": "He hath appeared, best prosperer, in whom men lay their holy acts:<br>So may our songs of praise come nigh to Agni who was born to give the Arya strength."}, {"st": "327.2", "t": "Him before whom the people shrink when he performs his glorious deeds,<br>Him who wins thousands at the sacrifice, himself, that Agni, reverence with songs!"}, {"st": "327.3", "t": "Agni of Divoddsa, God, comes forth like Indra in his might.<br>Rapidly hath he moved along his mother earth; he stands in high heaven’s dwelling-place."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Agni"}, {"st": "328.1", "t": "Agni, thou pourest life: send down upon us food and vigorous strength:<br>Drive thou misfortune far away!"}, {"st": "328.2", "t": "Agni is Pavamana, Sage, Chief Priest of all the fivefold tribes; To him whose wealth is great we pray."}, {"st": "328.3", "t": "Skilled in thy task, O Agni, pour splendour with hero strength on us, Granting me wealth that nourishes!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Agni"}, {"st": "329.1", "t": "O Agni, holy and divine with splendour and thy pleasant tongue. Bring thou the Gods and worship them!"}, {"st": "329.2", "t": "We pray thee bathed in butter, O bright-rayed! who lookest on the sun, Bring the Gods hither to the feast!"}, {"st": "329.3", "t": "Sage, we have kindled thee, the bright, the feaster on oblation, thee, O Agni, great in sacrifice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Agni"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Adorable in all our prayers, favour us, Agni, with thine aid.<br>What time the psalm is chanted forth!<br>2. Bring to us ever-conquering wealth, wealth, Agni, worthy of our choice,<br>Invincible in all our frays!<br>3. Grant us, O Agni, through thy grace wealth to support us evermore,<br>Thy favour so that we may live!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Agni"}, {"st": "331.1", "t": "Let songs of ours speed Agni forth like a fleet courser in the race,<br>And we will win each prize through him"}, {"st": "331.2", "t": "Agni! the host whereby we gain kine for ourselves with help from thee,-<br>That send us for the gain of wealth!"}, {"st": "331.3", "t": "O Agni, bring us wealth secure, vast wealth in horses and in kine:<br>Oil thou the socket, turn the wheel!"}, {"st": "331.4", "t": "O Agni, thou hast made the Sun, the eternal star, to mount the sky,<br>Giving the boon of light to men."}, {"st": "331.5", "t": "Thou, Agni, art the people’s light, best, dearest, seated in thy shrine<br>Watch for the singer, give him life!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Agni"}, {"st": "332.1", "t": "Agni is head and height of heaven, the master of the earth is he:<br>He quickeneth the waters’ seed."}, {"st": "332.2", "t": "Yea, Agni, thou as Lord of light rulest o’er choicest gifts may I,<br>Thy singer, find defence in thee"}, {"st": "332.3", "t": "Upward, O Agni, rise thy flames, pure and resplendent, blazing high,<br>Thy lustres, fair effulgences."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "333.1", "t": "Who, Agni, is thy kin, of men? who honours thee with sacrifice?<br>On whom dependent? who art thou?"}, {"st": "333.2", "t": "The kinsman, Agni! of mankind, their well-beiaved friend art thou,<br>A friend whom friends may supplicate."}, {"st": "333.3", "t": "Bring Mitra, Varukia, bring the Gods hither to. our great sacrifice:<br>Bring them, O Agni, to thine home"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Agni"}, {"st": "334.1", "t": "Meet to be worshipped and implored, showing in beauty through the gloom,<br>Agni, the strong, is kindled well."}, {"st": "334.2", "t": "Strong Agni is enkindled well, even as the horse that brings the Gods:<br>Men with oblations pray to him."}, {"st": "334.3", "t": "We will enkindle thee, the strong, we, hero! who axe strong ourselves,"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Agni"}, {"st": "335.1", "t": "Thy mighty flames, O Agni, when thou art enkindled, rise on high,<br>Thy bright flames, thou refulgent one"}, {"st": "335.2", "t": "Beloved! let my ladies full of sacred oil come nigh to thee.<br>Agni, accept our offerings!"}, {"st": "335.3", "t": "I pray to Agni — may he hear! — the Hotar with sweet tones, the Priest,<br>Wondrously splendid, rich in light,"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Agni"}, {"st": "336.1", "t": "O King, the potent and terrific envoy, kindled for strength, is<br>manifest in beauty.<br>He shines, observant, with his lofty splendour; chasing black night he comes with white-rayed morning."}, {"st": "336.2", "t": "Having o’ercome the glimmering Black with beauty, and bringing forth the Dame, the great Sire’s daughter,<br>Holding aloft the radiant lights of Surya, as messenger of heaven he shines with treasures."}, {"st": "336.3", "t": "Attendant on the blessed Dame the blessed hath come: the lover followeth his sister.<br>Agni, far-spreading with conspicuous lustre, hath covered night with whitely-shining garments."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Agni"}, {"st": "337.1", "t": "What is the praise wherewith, O God, Angiras, Agni, Son of Strength,<br>We, after thine own wish and thought,"}, {"st": "337.2", "t": "May serve thee, O thou Child of Power, and with what sacrifice’s plan?<br>What reverent word shall I speak here?"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Agni"}, {"st": "338.1", "t": "Agni, come hither with thy fires; we choose thee as our Hotar; let<br>The proffered ladle filled with offerings balm thee, best of priests, to sit on sacred grass!"}, {"st": "338.2", "t": "For unto thee, O Angiras, O Son of Strength, move ladles in the sacrifice.<br>We pray to Agni, Child of Force, whose locks drop oil, foremost in sacrificial rites."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Agni"}, {"st": "339.1", "t": "Let our songs come anear to him beauteous and bright with piercing flame,<br>Our sacrifices with our homage unto him much-lauded, very rich, for help:"}, {"st": "339.2", "t": "To Agni Jatavedas, to the Son of Strength, that he may give us precious gifts,"}, {"st": "339.3", "t": "Immortal, from of old Priest among mortal men, whose tones are sweetest in the house!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Agni"}, {"st": "340.1", "t": "Invincible is Agni, he who goes before the tribes of men,<br>A chariot swift and ever new."}, {"st": "340.2", "t": "By bringing offerings unto him the mortal worshipper obtains<br>A home from him whose light is pure."}, {"st": "340.3", "t": "Inviolable power of Gods, subduing all his enemies, Agni is mightiest in fame."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Agni"}, {"st": "341.1", "t": "May Agni, worshipped, bring us bliss: may the gift, blessed one! and sacrifice bring bliss,<br>Yea, may our eulogies bring bliss"}, {"st": "341.2", "t": "Show forth the mind that brings success in war with fiends, wherewith thou conquerest in fight!<br>Bring down the many firm hopes of our enemies, and for thy victory let us win!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Agni"}, {"st": "342.1", "t": "O Agni thou who art the Lord of wealth in kine, thou Son of Strength,<br>Bestow on us, O Jatavedas, high renown"}, {"st": "342.2", "t": "He, Agni, kindled, good and wise, must be entreated with a. song;<br>Shine, thou of many forms, shine thou with wealth on us"}, {"st": "342.3", "t": "And, Agni, shining of thyself by night and when the morning breaks,<br>Burn, thou whose teeth are sharp, against the Rakshasas"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Agni"}, {"st": "343.1", "t": "Exerting all our strength with thoughts of power we glorify in speech,<br>Agni, your dear familiar friend, the darling guest of every house:"}, {"st": "343.2", "t": "Whom, served with sacrificial oil, like Mitra, men presenting gifts,<br>Glorify with their songs of praise"}, {"st": "343.3", "t": "Much-lauded Jatavedas, him who sends oblations up to heaven,<br>Prepared in service of the Gods."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Agni"}, {"st": "344.1", "t": "Agni, inflamed with fuel, in my song I sing, pure bright, and stedfast set in front at sacrifice.<br>Wise Jatavedas we implore with prayers for grace, the Sage, the Hotar-priest, bounteous, and void of guile."}, {"st": "344.2", "t": "Men, Agni, in each age, have made thee, deathless one, their envoy, offering-bearer, guard adorable.<br>With reverence Gods and mortals have established thee as everwatchful and almighty household Lord."}, {"st": "344.3", "t": "Though, Agni ordering the works and ways of both, as envoy of the Gods traversest both the realms.<br>When we lay claim to thy regard and gracious care, be thou to us a th rice-protecting friendly guard?"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Agni"}, {"st": "345.1", "t": "Still turning to their aim in thee the sacrificer’s sister hymns<br>Have come to thee before the wind."}, {"st": "345.2", "t": "Even the waters find their place in him whose three fold sacred grass<br>Is spread unbound, unlimited."}, {"st": "345.3", "t": "The station of the bounteous God, by his unconquerable aid,<br>Hath a fair aspect like the Sun."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Indra"}, {"st": "346.1", "t": "Men with their lauds are urging thee, Indra, to drink the Soma first.<br>The Ribhus in accord have lifted up their voice, and Rudras sung thee as the first."}, {"st": "346.2", "t": "Indra, at sacrifice, increased his manly strength, in the wild rapture of this juice:<br>And living men to-day, even as of old, sing forth their praises to his majesty."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Indra-Agni"}, {"st": "347.1", "t": "Indra and Agni! singers skilled in melody, with lauds, hymn you:<br>I choose you both to bring me food."}, {"st": "347.2", "t": "Indra and Agni! ye shook down, together, with one mighty deed, The ninety forts which Dasas held.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [57, 56]]}, {"st": "347.3", "t": "To Indra and to Agni prayers go forward from the holy task, Along the path of sacred Law."}, {"st": "347.4", "t": "Indra and Agni, powers are yours, yours are oblations ano abodes: Good is your zealous energy."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "348.1", "t": "Indra, with all thy saving helps assist us, Lord of power and might!<br>For after thee we follow even as glorious bliss, thee, hero, finder-out of wealth!"}, {"st": "348.2", "t": "Increaser of our steeds and multiplying kine, a golden well, G God, art thou,<br>For no one may impair the gift laid up in thee. Bring me whatever thing I ask!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "349.1", "t": "For thou — come to the worshipper! — wilt find great wealth to make us rich.<br>Fill thyself full, O Maghavan, for gain of kine, full, Indra, for the gain of steeds!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [141, 142]]}, {"st": "349.2", "t": "Thou as thy gift bestowest many hundred herds, yea, many thou-sands dost thou give.<br>With singers’ hymns have we brought the fortrender near, singing to Indra for his grace."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Agni"}, {"st": "350.1", "t": "To him who dealeth out all wealth, the sweet-toned Hotar-priest of men,<br>To him, like the first vessels filled with savoury juice, to Agni let the lauds go forth!"}, {"st": "350.2", "t": "Votaries, bounteous givers, deck him with their songs, even as the steed who draws the car.<br>To both, strong Lord of men! to kith and kin convey the bounties of our wealthy lords!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Varuna"}, {"st": "351.1", "t": "Hear this my call, O Varuna, and show thy gracious love today:<br>Desiring help I long for thee!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Indra"}, {"st": "352.1", "t": "O Hero, with what aid dost thou delight us, with what succour bring,<br>Riches to those who worship thee?"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Indra"}, {"st": "353.1", "t": "Indra, for service of the Gods, Indra while sacrifice proceeds,<br>Indra, as worshippers, in battle-shock we call, Indra that we may win the spoil."}, {"st": "353.2", "t": "With might hath Indra spread out heaven and earth, with power hath indra lighten up the Sun. In Indra are all creatures closely held; in him meet the distilling Soma-drops."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Visvakarman"}, {"st": "354.1", "t": "Bring, Visvakarman strengthened by oblation, thyself, thy body-’tis thine own-for worship<br>Let other men around us live in folly here let us have’, a rich and liberal patron!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "355.1", "t": "With this his golden splendour purifying him, he with his own allies subdues all enemies. as Sura with his own allies.<br>Cleansing himself with stream of juice he shines forth yellow-hued and red, when with his praisers he encompasses all forms, with praisers having seven mouths."}, {"st": "355.2", "t": "He moves intelligent directed to the east. The every beauteous car rivals the beams of light, the beautiful celestial car.<br>Hymns, lauding manly valour, came inciting Indra to success, that ye may be unconquered, both thy bolt and thou, both be unconquered in the war."}, {"st": "355.3", "t": "That treasure of the Panis thou discoveredst. Thou with the Mothers deckest thee in thine abode, with, songs of worship in thine home.<br>As ‘twere from far away is heard the psalm where hymns resound in joy. He, with the triple Dames red-hued, hath won life-power, he, gleaming, hath won vital strength."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Pusan"}, {"st": "356.1", "t": "Yea, cause our hymn to gain for us cattle and steeds and store of wealth,<br>That it may help us manfully!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Maruts"}, {"st": "357.1", "t": "Heroes of real strength, ye mark either the sweat of him who toils,<br>Or his desire who supplicates."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Visvedevas"}, {"st": "358.1", "t": "The Sons of immortality shall listen to our songs of praise,<br>And be exceeding kind to us."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Heaven and Earth"}, {"st": "359.1", "t": "To both of you, O Heaven and Earth, we bring our lofty song of praise,<br>Pure pair! to glorify you both."}, {"st": "359.2", "t": "Ye sanctify each other’s form by your own proper strength ye rule:<br>Further the sacrifice evermore!"}, {"st": "359.3", "t": "Promoting and fulfilling, ye, mighty ones, perfect Mitra’s law:<br>Ye sit around our sacrifice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Indra"}, {"st": "360.1", "t": "This is thine own. Thou drawest near, as turns a pigeon to his mate:<br>Thou carest, too, for this our prayer."}, {"st": "360.2", "t": "O hero, Lord of bounties, praised in hymns, may glorious fame and might<br>Be his who sings the laud to thee"}, {"st": "360.3", "t": "Lord of a Hundred Powers, rise up to be our succour in this fight:<br>In other fights let us agree"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Oblations"}, {"st": "361.1", "t": "Ye cows, protect the fount: the two mighty ones bless the sacrifice.<br>The handles twain are wrought of gold."}, {"st": "361.2", "t": "The pressing-stones are set at work: the meath is poured into the tank<br>At the out-shedding of the fount."}, {"st": "361.3", "t": "With reverence they drain the fount that circles with its wheel above.<br>Exhaustless, with the mouth below."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Indra"}, {"st": "362.1", "t": "Let us not tire or be afraid with thee, the mighty, for our friend!<br>May we see Turvasa and Yadu! thy great deed, O hero, must be glorified."}, {"st": "362.2", "t": "On his left hip the hero hath reclined himself: the proffered feast offends him not.<br>The milk is blended with the honey of the bee: quickly come hither, haste, and drink!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Indra"}, {"st": "363.1", "t": "May these my songs of praise exalt thee, Lord, who hast abundant wealth!<br>Men skilled in holy hymns, pure, with the hues of fire, have<br>sung them with their lauds to thee."}, {"st": "363.2", "t": "He, when a thousand Rishis have enhanced his might, hath like an ocean spread himself.<br>His majesty is praised as true at solemn rites, his power where holy singers rule."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Indra"}, {"st": "364.1", "t": "Good Lord of wealth is he to whom all Aryas, Dasas here belong.<br>Directly unto thee, the pious Rusama Paviru, is that wealth brought nigh."}, {"st": "364.2", "t": "In zealous haste the singers have sung forth a song distilling<br>fatness, rich in sweets.<br>Riches have spread among us and heroic strength, with us are flowing Soma-drops."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 20 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "365.1", "t": "Flow to us, Indu, very strong, effused, with wealth of kine and steeds,<br>And do thou lay above the milk thy radiant hue"}, {"st": "365.2", "t": "Lord of the tawny, Indu, thou who art the Gods’ most special food,<br>As friend to friend, for splendour be thou good to men!"}, {"st": "365.3", "t": "Drive utterly, far away from us each godless, each voracious; foe;<br>O Indu, overcome and drive the false afar!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 21 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "366.1", "t": "They balm him, balm him over, balm him thoroughly, caress. the mighty strength and balm it with the meath.<br>They seize the flying Steer at the stream’s breathing place cleansing with gold they grasp the animal herein."}, {"st": "366.2", "t": "Sing forth to Pavamana skilled in holy song! the juice is flowing onward like a mighty stream.<br>He glideth like a serpent from his ancient skin, and like a. playful horse the tawny Steer hath run."}, {"st": "366.3", "t": "Dweller in floods, King, foremost, he displays his might, set among living things as measure of days.<br>Distilling oil he flows, fair, billowy, golden-hued, borne on car of light, sharing on home with wealth."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "367.1", "t": "With all thy fires, O Agni, find pleasure in this our sacrifice,<br>And this our speech, O son of Strength!"}, {"st": "367.2", "t": "Whate’er, in this perpetual course, we sacrifice to God and God,<br>That gift is offered but in thee."}, {"st": "367.3", "t": "May he be our beloved King and excellent sweet-toned Hotar may<br>We with bright fires be dear to him"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "368.1", "t": "For you from every side we call Indra away from other men<br>Ours, and none others, may he be!"}, {"st": "368.2", "t": "Unclose, our manly hero! thou for ever bounteous, yonder cloud<br>For us, thou irresistible"}, {"st": "368.3", "t": "As the strong bull leads on the herds, he stirs the people with his might,<br>The ruler irresistible."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Agni"}, {"st": "369.1", "t": "Wonderful, with thy saving help, send us thy bounties, gracious Lord!<br>Thou art the charioteer, Agni, of earthly wealth: find rest and safety for our seed!"}, {"st": "369.2", "t": "Prosper our kith and kin with thy protecting powers inviolate, never negligent!<br>Keep far from us, O Agni, all celestial wrath. and wickedness of godless men!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Vishnu"}, {"st": "370.1", "t": "What, Vishnu, is the name that thou proclaimest when thou declaredst, I am Sipivishta?<br>Hide not this form from us, nor keep it secret, since thou didst wear another shape in battle."}, {"st": "370.2", "t": "This offering to-day, O Sipivishta, I, skilled in rules, extol, to thee the noble.<br>Yea, I, the poor and weak, praise thee, the mighty, who dwellest in the realm beyond this region."}, {"st": "370.3", "t": "O Vishnu, unto thee my lips cry Vashat! Let this mine offering, Sipivishta, please thee!<br>May these my songs of eulogy exalt thee! Do ye preserve us evermore with blessings!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Vayu, Indra and Vayu"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Vayu, the bright is offered thee, best of the meath, at morning rites.<br>Come thou to drink the Soma juice, God, longed for on thy team-drawn car!<br>2. O Vayu, thou and Indra are meet drinkers of these Soma draughts,<br>For unto you the drops proceed like waters gathering to the vale.<br>3. Vayu and Indra, mighty twain, borne on one chariot, Lords of strength,<br>Come to ouf succour with your steeds, that ye may drink the<br>Soma juice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "372.1", "t": "Then thou, made beautiful by night, enterest into mighty deeds,<br>When prayers impel the golden-hued to hasten from Vivasvan’s place."}, {"st": "372.2", "t": "We cleanse this gladdening drink of his, the juice which Indra chiefly drinks,<br>That which kine took into their mouths, oF old, and princes take it now."}, {"st": "372.3", "t": "Thy with the ancient psalm have sung to him as he is purified,<br>And sacred songs which bear the Dames of Gods have supplicated him."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Agni"}, {"st": "373.1", "t": "With homage will I reverence thee, Agni, like a long-tailed steed,<br>Imperial Lord of holy rites."}, {"st": "373.2", "t": "May the far-striding Son of Strength, our friend who brings felicity,<br>Who pours his gifts like rain, be ours"}, {"st": "373.3", "t": "From near and far away do thou, the everlasting, evermore<br>Protect us from the sinful man!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Indra"}, {"st": "374.1", "t": "Thou in thy battles, Indra, art subduer of all hostile bands.<br>Father art thou, all-conquering, cancelling the curse, thou victor of the vanquisher!"}, {"st": "374.2", "t": "The earth and heaven cling close to thy victorious might, as sire and mother to their child.<br>When thou attackest Vritra, all the hostile bands shrink and faint, Indra, at thy wrath."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra"}, {"st": "375.1", "t": "The sacrifice made Indra great when he unrolled the earth, and made<br>Himself a diadem in heaven."}, {"st": "375.2", "t": "In Soma’s ecstasy Indra spread the firmament and realms of light,<br>When he cleft Vala limb from limb."}, {"st": "375.3", "t": "Showing the hidden, he drave forth the cows for the Angirasas,<br>And Vala he cast headlong down."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Indra"}, {"st": "376.1", "t": "Thou speedest down to succour us this-ever-conquering God of yours,<br>Him who is drawn to all our songs;<br>2, The warrior whom none may wound, the Soma-drinker ne’er o’erthrown,<br>The chieftain of resistless might."}, {"st": "376.3", "t": "O Indra, send us riches, thou omniscient, worthy of our hymns:<br>Help us in the decisive fray!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Indra"}, {"st": "377.1", "t": "That lofty power and might of thine, thy strength and thine intelligence,<br>And thy surpassing thunderbolt, the wish makes keen."}, {"st": "377.2", "t": "O Indra, heaven and earth augment thy manly force and thy renown:<br>The waters and the mountains stir and urge thee on:"}, {"st": "377.3", "t": "Vishnu in the lofty ruling power, Varuna, Mitra sing thy praise:<br>In thee the Maruts’ company have great delight."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Agni"}, {"st": "378.1", "t": "O Agni, God, the people sing reverent praise to thee for strength:<br>With terrors trouble thou the foe"}, {"st": "378.2", "t": "Wilt thou not, Agni, lend us aid to win the cattle, win the wealth?<br>Maker of room, make room for us"}, {"st": "378.3", "t": "In the great fight cast us not off, Agni, as one who bears a load:<br>Snatch up the wealth and win it all!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "379.1", "t": "Before his hot displeasure all the peoples, all the men bow down,<br>As rivers bow them to the sea."}, {"st": "379.2", "t": "Even fiercely-moving Vritra’s head he served with his thunderbolt,<br>His mighty hundred-knotted bolt."}, {"st": "379.3", "t": "That might of his shone brightly forth when Indra brought together, like<br>A skin, the worlds of heaven and earth."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "380.1", "t": "Kind-thoughted is the noble, gladdening, friendly one."}, {"st": "380.2", "t": "Approach, O beauteous hero, this auspicious pair that draws the car!<br>These two are coming near to us."}, {"st": "380.3", "t": "Bend lowly down, as ‘twere, your beads: be stands amid the water-flood,<br>Pointing with his ten horns the way."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Indra"}, {"st": "381.1", "t": "Pressers, blend Soma juice for him, each draught most excellent, for him<br>The brave, the: hero, for his joy!", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "381.2", "t": "The two strong bay steeds, yoked by prayer, hither shall bring to us our friend,<br>Indra, song-lover, through our songs.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [13, 12]]}, {"st": "381.3", "t": "The Vritra-slayer drinks the juice. May he who gives a hundred<br>aids<br>Approach, nor stay afar from us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "382.1", "t": "Let the drops pass within thee as the rivers flow into the sea<br>O Indra, naught excelleth thee."}, {"st": "382.2", "t": "‘Thou’ wakeful hero, by thy might hast taken food of Soma juice,<br>Which, Indra, is within thee now."}, {"st": "382.3", "t": "O Indra, Vritra-slayer, let Soma be ready for thy maw, The drops be ready for thy forms!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Agni"}, {"st": "383.1", "t": "Help, thou who knowest lauds, this work, a lovely hymn in Rudra’s praise,<br>Adorable in every house"}, {"st": "383.2", "t": "May this our God, great, limitless, smoke-bannered, excellently bright,<br>Urge us to holy thought and wealth"}, {"st": "383.3", "t": "Like soma rich lord of men, may he, Agni, the banner of the Gods,<br>Refulgent, hear us through our lauds!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "384.1", "t": "Sing this, beside the flowing juice, to him, your hero, much invoked,<br>To please him as a mighty Bull!"}, {"st": "384.2", "t": "He, excellent, withholdeth not his bounteous gift of wealth in kine.<br>When lie bath listened to our songs."}, {"st": "384.3", "t": "May he with might unclose for us the cow’s stall, whosesoe’er it be,<br>To which the Dasyu-slayer goes!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Vishnu"}, {"st": "385.1", "t": "Through all this world strode Vishnu: thrice his foot he planted, and the whole<br>Was gathered in his footstep’s dust."}, {"st": "385.2", "t": "Vishnu, the guardian, he whom none deceiveth, made three steps, thenceforth<br>Establishing his high decrees."}, {"st": "385.3", "t": "Look ye on Vishnu’s works whereby the friend of Indra, close allied,<br>Hath let his holy ways be seen"}, {"st": "385.4", "t": "The princes evermore behold that loftiest place of Vishnu, like<br>An eye extended through the heavens."}, {"st": "385.5", "t": "This, Vishou’s station most sublime, the sages, ever-vigilant,<br>Lovers of holy song, light up."}, {"st": "385.6", "t": "May the Gods help and favour us out of the place whence Vishnu strode<br>Over the back and ridge of earth."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Indra"}, {"st": "386.1", "t": "Let none, no, not thy worshippers, delay thee far away from us!<br>Even from far away come thou unto our feast, or listen it already here!"}, {"st": "386.2", "t": "For here, like rites on honey, those who pray to thee sit by the juice that they have poured.<br>Wealth-craving singers have on Indra set their hope, as men set foot upon a car."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Indra"}, {"st": "387.1", "t": "Sung is the song of ancient time: to Indra have ye said the prayer.<br>They have sung many a Brihati of sacrifice, poured forth the worshipper’s many thoughts."}, {"st": "387.2", "t": "Indra hath tossed together mighty stores of wealth, and both the worlds, yea, and the sun.<br>Pure, brightly-shining, mingled with the milk, the draughts of Soma have made Indra glad."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "388.1", "t": "For Vritra-slaying Indra, thou, Soma, art poured that he may drink,<br>And for the guerdon-giving man, the hero sitting in his seat."}, {"st": "388.2", "t": "Friends, may the princes, ye and we, obtain this most resplendent one,<br>Gain him who hath the smell of strength, win him whose home is very strength!"}, {"st": "388.3", "t": "Him with the fleece they purify, brown, golden-hued, beloved of all.<br>Who with exhilarating juice flows forth to all the deities."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra"}, {"st": "389.1", "t": "Indra whose wealth is in thyself, what mortal will attack this man?<br>The strong will win the spoil on the decisive day through faith in thee, O Maghavan!"}, {"st": "389.2", "t": "In battles with the foe urge on our mighty ones who give the treasures dear to thee<br>And may we with our princes, Lord of tawny steeds! pass through all peril, led by thee!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Indra"}, {"st": "390.1", "t": "Come, priest, and of the savoury juice pour forth a yet more gladdening draught!<br>So is the hero praised who ever prospers us."}, {"st": "390.3", "t": "Indra, whom tawny coursers bear, praise such as thine, preeminent,<br>None by his power or by his goodness hath attained."}, {"st": "390.3", "t": "We, seeking glory, have invoked this God of yours, the Lord of wealth,<br>Who must be magnified by constant sacrifice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Agni"}, {"st": "391.1", "t": "Sing praise to him, the Lord of light. The Gods have made the God to be their messenger,<br>To bear oblation to the Gods."}, {"st": "391.2", "t": "Agni, the bounteous giver, bright with varied flames, laud thou, O singer Sobhari,<br>Him who controls this sacred food with Soma blent, who hath first claim to sacrifice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "392.1", "t": "Expressed by stones, O Soma, and urged through the long wool of the sheep,<br>Thou, entering the press-boards, even as men a fort, goldbued, hast settled in the vats."}, {"st": "392.2", "t": "He beautifies himself through the sheep’s long fine wool, the bounteous, like the racing steed,<br>Even Soma Pavamana who shall be the joy of sages and of holy bards."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "393.1", "t": "Here, verily, yesterday we let the Thunder-wielder drink his fill.<br>Bring him the juice poured forth in sacrifice to-day! Now range you by the glorious one!"}, {"st": "393.2", "t": "Even the wolf, the savage beast that rends the sheep, follows the path of his decrees.<br>So graciously accepting, Indra, this our praise, with wondrous thought come forth to us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra-Agni"}, {"st": "394.1", "t": "Indra and Agni, in your deeds of might ye deck heaven’s lucid realms:<br>Famed is that hero strength of yours."}, {"st": "394.2", "t": "To Indra and to Agni prayers go forward from the holy task.<br>Along the path of sacred Law."}, {"st": "394.3", "t": "Indra and Agni, powers are yours, yours are oblations and abodes:<br>Good is your zealous energy."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Indra"}, {"st": "395.1", "t": "Who knows what vital power he wins, drinking beside the flowing juice?<br>This is the fair-cheeked God who, joying in the draught, breaks down the castles in his strength."}, {"st": "395.2", "t": "As a wild elephant rushes on, this way and that way mad with<br>heat,<br>None may restrain thee, yet come hither to the draught! Thou, movest mighty in thy power."}, {"st": "395.3", "t": "When he, the terrible, ne’er o’erthrown, stedfast, made ready for the fight — <br>When Indra Maghavan lists to his praiser’s call, he will not stand aloof, but come."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "396.1", "t": "The Pavamanas have been poured, the brilliant drops of Soma juice,<br>For holy lore of every kind."}, {"st": "396.2", "t": "From heaven, from out the firmament hath PavamAna been effused<br>Upon the back and ridge of earth."}, {"st": "396.3", "t": "The Pavamanas have been shed, the beautified swift Somadrops,<br>Driving all enemies afar."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Indra-Agni"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Indra and Agni I invoke, joint-victors, bounteous, unsubdued,<br>Foe-slayers, best to win the spoil.<br>2. Indra and Agni, singers skilled in melody hymn you bringing lauds:<br>I choose you both to bring me food.<br>3. Together, with one mighty deed, Indra and Agni, ye shook down.<br>The ninety forts which Dasas held."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Agni"}, {"st": "398.1", "t": "O Child of Strength, to thee whose look is lovely, with oblations we,<br>O Agni, have poured forth our songs."}, {"st": "398.2", "t": "To thee for shelter are we come, as to the shade from fervent heat,<br>Agni, who glitterest like gold"}, {"st": "398.3", "t": "Mighty as one who slays with shafts, or like a bull with sharpened horn,<br>Agni, thou brakest down the forts."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 19 · Agni"}, {"st": "399.1", "t": "To give eternal glow, we pray Vaisvanara the holy one, Lord of the light of sacrifice."}, {"st": "399.2", "t": "Who, furthering the light of Law, hath spread himself to meet this work:<br>He sends the seasons, mighty one."}, {"st": "399.3", "t": "Love of what is and what shall be, Agni, in his beloved forms,<br>Shines forth alone as sovran Lord."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "", "t": "1.Wise Agni, in the ancient way, making his body beautiful,<br>Hath been exalted by the sage.<br>2. I invocate the Child of Strength, Agni whose glow is bright and pure,<br>In this well-ordered sacrifice.<br>3. So, Agni, rich in many friends, with fiery splendour seat thyself.<br>With Gods upon our sacred grass!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "401.1", "t": "O thou with stones for arms, thy powers, rending the fiends, have raised themselves:<br>Drive off the foes who compass us"}, {"st": "401.2", "t": "Hence conquering with might when car meets car, and when the prize is staked,<br>With fearless heart will I sing praise."}, {"st": "401.3", "t": "None, evil-minded, may assail this Pavamana’s holy laws<br>Crush him who fain would fight with thee!"}, {"st": "401.4", "t": "For Indra to the streams they urge the tawny rapture-dropping steed,<br>Indu, the bringer of delight."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "402.1", "t": "Come hither, Indra, with bay steeds, joyous, with tails like peacocks’ plumes!<br>Let no men check thy course as fowlers stay the bird: pass o’er them as o’er desert lands!"}, {"st": "402.2", "t": "Vritra’s devourer, he who burst the cloud, brake forts, and drave the floods,<br>Indra, who mounts his chariot at his bay steeds’ cry, shatters e’en things that stand most firm."}, {"st": "402.3", "t": "Like pools of water deep and full, like kine thou cherishest thy might;<br>Like the milch-cows that go well-guarded to the mead, like water-brooks that reach the lake."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Indra"}, {"st": "403.1", "t": "Even as the wild bull, when he thirsts, goes to the desert’s watery pool,<br>Come hither quickly both at morning and at eve, and with the Kanvas drink thy fill!"}, {"st": "403.2", "t": "May the drops gladden thee, Lord Indra, and obtain bounty for him who pours the juice!<br>Soma, shed in the press, thou stolest and didst drink, and hence hast won surpassing might."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Indra"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. Thou as a God. O mightiest, verily blessest mortal man.<br>O Maghavan, there is no comforter but thou: Indra, I speak my words to thee.<br>2. Let not thy bounteous gifts, let not thy saving help all fail us good Lord, at any time!<br>And measure out to us, thou lover of man-kind, all riches hitherward from men"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Dawn"}, {"st": "", "t": "I. This Lady, excellent and kind, after her sister shining forth, Daughter of Heaven, hath shown herself.<br>2. Red, like a mare, and beautiful, holy, the mother of the kine, The Dawn became the Asvins’ friend.<br>3. Yea, and thou art the Asvins’, friend the mother of the cows art thou: O Dawn, thou rules over wealth"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Asvins"}, {"st": "406.1", "t": "Now Morning with her earliest light shines forth, dear daughter of the Sky:<br>High, Asvins, I extol your praise"}, {"st": "406.2", "t": "Children of Ocean, mighty ones, discoverers of riches, Gods,<br>Finders of treasure through our prayer!"}, {"st": "406.3", "t": "Your lofty coursers hasten over the everlasting realm, whea your car flies with winged steeds."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Dawn"}, {"st": "407.1", "t": "O Dawn who hast a store of wealth, bring unto us that splendid gift<br>Wherewith we may support children and children’s sons"}, {"st": "407.2", "t": "Thou radiant Lady of sweet strains, with wealth of horses and of kine<br>Shine thou on us this day, O Dawn, auspiciously"}, {"st": "407.3", "t": "O Dawn who hast a store of wealth, yoke red steeds to thy car to-day.<br>Then bring us all delight and all felicities"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Asvins"}, {"st": "408.1", "t": "O Asvins, wonderful in act, do ye unanimous direct<br>Your chariot to our home wealthy in kine and gold!"}, {"st": "408.2", "t": "Hither may they who wake at dawn bring, to drink Soma, both the Gods,<br>Health-givers, wonder-workers, borne on paths of gold!"}, {"st": "408.3", "t": "Ye who brought down the hymn from heaven, a light that giveth light to men,<br>Do ye, O Asvins, bring strength hither unto us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Agni"}, {"st": "409.1", "t": "I think of Agni who is kind, whom, as their home, the milch-kine seek;<br>Whom fleet-foot coursers seek as home, and strong enduring, steeds as home.<br>Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"st": "409.2", "t": "For Agni, God of all mankind, gives the strong courser to theman.<br>Agni gives ready gear for wealth, he gives the best when he ix pleased.<br>Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"st": "409.3", "t": "The Agni who is praised as kind, to whom the milch-kine come. in herds,<br>To whom the racers, swift of foot, to whom our wellborn princes come. Bring food to those who sing thy praise!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Dawn"}, {"st": "410.1", "t": "O heavenly Dawn, awaken us to ample opulence today,<br>Even as thou didst waken us with Satyasravas, Vayya’s, Son, high-born! delightful with thy steeds!"}, {"st": "410.2", "t": "Daughter of heaven, thou dawnedst of Sunitha, Suchadratha’s son;<br>So dawn thou on one mightier still, on Satyasravas, Vayya’s son, high-born! delightful with thy steeds!"}, {"st": "410.3", "t": "So bringing treasure, shine to-day on us, thou daughter, of the Sky,<br>As on one mightier thou hast dawned, on Satyasravas, Vayya’s son, high-born! delightful with thy steeds!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Asvins"}, {"st": "411.1", "t": "To meet your treasure-bringing car, the car that is most dear to us,<br>Asvins the Rishi is prepared, your worshipper with, songs of praise. Lovers of sweetness, hear my call"}, {"st": "411.2", "t": "Pass, Asvins, over all away. May I obtain you for myself,<br>Wonderful, with your golden paths, most gracious, bringers of the flood! Lovers of sweetness, hear my call!"}, {"st": "411.3", "t": "Come to us, O ye Asvins twain, bringing your precious treasures, come<br>Ye Rudras, on your paths of gold, rejoicing, with your store of wealth! Lovers of sweetness, hear my call!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Agni"}, {"st": "412.1", "t": "Agni is wakened by the people’s fuel to meet the Dawn who cometh like a milch-cow.<br>Like young trees shooting up on high their branches, his flames mounting to the vault of heaven."}, {"st": "412.2", "t": "For the Gods’ worship hath the priest been wakened: kind Agni hath arisen erect at morning.<br>Kindled, his radiant might is made apparent, and the great God hath been set free from darkness."}, {"st": "412.3", "t": "When he hath roused the line of his attendants, with the bright milk bright Agni is anointed.<br>Then is prepared the effectual oblation, which spread in front, with tongues, erect, he drinketh,"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Dawn"}, {"st": "413.1", "t": "This light is come, amid all lights the fairest: born is the brilliant, far-extending brightness.<br>Night, sent away for Savitar’s uprising, hath yielded up a birthplace for the morning."}, {"st": "413.2", "t": "The fair, the bright is come with her white offspring to her the Dark one hath resigned her dwelling.<br>Akin, immortal, following each other, changing their colours both the heavens move onward."}, {"st": "413.3", "t": "Common, unending is the sisters’ pathway: taught by the Gods alternately they travel,<br>Fair-formed, of different hues and yet one-minded, Night and Dawn clash not, neither do they tarry."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Asvins"}, {"st": "414.1", "t": "Agni, the bright face of the Dawns, is shining: the singers’ pious voices have ascended.<br>Borne on your chariot, Asvins, turn you hither, and come unto our brimming warm libation!"}, {"st": "414.2", "t": "Most frequent guests, they scorn not what is ready: even now the lauded Asvins are beside us.<br>With promptest aid they come at morn and evening, the worshipper’s most healthful guards from trouble."}, {"st": "414.3", "t": "Yea, come at milking-time, at early morning, at noon of day, and when the Sun is setting,<br>By day, at night, with most auspicious favour! Not only now the draught hath drawn the Asvins."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Dawn"}, {"st": "415.1", "t": "These Dawns have raised their banner: in the eastern half of middle air they spread abroad their shining light.<br>Like heroes who prepare their weapons for the fray, the cows are coming on, the mothers, red of hue."}, {"st": "415.2", "t": "Rapidly have the ruddy beams of light shot up: the red cows have they harnessed, easy to be yoked.<br>The Dawns have made their pathways as in former times: redhued, they have attained refulgent brilliancy."}, {"st": "415.3", "t": "They sing their song like women active in their tasks, along their common path hither from far away,<br>Bringing refreshment to the liberal devotee, yea, all things to the worshipper who pours the juice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Asvins"}, {"st": "416.1", "t": "Agni is wakened: Surya riseth from the earth. Bright Dawn hath opened out the mighty twain with light.<br>The Asvins have equipped their chariot for the course. God Savitar hath roused the world in sundry ways."}, {"st": "416.2", "t": "When, O ye Asvins, ye equip your mighty car, with fatness and with honey balm, ye twain, our power!<br>To our devotion give victorious strength in war: may we win riches in the heroes’ strife for spoil!"}, {"st": "416.3", "t": "Nigh to us come the Asvins’ lauded three wheeled car, the car laden with meath and drawn by fleet-foot steeds,<br>Three-seated, opulent, bestowing all delight: may it bring weal to us, to cattle and to men!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "417.1", "t": "Thy streams that never fail or waste flow forth like showers of rain from heaven,<br>To bring a thousand stores of wealth."}, {"st": "417.2", "t": "He, flows beholding on his way all well-beloved sacred lore,<br>Green-tinted, brandishing his arms."}, {"st": "417.3", "t": "He, when the people deck him like a docile king of elephants,<br>Sits as a falcon in the wood."}, {"st": "417.4", "t": "So bring thou hitherward to us, Indu, while thou art purified.<br>All treasures both of heaven and earth!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "418.1", "t": "Forward have flowed the streams of power, of this the mighty one effused,<br>Of him who waits upon the Gods."}, {"st": "418.2", "t": "The singers praise him with their song, and learned priests adorn the steed<br>Born as thelight that merits laud."}, {"st": "418.3", "t": "These things thou winnest quickly, while men cleanse thee, Soma, nobly rich!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Indra"}, {"st": "419.1", "t": "This Brahman, comer at the due time, named Indra, is renowned and praised."}, {"st": "419.2", "t": "To thee alone, O Lord of Strength, go, as it were, all songs of praise."}, {"st": "419.3", "t": "Like streams of water on their way, let bounties, Indra, flow from thee!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Indra"}, {"st": "420.1", "t": "Even as a car to give us aid, we draw thee nigh to favour us,<br>Strong in thy deeds, quelling attack, Indra, Lord, mightiest! of the brave."}, {"st": "420.2", "t": "Great in thou power and wisdom, strong, with thought that comprehendeth all!<br>Wide hast thou spread in majesty."}, {"st": "420.3", "t": "Thou very mighty one, whose hands by virtue of thy greatness wield<br>The golden bolt that beaks its way!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Agni"}, {"st": "421.1", "t": "He who hath lighted up the joyous castle, wise courser like the steed of cloudy heaven,<br>Bright like the Sun with hundredfold existence"}, {"st": "421.2", "t": "He, doubly born, hath spread in his effulgence through the three luminous realms, through all the regions,<br>Best sacrificing Priest where waters gather."}, {"st": "421.3", "t": "Priest doubly born, he through his love of glory hath in his keeping all things worth the choosing.<br>The man who brings him gifts hath noble offspring."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Agni"}, {"st": "422.1", "t": "Agni, with hymns may we now accomplish that which thou lovest,<br>Strength, like a horse auspicious, with service!"}, {"st": "422.2", "t": "For, Agni, thou art now the promoter of strength auspicious,<br>Lofty sacrifice, power effective."}, {"st": "422.3", "t": "Through these our praises, come thou to meet us, bright as the sunlight,<br>Agni, kindly with all thy faces!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Agni"}, {"st": "423.1", "t": "Immortal Jatavedas, thou bright-hued refulgent gift of Dawn.<br>Agni, this day to him who pays oblations bring the Gods who waken with the morn!"}, {"st": "423.2", "t": "For thou art offering-bearer, well-loved messenger, and charioteer of holy rites.<br>Accordant with the Asvins and with Dawn grant us heroic strength and lofty fame!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Indra"}, {"st": "424.1", "t": "The old hath waked the young Moon from his slumber who runs his circling course with many round him<br>Behold the God’s high wisdom in its greatness: he who died yesterday to-day is living."}, {"st": "424.2", "t": "Strong is the red Bird in his strength, great hero, who from of old bath had no nest to dwell in.<br>That which he knows is truth and never idle: he wins and gives the wealth desired of many."}, {"st": "424.3", "t": "Through these Thunderer gained strong manly vigour, through whom he waxed in strength to slaughter Vritra;<br>These who through might of actual operation sprang forth as Gods in course of Law and Order.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [83, 82]]}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Maruts"}, {"st": "425.1", "t": "Here is the Soma ready pressed: of this the Maruts, yea, of this<br>Self-luminous, the Asvins, drink."}, {"st": "425.2", "t": "Of this, moreover, purified, set in three places, procreant,<br>Drink Varuna, Mitra, Aryaman."}, {"st": "425.3", "t": "Yea, Indra, like the Hotar-priest, will in the early morning<br>drink,<br>At pleasure, of the milky juice:"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Surya"}, {"st": "426.1", "t": "Verily, Surya, thou art great; truly, Aditya, thou art great.<br>O most admired for greatness of thy majesty, God, by thy greatness thou art great.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [125, 124]]}, {"st": "426.2", "t": "Yea, Surya, thou art great in fame: thou evermore, O God, art great.<br>Thou by thy greatness art the Gods’ High-Priest, divine, farspread unconquerable light."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · Indra"}, {"st": "427.1", "t": "Come, Lord of rapturous joys, to our libations with thy bay steeds, come<br>With bay steeds to our flowing juice!"}, {"st": "427.2", "t": "Known as best Vritra-slayer erst, as Indra $atakratu, come<br>With bay steeds to our flowing juice!"}, {"st": "427.3", "t": "For, Vritra-slayer, thou art he who drinks these drops of Soma come<br>With bay steeds to our flowing juice!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Indra"}, {"st": "428.1", "t": "Bring to the wise, the great, who waxeth mighty your offerings and make ready your devotion.<br>Go forth to many tribes as man’s controller!"}, {"st": "428.2", "t": "For Indra the sublime, the far-pervading, have singers generated prayer and praises;<br>The sages never violate his statutes.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "428.3", "t": "The choirs have established Indra King for ever for victory him, whose anger is resistless:<br>And for the bays’ Lord strengthened those he loveth."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Indra"}, {"st": "429.1", "t": "If I, O Indra, were the lord of riches ample as thine own,<br>I would support the singer, God who scatterest wealth! and, not abandon him to woe."}, {"st": "429.2", "t": "Each day would I enrich the man who sang my praise, in whatsoever place he were.<br>No kinship is there better, Maghavan, than thine: a father even, is no more."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Indra"}, {"st": "430.1", "t": "Here thou the call of the juice-drinking press-stone: mark thou the sage’s hymn who sings and lauds thee!<br>Take to thine inmost self these adorations!"}, {"st": "430.2", "t": "I know and ne’er forget the hymns and praises of thee, theconqueror, of thy power immortal.<br>Thy name I ever utter, self-refulgent!"}, {"st": "430.3", "t": "Among mankind many are thy libations, and many a time the pious sage invokes thee.<br>O Maghavan, be not long distant from us!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 14 · Indra"}, {"st": "431.1", "t": "Sing strength to Indra that shall. set his chariot in the foremost<br>place!<br>Giver of room in closest fight, slayer of foes in shock of war, be thou our great encorager! Let the weak bowstrings break upon the bows of our weak mies!"}, {"st": "431.2", "t": "Thou didst destroy the Dragon: thou sentest the rivers down to Earth.<br>Foeless, O Indra, wast thou born. Thou tendest well each choicest thing. Therefore we draw us close to thee. Let the weak bowstrings break upon the bows of our weak enemies!<br>Destroyed be all malignitics and all our enemy’s designs!"}, {"st": "431.3", "t": "Thy bolt thou castest at the foe, O Indra, who would smite us dead: thy liberal bounty gives us wealth. Let the weak bowstrings break upon the bows of our weak enemies!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 15 · Indra"}, {"st": "432.1", "t": "Rich be the praiser of one rich and liberal, Lord of days! like thee:<br>High rank be his who lauds the juice!"}, {"st": "432.2", "t": "His wealth who hath no store of kine hath ne’er found out recited laud,<br>Nor song of praises that is sung."}, {"st": "432.3", "t": "Give us not, Indra, as a prey unto the scornful or the proud:<br>Help, mighty one, with power and might!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 16 · Indra"}, {"st": "433.1", "t": "Come hither, Indra, with thy bays, come thou to Kanva’s eulogy!<br>Ye by command of yonder Dyaus, God bright by day! have gone to heaven."}, {"st": "433.2", "t": "The stones’ rim shakes the Soma here like a wolf worrying a sheep.<br>Ye by command of yonder Dyaus, God bright by day I have gone to heaven."}, {"st": "433.3", "t": "May the stone bring thee as it speaks, the Soma-stone with ringing voice!<br>Ye by command of yonder Dyaus, God bright by day! have gone to heaven."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 17 · Soma Pavamana"}, {"st": "434.1", "t": "For Indra flow most rich in sweets, O Soma, bringing him delight!"}, {"st": "434.2", "t": "Bright, meditating sacred song, these juices have sent Vayu forth."}, {"st": "434.3", "t": "They were sent forth to feast the Gods, like chariots speeding in the race."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 18 · Agni"}, {"st": "435.1", "t": "Agni I deem our Hotar priest, munificent wealth-giver, Son of Strength, who knoweth all that is even as the Sage who knoweth all.<br>Lord of fair rites, a God with form erected turning to the Gods, he when the flame hath sprung forth from the holy oil, the offered fatness, longs for it as it grows bright."}, {"st": "435.2", "t": "We, sacrificing, call on the best worshipper thee eldest of Angirasas, singer! with hymns, thee, brilliant one! with singers’ hymn;<br>Thee, wandering round, as ‘twere the sky, thee who art Hotar-priest of men, whom, Bull with hair of flame, the people must observe, tile people that he speed them on.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0], [88, 87]]}, {"st": "435.3", "t": "He with his blazing Power refulgent far and wide, he verily it iswho conquers demon foes, conquers the demons like an axe:<br>At whose close touch things solid part, and what is stable yields he keeps his ground and flinches not, like trees. Subduing all from the skilled archer flinches not.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Agni"}, {"st": "436.1", "t": "O Agni, strength and fame are thine: thy fires blaze forth on high, O thou refulgent God!<br>Sage, passing bright, thou givest to the worshipper with power, the wealth that merits laud."}, {"st": "436.2", "t": "With brilliant, purifying sheen, with perfect sheen thou liftest up thyself in light.<br>Thou, visiting both thy mothers, aidest them as son; thou joinest close the earth and heaven.", "hvShift6": [[0, 0]]}, {"st": "436.3", "t": "O Jatavedas, Son of Strength, rejoice thyself, gracious, in our fair hymns and songs!<br>In thee have they heaped viands various, many formed; wealthborn, of wondrous help are they."}, {"st": "436.4", "t": "Agni, spread forth, as ruler, over living things: give wealth, to<br>us, immortal God!<br>Thou shinest out from beauty fair to look upon: thou leadest<br>us to beauteous Power."}, {"st": "436.5", "t": "I laud the Sage, who orders sacrifice, who hath great riches under his control.<br>Thou givest blest award of good, and plenteous food, thou givest wealth that wins success."}, {"st": "436.6", "t": "The men have set before them, for his favour, Agni, strong, visible to all, the holy.<br>Thee, Lord divine, with ears to hear, most famous, mens’ generations magnify with praise-songs."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Agni"}, {"st": "437.1", "t": "Agni, he conquers by thine aid that brings him store of valiant sons and does great deeds,<br>Whose bond of friendship is thy choice."}, {"st": "437.2", "t": "Thy spark is black and crackling; kindled in due time, O bounteous, it is taken up.<br>Thou art the dear friend of the mighty Mornings: thou shinest in glimmerings of the night."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Agni"}, {"st": "438.1", "t": "Him, duly coming, as their germ have plants received: this Agni have maternal Waters brought to life.<br>So, in like manner, do the forest trees and plants bear him within them and produce him evermore."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Agni"}, {"st": "439.1", "t": "Agni grows bright for Indra: he shines far resplendent in the sky:<br>He sends forth offspring like a queen."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Agni"}, {"st": "440.1", "t": "The sacred hymns love him who wakes and watches: to him who watches the holy verses.<br>This Soma saith to him Who wake my dwelling in thy friendship."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Agni"}, {"st": "441.1", "t": "Agni is watchful, and the Richas love him: Agni is watchful, Sama hymns approach him.<br>Agni is watchful, to him saith this Soma, I rest and have my dwelling in thy friendship."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Gods"}, {"st": "442.1", "t": "Praise to the friends who sit in front! to those seated together, praise<br>I use the hundred-footed speech speech."}, {"st": "442.2", "t": "I use the hundred-footed speech, I sing what hath a thousand paths,<br>Gayatra, Trishtup, Jagat hymn."}, {"st": "442.3", "t": "Gayatra, Trishtup, Jagat hymn, the forms united and complete,<br>Have the Gods made familiar friends."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Agni"}, {"st": "443.1", "t": "Agni, is light, light is Agni, Indra is light, light is Indra<br>Surya is light, light is Surya."}, {"st": "443.2", "t": "O Agni, turn again with strength, turn thou again with food and life:<br>Save us again from grief and woe!"}, {"st": "443.3", "t": "O Agni, turn again with wealth sprinkle thou us from everyside.<br>With thine own all-supporting stream!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra"}, {"st": "444.1", "t": "If I, O Indra, were like thee, the single ruler over wealth.<br>My worshipper should be rich in kine."}, {"st": "444.2", "t": "I should be fain, O Lord of power, to strengthen and enrich thesage,<br>Where I the ford of herds of kine."}, {"st": "444.3", "t": "Thy goodness, Indra, is a cow yielding in plenty kine and steeds.<br>To worshippers who press the juice."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 10 · The Waters"}, {"st": "445.1", "t": "Yea, Waters, ye bring health and bliss: so help ye us to energy.<br>That we may look on great delight!"}, {"st": "445.2", "t": "Give us a portion of the dew, the most auspicious that ye have,<br>Like mothers in their longing love!"}, {"st": "445.3", "t": "For you we gladly go to hirn to whose abode ye speed us on,<br>And, Waters, give us procreant strength!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 11 · Vata"}, {"st": "446.1", "t": "May Vata breathe his balm on us, healthful, delightful to our heart:<br>May he prolong our days of life!"}, {"st": "446.2", "t": "Thou art our father, Vata, yea, thou art our brother and our friend:<br>So give us strength that we may live!"}, {"st": "446.3", "t": "The store of Amrit that laid away yonder, O Vata, in thine home — <br>Give us strength that we may live!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 12 · Agni"}, {"st": "447.1", "t": "The fleet steed wearing divers forms, the eagle bearing his golden raiment to his birthplace,<br>Clothed in due season with the light of Surya, red, hath begot the sacrifice in person."}, {"st": "447.2", "t": "Multiform seed he laid in waters, lustre which gathered on the earth and there developed.<br>In the mid-air establishing his greatness, he cries aloud, seed of the vigorous courser."}, {"st": "447.3", "t": "He hath, enduing thousand robes that suit him, as sacrifice upheld the light of Surya,<br>Giver of ample gifts in hundreds, thousands, supporter of the heavens, earth’s Lord and ruler."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 13 · Vena"}, {"st": "448.1", "t": "They gaze on thee with longing in their spirit, as on a strong-winged bird that mounteth sky-ward;<br>On thee with wings of gold, Varuna’s envoy, the Bird that hasteneth to the home of Yama."}, {"st": "448.2", "t": "Erect, to heaven hath the Gandharva mounted, pointing at us his many-coloured weapons:<br>Clad in sweet raiment beautiful to look on, for he, as light, produceth forms that please us.."}, {"st": "448.3", "t": "When as a spark he cometh ilear the ocean, looking with vulture’s eye as Law commandeth,<br>His lustre, joying in its own bright splendour, maketh dear glories in the loftiest region."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 1 · Indra"}, {"st": "449.1", "t": "Swift, rapidly striking, like a bull who sharpens his horns, terrific, stirring up the people.<br>With eyes that close not, bellowing, sole hero, Indra subdued at once a hundred armies."}, {"st": "449.2", "t": "With him loud-roaring, ever watchful victcr, bold, hard to overthrow, rouser of battle,<br>Indra. the strong, whose hand bears arrows, conquer, ye heroes, now, now vanquish in the combat!"}, {"st": "449.3", "t": "He rules with those who carry shafts and quivers, Indra who with his band brings hosts together,<br>Foe-conquering strong of arm the Soma-drinker, with mighty bow, shooting with well-laid arrows."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 2 · Brihaspati. Indra"}, {"st": "450.1", "t": "Brihaspati, fly with thy chariot hither, slayer of demons, driving off our foemen!<br>Be thou protector of our cars, destroyer, victor in battle, breaker-up of armies!<br>2, Conspicuous. by thy strength, firm, foremost fighter, mighty and<br>fierce, victorious, all-subduing,<br>The Son of Conquest, passing men and heroes, kinewinner, mount thy conquering car, O Indra!"}, {"st": "450.3", "t": "Cleaver of stalls, kine-winner, armed with thunder, who quells an army and with might destroys it — <br>Follow him, brothers! quit yourselves like heroes, and like this Indra show your zeal and courage!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 3 · Indra. Brihaspati"}, {"st": "451.1", "t": "Piercing with conquering strength the cow-stalls, Indra, pitiless hero with unbounded anger,<br>Victor in fight, unshaken and resistless — may he protect our armies in our battles!"}, {"st": "451.2", "t": "Indra guide these! Brihaspati, and Soma, the guerdon and the sacrifice precede them;<br>And let the banded Maruts march in forefront of heavenly hosts that conquer and demolish!"}, {"st": "451.3", "t": "Ours be the potent host of mighty Indra, King Varuna the Maruts, and Adityas!<br>Uplifted is the shout of Gods who conquer, hightninded Gods who cause the worlds to tremble."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 4 · Indra.Maruts"}, {"st": "452.1", "t": "Bristle thou up, O Maghavan, our weapons: excite the spirits, of my warring heroes!<br>Urge on the strong steed’s might, O Vyitra-slayer, and let the din of conquering cars go upward"}, {"st": "452.2", "t": "May Indra aid us when our flags are gathered: victorious be ther arrows of our army!<br>May our brave men of war prevail in battle. Ye Gods, protect us in the shout of onset!"}, {"st": "452.3", "t": "That army of the foemen, O ye Maruts, which, striving in its. mighty strength, approaches,<br>Hide ye and bury it in pathless darkness that not a man oF them may know the other!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 5 · Agha"}, {"st": "453.1", "t": "Bewildering the senses of our foemen, seize thou their bodies, and depart, O Agha!<br>Attack them, set their hearts on fare with sorrows; so let our foes abide in utter darkness!"}, {"st": "453.2", "t": "Advance, O heroes, win the day, May Indra be your sure defence!<br>Mighty and awful be your arms, that none may wound or injure you!"}, {"st": "453.3", "t": "Loosed from the bowstring fly away, thou arrows sharpened by<br>our prayer!<br>Go to the foemen, strike them home, and let not one be left alive!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 6 · Indra and others"}, {"st": "454.1", "t": "Let ravens and strong-pinioned birds pursue them: yea, let that army be the food of vultures!<br>Indra, let none escape, no sin-remover: behind them all let following birds be gathered!"}, {"st": "454.2", "t": "This host of foemen Maghavan! that cometh on in warlike show — <br>Meet it, O Vritra-slayer, thou, Indra, and Agni, with your flames!"}, {"st": "454.3", "t": "There where the flights of arrows fall like boys whose locks are yet unshorn.<br>Even there may Brahmanaspati, may Aditi protect us well, protect us well through all our days!"}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 7 · Indra"}, {"st": "455.1", "t": "Drive Rakshasas and foes away, break thou in pieces Vritra’s jaws:<br>O Vritra-slaying Indra, quell the foeman’s wrath who threatens us!"}, {"st": "455.2", "t": "O Indra, beat our foes away, humble the men who challenge us:<br>Send down to nether darkness him who seeks to do us injury!"}, {"st": "455.3", "t": "Strong, ever-youthful are the arms of Indra, fair unassailable, never to be vanquished:<br>These first let him employ when need hath come on us, wherewith the Asuras’ great might was overthrown."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 8 · Soma, Varuna"}, {"st": "456.1", "t": "Thy vital parts I cover with thine armour: with immortality King Soma clothe thee!<br>Varuna give thee what is more than ample, and in thy victory may Gods be joyful!"}, {"st": "456.2", "t": "Blind, O my foemen, shall ye be, even as headless serpents are<br>May Indra slay each best of you when Agni’s flame hath struck you down!"}, {"st": "456.3", "t": "Whoso would kill us, whether he be a stranger foe or one of us,<br>May all the Gods discomfit him! My nearest, closest mail is prayer, my closest armour and defence."}, {"sp": "SEC", "t": "Hymn 9 · Indra. All-Gods"}, {"st": "457.1", "t": "Like a dread wild beast roaming on the mountain thou hast approached us from the farthest distance.<br>Whetting thy bolt and thy sharp blade, O Indra, crush thou the foe and scatter those who hate us!"}, {"st": "457.2", "t": "Gods, may our ears hear that which is auspicious, may our eyes see that which is good, ye holy!<br>Extolling you with still strong limbs and bodies, may we attain the age by Gods appointed!"}, {"st": "457.3", "t": "Illustrious far and wide, may Indra bless us, may Pushan bless us, master of all riches!<br>May Tarkshya with uninjured fellies bless us! Brihaspati bestow on us his favour! Brihaspati bestow on us his favour!"}],[])})();
